OXFAM Praises Government for Prioritizing Vaccination of Informal Economy Workers
According to a letter issued on the afternoon of March 26, the international organization said that this priority would not only demonstrate the Cambodian government's commitment to equitable distribution of vaccines, but also help maintain Cambodia's economy to move forward in these difficult circumstances.
The letter said that these informal economic workers have been fighting to save their lives since the first epidemic of COVID-19. A large number of them lost their jobs and had to struggle every day to support themselves and their families. The disease has spread across the country and around the world, teaching us that these informal economic workers play an important role.
They risked their lives and continued to care for our children, dress us up, cook us, transport us to the hospital, clean the streets, clean the sewers, collect garbage and other work. In addition, they help keep us safe and healthy.
According to OXFAM, informal economic workers include: street vendors, taxi and tricycle drivers, sanitation workers, service workers, factory workers and those who can not work from home. However, OXFAM hopes that the vaccine, which arrived in Cambodia on March 26, will give priority to informal economic workers, the most vulnerable group.
It should be noted that on the morning of March 26, 2021, Cambodia received the SINOVAX vaccine, which was ordered from China in the amount of 1.5 million doses to be injected to the people. This is the third time that Cambodia has received vaccines for its people after the Chinese government-assisted vaccine and the World Health Organization (WHO) vaccine through the KOAC mechanism.
