Ministry of Commerce Establishes Subcommittee on Kovid 19 Vaccination
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, has decided to establish a subcommittee on vaccination for Kovid 19 to control and coordinate the vaccination of civil servants of the Ministry.
In the decision received by Fresh News on March 26, 2021, it was stated that the subcommittee was chaired by Mr. Khim Serey Vong, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce and Mr. Buon Sarak Mony, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce.
The sub-committee has 41 members, including the directors of the 25 capital-provincial trade departments.
The decision states that the subcommittee has the following roles:
Coordinate, manage and administer Kovid-19 vaccination with the Ministry of Health to ensure that the leaders, civil servants and contract officials of the Ministry of Commerce are vaccinated against Kovid-19.
* Compile statistics on the list of leaders, civil servants and contracted volunteers to vaccinate Kovid-19
* Prepare a calendar with the Commission for Kov-19 vaccination in the nationwide framework for Kovid-19 vaccination for leaders, civil servants and contracted officials.
* Monitor and report on the progress of Kovi-19 vaccination on a daily basis to the Commission for Kovid-19 vaccination on a regular basis.
Coordinate vaccination and related work
Prepare reports and report to the Minister of Commerce - Perform other duties as directed by the Ministry leadership.
