(Banteay Meanchey): Starting from a thief stealing a motorcycle of an Indonesian national, the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie searched a pawn shop and suddenly found 41 motorcycles, all of which were undocumented motorcycles, and arrested them. One shop owner and two thieves.
The search of the motorcycle shop was ordered by Brigadier General Born Bin, Provincial Gendarmerie Commander, and according to the complaint of the victim, Willie, a 34-year-old Indonesian national, temporarily staying in Kbal Spean 1 Village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
The case of missing his motorcycle, a black and white Honda Click, made in 2006, without a license plate, which he parked in front of his shop at 1 am on March 25, 2021.
Colonel Nuon Ninaro led a professional force to search and check the security cameras in the shop and arrested two suspects: First: Keo Kosal, alias Mao, male, 18 years old, living in Kbal Spean 1 Village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province; and 2: Penh Veasna, male, 25 years old, living in Palilei 2 Village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province, and sent to the Municipal Armed Forces for questioning.
The suspect, Lay San, who was interrogated by professional forces, confessed that he had been buying and pawning new and old motorcycles from hippies every day for more than three months. On the 25th, he actually received a pawn on a Honda Click motorcycle with the same parts as in the above complaint from two boys who were actually detained by the police.
Based on the victim's complaint, the suspect's confession and the confiscated exhibits, the three suspects, Keo Kosal, Penh Veasna and Lay San, were sent by the Municipal Gendarmerie to the Provincial Gendarmerie to continue the proceedings.
Colonel Em Men Phirum, Deputy Chief of Provincial Gendarmerie for Justice, would like to inform all residents in Poipet City who have lost their motorcycles in the past, please contact us at: 012 99 99 94 and 017 55 55 99 every working hour.
