Earth Hour will be celebrated on March 27 tomorrow
(Phnom Penh): In accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Health, the Ministry of Environment and WWF will organize an hour for the planet on March 27, 2021, tomorrow at 8:30 pm digitally (online social network) In the spirit of solidarity with all people throughout Cambodia and the world.
This is the 14th time that the One Hour Day for the Planet is celebrated in order for people to love the environment and participate in protecting the planet. While One Hour for Earth Day 2021 focuses on the need for joint action to protect nature, which is our common home.
"Now is the time to reflect more clearly on the importance and connection between nature and biodiversity to our survival and well-being," said Neth Pheaktra.
The spokesman for the Ministry of Environment also encouraged young people to create short videos in the sense of loving the environment to share with the public. The "One Hour for the Earth Day" since 2007 always encourages millions of people around the world to take part in protecting nature and the planet for everyone.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, on March 26, 2021, stated that Cambodia has sufficient financial resources to cope with the Kovid-19 crisis. In the next two years.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, receiving about 1.5 million doses of Chinese vaccine (Sinovac) at Phnom Penh International Airport on the morning of March 26, 2021. This.
Speaking to reporters after the reception and handover of the vaccine, Mr. Vongsey Visoth confirmed, "I say that if Kovid-19 continues until this year and next year, we will have enough resources to resist."
However, Mr. Vongsy Visoth also said that if the Kovid disease continues to spread beyond this year and next, he does not dare to guarantee resources, but this is not the only problem. Cambodia's is a global problem.
As for the assessment of the economic situation in 2021, Mr. Vongsey Visoth said that he could not assess it yet, but will have to wait and see how serious the outbreak of Kovid-19 community event on February 20 continues.
Please be informed that the $ 1.164 million budget that the Royal Government of Cambodia has allocated to solve the problem of Kovid-19 and restore the national economy in 2020 has been used up in large quantities, while the remaining budget will continue to be spent for 2021.
For the year 2021, the Royal Government has prepared a budget of more than 800 million dollars to help solve the crisis of Kovid 19 and restore the Cambodian economy after Kovid-19.
The second vaccination campaign in Kampong Cham province plans to set up 28 sites and vaccinate more than 20,000 government officials and residents
(Kampong Cham): In the second Kovid-19 vaccination campaign, the Kampong Cham Provincial Administration is ready to launch 19 Kovid vaccination operations to more than 20,000 civil servants and citizens and prepare locations for vaccination. 28 vaccines in referral hospitals and health centers in cities and districts in Kampong Cham province.
Mr. Kim Sour Phirun, Director of Kampong Cham Provincial Health Department, said this in the morning of March 26, 2021 at Kampong Cham Provincial Hall in the subcommittee meeting on Kovid-19 vaccine, chaired by Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham and Chairman. Kovid-19 Provincial Fighting Committee is attended by departments, institutions, units around the province and district governors in Kampong Cham province.
The director of the Kampong Cham Provincial Health Department, Mr. Kim Sour Phirun, said that the first vaccination campaign, the provincial health department received 10,800 doses of vaccine, which can vaccinate 5,400 people. Therefore, as of March 26, 2021, 3,331 doctors have been vaccinated with the second dose, setting up 9 locations in the referral hospitals in Kampong Cham province and 11 teams of doctors. There are 10 people in each group.
Separately, in the plan of the second vaccination campaign, the director of the Department of Health said that according to unofficial information, the Kampong Cham Provincial Health Department can receive 50,000 doses of vaccine, which can vaccinate 25,000 people.
At the same time, the Department of Health has also set up additional locations, a total of 28 locations in referral hospitals and health centers in cities and districts in Kampong Cham province. There are a total of 41 doctors in each group of 10 doctors.
Mr. Kim Sour Phirun confirmed that the second campaign in the near future, the Ministry of Health has recommended only 14 days to complete the vaccination.
At the same time, Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province and Chairman of Kovid-19 Provincial Commission for Combating Diseases, instructed the relevant departments to prepare the planning documents as soon as possible to send to the Ministry of Health for review and decision.
