Love in the Kovid 19 barrier! Mrs. Pich Chanmony can talk to her child outside the glass curtain
(Phnom Penh): A picture of a conversation between Ms. Pich Chanmony and her 4-year-old son under a glass screen attracted and moved the hearts of the people who play social media. This picture shows the deep feelings between mother and child that are separated because of Kovid 19.
Ms. Pich Chanmony is a female commander on the battlefield against Kovid 19, leading the volunteer forces of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to fight Kovid 19, which is rampant in Cambodia, especially at the February 20 community event. . Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Volunteer Army has been instrumental in collecting patient samples, caring for patients and arranging facilities for treating patients.
Due to the mission on the battlefield of Kovid 19 and to keep the children safe, both Mrs. Pich Chanmony and Mr. Hun Manet decided to live separately from their children. The mother and father, who are key players in the fight against Kovid 19, can not live or talk to their children in person, only on the phone.
For those of you who have not yet had a child, it may be hard to imagine the deep emotions and love between parents and children. But for those who have children, it is important to understand the depth of the relationship between parents and children, especially young children who need to be nurtured and released daily with their children. Some even consider their children to be medicine, vital energy when they are tired from work or have problems.
For Mrs. Pich Chanmony and Mr. Hun Manet did not do these things while leading the fighting force on the Battle of Kovid 19. The feeling of a parent who is not close to their child is one thing, but the feeling of the child is small and needs the affection of the mother, the father does not know how sad he is when separated from his parents like this?
These gestures are considered by social media users as a sacrifice for the personal well-being of the two Cambodian people in joining the Royal Government to fight Kovid 19 in exchange for the well-being of the Cambodian people who are disturbed and harassed. Kovid's disease 19.
On a picture of Ms. Pich Chanmony meeting her son Khang Khan with a mirror, which received almost 3,000 "share" clicks, the public on social media expressed sympathy for the mother and child. They also appreciated and thanked her for her dedication and heroism to Cambodian society and people.
