(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia on March 25, 2021, decided to introduce additional measures to continue to manage the impact on key sectors to restore and promote Cambodia's economic growth from the Kovid 19 crisis (Round 8).
In this additional measure, the Royal Government continues to advise ministries and state institutions and calls on private individuals who own buildings, business locations and factories to facilitate the tenants by avoiding contract termination or eviction in the absence of the tenants. Ability to pay rent on time.
The Royal Government also encourages the owners of buildings, business locations and factories to negotiate with the tenants on the delay in payment of rental fees and eventual changes in rental fees.
