Doctors call the rescue of Kovid 19 patients a life-saving mission with the monarchy and ask them to implement "3 protect 3 do not"
(Phnom Penh): Respiratory and pulmonologist Dr. Va Meng, who is working to rescue 19 Kovid patients at the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital, considers the treatment and rescue of 19 Kovid patients to be a difficult mission. He considered the effort to bargain and seize life from the monarch.
Va Meng posted on Facebook on the night of March 25, 2021, with a picture of 19 Kovid patients recovering from several days of rescue efforts. The patient shown here is Dr. M. Sophy Kovid 19 patient from Prey Veng province.
"I and my team at the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital tried to bargain with the Royal Government to save the life of Dr. M. Sophy in Prey Veng and many other patients," he said. "She is in critical condition, using an oxygen machine to help her breathe and take her life, and the medical team here is doing her best."
According to Mr. Va Meng, under this rescue effort, the health condition of Mr. M. Sophy, who was severely affected by Kovid 19 virus, is now much better.
Dr. Va Meng also mentioned in his mission statement that all the doctors had done and hoped that the angels would take care of the patients who had passed through this tragedy.
Mr. Va Meng expressed his commitment to help 19 patients, "The patients continue to die, and the doctors continue to do their best to negotiate with Yom Reach to bring their lives to their families. "Patients."
In this article, the doctor also described the tragedy of the death of Kovid 19 as an unwanted thing. "The breakup and loss of a family member who could not even see each other for the last time and was close enough to touch the corpse before the corpse was very difficult to accept and the corpse could not be sent," he said. Hometown.
"I hope you do not really want to know this feeling, so please respect the principles of the three-pronged and three-pronged leadership," he said.
So far, seven deaths have been reported in Cambodia from 19 Kovid, while two others have died of drug overdose and high blood pressure.
While continuing the mission to rescue patients at the hospital, Mr. Va Meng, as well as the doctors of the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital, prayed to the angels to take care of the Cambodian people and humanity through this tragedy and hope for disaster. This one will soon disappear.
