Singapore supports Cambodia to host 13th Asia-Europe Summit in 2021
(Phnom Penh): The Government of Singapore has expressed its support for the Royal Government of Cambodia in hosting the 13th Asia-Europe Summit in 2021. This is according to a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, obtained by Fresh News.
This statement was made by the newly appointed Ambassador of the Republic of Singapore to Cambodia, Ms. Teo Lay Cheng, during a courtesy call and discussion with Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation. On the morning of March 25, 2021 at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
A statement from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated: "Singapore has supported Cambodia in hosting the 13th Asia-Europe Meeting (The ASEM13) in 2021, and Cambodia is confident that Singapore will continue to do so. "Full support when Cambodia takes over the ASEAN chairmanship in 2022."
The 13th Asia-Europe Summit, which Cambodia is hosting and scheduled for June, has been postponed for a second time, with a rescheduled date for the end of 2021. Originally, as the host country, Cambodia was scheduled to host the 13th Asia-Europe Summit on 16-17 November 2020, but due to the 199 Kovid epidemic, the Royal Government has already proposed to postpone it once. Organize this big meeting in the middle of 2021.
He stressed that the good relations between the two countries' top leaders and close cooperation in all fields, including education, trade, investment and people-to-people exchanges, have helped. Bilateral relations are constantly improving.
For international cooperation, the two sides agreed to continue to work closely and support each other in the international arena for mutual benefit. The two sides also exchanged views on regional and international issues of common concern.
