(Phnom Penh): China's vaccine Kovid 19 Sinovac (Sinovac) about 1.5 million doses will arrive in Cambodia on Friday morning, March 26, 2021 tomorrow. The vaccine is an order of the Royal Government of Cambodia to increase the number of vaccines given to the people in the mission to fight Kovid 19.
Mr. Vongsy Visoth, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen received the vaccine, while the Chinese side, represented by Mr. Wang Vinthean, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, handed over the vaccine. .
The reception and handover ceremony will take place at Phnom Penh International Airport. From February 20, 2020 to March 25, 2021, Cambodia identified a total of 1,872 people with 19 cases of Kovid, including 1,056 who were cured and 809 who were being treated. .
Cambodia, like any other country in the world, has made great efforts to find the Kovid 19 vaccine for its people. Cambodia has already received 19 doses of Kovid 19 vaccine, equivalent to 924,000 doses. Of these, 600,000 doses were vaccinated with the Chinese government and 324,000 doses provided by Kovak through the World Health Organization.
About 700,000 doses (300,000 doses for the Ministry of National Defense and 400,000 doses for the Ministry of Health) are expected to arrive in Cambodia in the near future. With the advent of the vaccine, it is expected that Cambodians will be vaccinated to prevent further Kovid 19 and also contribute to the success of Cambodia in the fight against Kovid 19.
