Phnom Penh Capital Administration Launches More Than 100 Street Lighting Poles on New Boulevard from Borey Angkor Phnom Penh to Grand Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration has launched 100 street lighting poles on a new 30-meter-wide boulevard from Angkor Phnom Penh to Grand Phnom Penh to enhance Phnom Penh's beauty and reduce crime. Other and traffic accidents as well.
This new boulevard is nearly 6 km long and has a central park from Street 1003 (turn to Aeon Mall Sen Sok) along the main canal north of Phnom Penh to Victory Blvd in Russey Keo district, Phnom Penh. .
The installation of the above two canals was carried out by the Phnom Penh Capital Administration on the night of March 24, along 100 main canals north of Phnom Penh, from Borey Angkor Phnom Penh to Grand Phnom Penh in Russey Keo district.
Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, while leading professional officers and authorities to inspect the construction site on the road on the afternoon of February 15, 2021, he had already confirmed that the new boulevard above. Due to the participation of philanthropists who have been developing housing along this road in collaboration with the Phnom Penh authorities.
This boulevard will be built in two steps, the first step from Street 1003 to the front of Grand Phnom Penh and continue from Grand Phnom Penh to Victory Boulevard, which is 30 meters wide with a garden in the middle with placement Drainage networks on both sides of the road as well.
It should be noted that the construction of the above boulevard started on September 7, 2020 in the presence of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh. The new boulevard runs in a straight line that connects Angkor Boulevard to the Camko roundabout. It is a kind of twin road with a length of 5860 meters and a width of 30 meters. It is a concrete road with a thickness of 20 cm.
There are 12 meters on each side of the road, 2 meters on the central park and 2 meters on both sides of the sidewalk. There are 3 lanes for cars and 1 lane for motorcycles. Drainage network on both sides of the road with a size of 0.8 meters, a length of 11,720 meters and install drainage across 8 road widths.
