Chin Malin, Spokesman for the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, on March 25, 2021, welcomed the new Special Rapporteur. He told Fresh News that he expects three points from the new Special Rapporteur on human rights cooperation in Cambodia:
1. Able to cooperate honestly with all stakeholders in Cambodia, including government, political parties, civil society organizations, as well as opposition groups.
2. To study, research, analyze, evaluate, report and make recommendations on the human rights situation in Cambodia professionally as an independent researcher and expert rather than a politician, and to be based on the technical aspects of rights, the actual situation and the context of Cambodia, too, rather than based on its own political agenda and tendencies.
3. Properly perform its duties and responsibilities as mandated by the mandate of the UN Special Rapporteur and adhere to the principles and charter of the United Nations, in particular political neutrality, mutual respect, and respect for sovereignty. Of the state and non-interference in the internal affairs of the sovereign state.
