Chinese State Council Information Office Releases 'US Report on Human Rights Violations 2020'
BEIJING, March 24 (Xinhua) - The State Council Information Office released a report on "US Human Rights Violations 2020" on March 24. The preamble of the report states that by 2020, Kovid 19 has spread rapidly around the world, posing a serious threat to the safety and well-being of humanity. Mutual solidarity and cooperation.
But the United States has not only lost control of communicable diseases in its own country, but also lost political order and racial clashes, setting a record for human rights abuses. As of the end of February 2021, 19 cases of measles in the United States accounted for more than 25% of the global total of more than 500,000 Americans.
People's confidence in American democracy has plummeted to its lowest point in 20 years. American minorities are generally discriminated against on the basis of race or ethnicity. The gap between the rich and the poor is rapidly widening, and the living standards of the lower classes in society are very bitter.
