Astronauts may suffer from memory loss while traveling to Mars, according to a new study
But long-distance travel to Mars is not uncommon compared to sending people to the moon, which is close to our own planet decades ago. We know that space is the most dangerous environment for human life, such as lack of gravity, the presence of radiation, as well as loneliness and ignorance day and night.
It is clear that the long-distance mission to Mars will be the most demanding of the human body and mind compared to any other mission we have accomplished so far during the space exploration effort of about 60 years.
The journey to Mars and back to Earth will take about 14 months, while the exact time of the full mission is estimated to be at least three years. To ensure the safety and success of manned space missions, astronauts need to have the highest level of thinking and understanding skills and the most effective teamwork.
However, according to a new study, the lack of gravity in such missions, especially such as the mission to Mars, which is far from our planet, can have a very negative impact on the ability to Think and understand as well as the astronaut's emotions.
It should be noted that the results of the above study is certainly not new, but the discovery of the same effect is becoming more and more motivated for scientists to think of a comprehensive solution. Will decide to lead people to Mars, because we can not let them take the risk that lies ahead.
