China and Taiwan were separated after the end of the civil war in 1949. For decades, China has maintained that Taiwan is a province under international law, while the United States has recognized the one-China policy since the 1970s.
Recognizing the one-China policy is tantamount to recognizing Taiwan as just one Chinese province. However, Beijing has repeatedly warned that it will use military force to invade Taiwan if Taiwan dares to declare independence or any outside force wants to secede from China.
Former Director of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Department of Land Management sues Mr. Pheng Vannak for 4 crimes and demands $ 100,000 in compensation (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Prak Poly, former Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and an advisor to the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction decided to sue Mr. Pheng Vannak to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for four offenses, demanding $ 100,000 in damages.
In a complaint filed with the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on March 9, 2021, Mr. Prak Poly sued Mr. Pheng Vannak on charges of incitement to discrimination, public defamation, insult and aggravated assault. Against public officials and threats to defame and aggravate the situation.
In both of these articles, Mr. Pheng Vannak described that the Governor of Banteay Meanchey, Mr. Ou Rath, proposed to appoint Mr. Prak Poly as Deputy Governor. Mr. Pheng Vannak stated that Mr. Prak Poly had a godfather who was the Deputy Prime Minister, so he was nominated as the Deputy Governor, although he had made mistakes in the province when he was the director of the provincial territorial department.
In the same complaint, Mr. Prak Poly further stated that in addition to attacking him on the news of his appointment as Deputy Governor in all live broadcasts, Mr. Pheng Vannak spoke harshly and accused and incited discrimination against him. As a Cham, apostate and steals pork.
Prak Poly claims that in fact he never dared to violate his religion. He described Pheng Vannak's remarks as a serious insult to him and to Islam, as well as to the entire Muslim community, which he could not accept.
Mr. Prak Poly further stated that this information is exaggerated, inflated, untrue and false information that pollutes society and incites discrimination against him. News that has seriously damaged my honor and dignity, yes, and the leadership.
In the complaint, Mr. Poly requested that Pheng Vannak be punished according to the law. Mr. Poly demanded $ 100,000 in compensation from Mr. Pheng Vannak.
Please note that recently, Mr. Pheng Vannak was also sued by the Ministry of Cults and Religions and the Siem Reap Provincial Hall. The Ministry of Cults and Religions has filed a complaint with the Kandal Provincial Court for insulting monks and Buddhists, while the Siem Reap Provincial Court has filed a complaint with the Siem Reap Provincial Court for insulting public officials.
