Ministry of Environment Spokesperson: Nine protected communities are preparing procedures to contribute to the conservation of natural resources
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, confirmed to Fresh News on the afternoon of March 23, 2021 that 9 new protected areas are being set up, which makes Increased to 183 protected area communities to apply for establishment and recognition by the Ministry of Environment to contribute to the protection and conservation of natural resources and biodiversity.
Establishment of protected area communities to establish dialogue partnerships between communities and the Royal Government, providing responsibilities for management, exchanging ideas, finding common solutions, participating in the protection and conservation of natural resources, as well as participating in the preservation of traditional and tangible cultural heritage. And intangible to survive and join the Royal Government in creating ecotourism to boost the local economy.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Environment stated: "The number of new protected area communities will be nine, bringing the total number of communities in Cambodia under the Ministry of Environment to 183. The community is preparing a process to request the establishment and recognition of the Ministry of Environment.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra emphasized that the purpose of establishing a protected area community has three points, including:
* First: Provide opportunities for local communities to contribute to the protection and conservation of natural resources and biodiversity.
* Second: Provide easy access to government institutions and institutions to facilitate intervention and development of local livelihoods and economy, rights and legal framework to local communities.
* Third: Participate in the implementation of the policy of decentralization and centralization of the Royal Government.
At the same time, Mr. Neth Pheaktra continued that the financial support by the project and the partner organizations of the protected area community members also contributed to the suppression of natural resource crimes, including the release of traps, which in 2020, park officials and local communities. Nature protection has removed nearly 50,000 traps, cracked down on crime in natural resource areas, nearly 8,000 cases, confiscated more than 4,000 chainsaws and nearly 1,000 firearms, etc.
With the right policies of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the community will prosper in the future. You will make the right decisions for the future of the community. The Royal Government of Cambodia, the Ministry of Environment, wants to see the smiles, solidarity of the community, the children of the people study deeply, organize the community economy, grow and natural resources are better protected for future generations.
At the same time, the Ministry of Environment would like to thank the park officials and the protected area community for their dedicated efforts to protect and conserve natural resources for future generations.
