BEIJING (Reuters) - Discrimination against Asian Americans, including Chinese expats and overseas Chinese, has recently emerged in the United States, leading to more violent crimes. Happened too often.
On March 20, marches and rallies erupted in several parts of the United States to protest the growing hostility of Asian Americans in the United States. Recently.
From the deaths of six Asian women in a shooting to the death of an Asian man in his 70s being beaten on the street and the death of two Asian women in a car crash. 100 meters in traffic accidents, crimes against Asian Americans in American society are getting worse.
Racial discrimination in the United States has become a systemic problem in American society. In fact, in the United States, minorities, including those of Asian, Latin American, and African descent, all face serious discrimination.
