(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on March 23, 2021 issued a guideline for the implementation of the three-day traditional Khmer New Year holiday from the 14th to the 16th of March. April 2021.
In the instructions received by Fresh News, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training advised all factory owners or directors to follow any of the following options:
Workers who work this New Year holiday are entitled to a bonus equal to the normal working day wage. The owner or director of the factory shall prepare a list of workers to be taken leave, leave on each of the above dates and keep it regularly for inspection by the Labor Inspector.
* Second: This leave shall be applied in conjunction with the holiday during Pchum Ben or any other appropriate holiday in the future, requiring the agreement between the employer and the employee representative or worker representative.
