Ministry of Justice Establishes Subcommittee on Kovid 19 Vaccination
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, has decided to establish a subcommittee on vaccination against Kovid 19 to manage and administer the vaccination work in the units under the Ministry of Justice and at all levels of the courts.
The sub-committee is chaired by Ms. Chan Sotheavy, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Justice, accompanied by four Vice-Chairmen: Mr. Kim Santepheap, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Justice, Mr. Keng Somarith, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Justice, Mr. Oung Sophearin, Under Secretary of State of the Ministry of Justice and Mr. Tim Sipha Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Justice.
The sub-committee has 15 other members who are officials under the Ministry of Justice.
This sub-committee has the following duties:
1: Compile statistics on vaccination volunteers code-19 in the units under the Ministry of Justice and at all levels of the courts. Leaders and civil servants of the Ministry of Justice, as well as judges, prosecutors, clerks, bailiffs and court officials of the Trial Chamber at all levels
3. Coordinate the operation of Kovid-19 vaccination to the leaders and civil servants of the Ministry of Justice, as well as judges, prosecutors, clerks, bailiffs and court officials of all levels of the Trial Chamber who volunteered to vaccinate Kovid-19 in accordance with the decision of Nationwide Commission on Vaccination Code 19
4. Prepare a report and report to the Minister of Justice on vaccination and other related matters.
