Samdech Techo Hun Sen tells Singaporean ambassador not to let Kovid 19 destroy cooperation between the two countries
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen on Tuesday morning, March 23, 2021, paid a courtesy call on the new Ambassador of Singapore to Cambodia, Ms. Chhay Le Ching.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo Prime Minister's personal assistant, during the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Ambassador mentioned the long-standing relationship and cooperation between Cambodia and Singapore.
Ambassador Chai Leqing noted that the two countries have good relations and good cooperation in the fields of economy, trade, investment, technology and human resource development.
She also mentioned that the two countries still have a lot of potential to seek cooperation together. In this regard, the Ambassador expressed her commitment to do her best to strengthen and expand the relationship between the two countries to be stronger and more prosperous.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, welcomed the Ambassador's commitment. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also raised a number of obstacles caused by Kovid 19 disease. Samdech Techo emphasized that Kovid 19 disease has destroyed all humanity, put a gap in even in this meeting to wear a mask during the conversation.
Samdech Techo added that despite the difficult obstacles, these issues should be overcome to promote relations and cooperation between the two countries. In this regard, Samdech Techo gave the idea that Cambodia and Singapore must promote relations and promote the implementation of all agreements and memoranda that have been signed so far. In addition, seek other cooperation in line with the potential that both countries have.
Please note that in this meeting, the Ambassador expressed his pleasure and honor to be appointed to work in Cambodia. She thanked Samdech Techo for taking the time out of his busy work to meet her.
She praised Samdech Techo's leadership and congratulated Samdech Techo for leading Cambodia towards rapid development. In particular, achieving economic growth in recent years and reducing poverty rapidly.
