1: The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports would like to thank and call on parents to continue to support the process of online learning, reading and all forms of education in the new direction of education. In fact, parents should spend time at home next to their children to read to their children and read to them by choosing books or digital content that children like to read in addition to textbooks.
2. Parents should keep their children at home to study, have fun, draw, exercise and do housework as much as possible, but do not let their children go out to do other unnecessary things.
3: Please students eat enough sleep.
5: The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports would like to thank and call on the education staff, management, educational institutions, teachers and all stakeholders to continue to implement the measures of the Royal Government and the guidelines of the Ministry of Health as consistently.
Cooperation between the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and relevant ministries and institutions, including the private sector, plays an important role in promoting the provision of distance education services, which the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports turns the challenges of Kovid-19 into an opportunity to strengthen education. Digital as stated in the Education Strategic Plan 2019-2023.
