BEIJING: Since the 18th National Congress of the Communist Party of China (CPC), China has made great achievements in overcoming the obstacles to eradicating poverty, and the task direction of overcoming the obstacles to eradicate poverty is near.
Chinese President Xi Jinping stressed the need to strengthen the achievement of overcoming obstacles to eradicate poverty and continue to promote the link between comprehensive eradication of poverty and rural development. The eradication of poverty is not the end, but the starting point for a new life and a new struggle.
With regard to the variability of key conflicts, it is important to be clear about the concept of employment, to promote poverty reduction strategies, and to change the labor system in a stable manner to be included in the rural development strategy. Xi Jinping made important recommendations on rural development strategies and outlined five roadmaps on rural development:
First, the key to modernizing agriculture is to modernize agricultural technology. To strengthen scientific and technological innovation in agriculture in each region, scientific researchers must provide the best techniques for farmers to use to grow the best food. We need to do a lot of work to manage our land well, manage our environment well soon and improve our production capacity.
Second, industrial development is the material basis of rural development, must focus on the development of modern agriculture and implement industrial development with a focus on increasing farmers' incomes.
Third, human resources are the key to rural development. We must strive to train local human resources and provide human resource guarantees for rural development.
Fifth, in rural development, we need to develop material civilization and intellectual civilization together, improve the mental state of farmers and bring a new face of rural civilization.
Fifth, a good ecological environment is the greatest excellence and a valuable asset of the countryside. Only when the environment is good can our lives improve and good ecosystems become the backbone of rural development.
