(Kampong Thom): A 12-kilometer-long dirt road, although short, has been of great importance to the people of Kork Trabek village, Sralao commune, Taing Kork district, Kampong Thom province, a remote area on the east bank of the Tonle Sap Lake. The construction of this road was carried out with the support of Mr. Thong Khon, Chairman of the Baray and Taing Kork District Assistance Team, as well as some other philanthropists.
The construction of this important road is in response to the request of the people in Kork Trabek village, as in the past it was very difficult for people to travel and transport their agricultural products to and from the above base. Especially during the rainy season and between the rainy season and the dry season, because when the river rises, the road is almost completely submerged, which often makes the mud difficult to travel.
That is why Mr. Thong Khon led the Samdech Techo Machinery Team, which is stationed at the "Hun Sen 5th Development Center", and released the machinery to build the road at the request of the people, while the construction has been going on for two years. And will be decided completely before the Khmer New Year.
The construction of a new road from the dam to the village of Kork Trabek also includes the construction of drainage ditches across the road and canals along the road, as well as help repair the old road from the connection. The dam rises to National Road 6.
Mr. Thong Khon spent about 20,000 US dollars to build and repair the road. In addition, other philanthropists have also donated fuel for the operation of the Samdech Techo team.
According to Mr. Thong Khon, when this road is completed, it will provide many benefits to the people and passengers, both those traveling from National Road 6, as well as people from Kork Trabek Chea village. The special plant will facilitate the transportation of agricultural products, rice, crops, fish, meat, consumer goods and groceries.
He said that through the achievement of this road, Kork Trabek village will no longer be a remote area. In addition to facilitating transportation, the canal that accompanies the road will also act as an irrigation system to irrigate farmers' farmland.
By chance meeting with Mr. Thong Khon during the inspection, the people, travelers, farmers as well as local authorities were very happy, they hope that this important road will facilitate Living a special business will help boost life to another level.
