General Knowledge: How many years did the famous Sam Kok War in China last and cause millions of deaths?
(China): Everyone has heard of Sam Kok or the Three Kingdoms, and some have even seen this famous ancient Chinese movie, but little is known about the great war in Chinese history. This one starts from year to year, causing millions of deaths and causing a lot of destruction.
Since Prince Uy Chao Chao announced the establishment of the Wei Kingdom during 220 AD in Chang-an, the three kingdoms have officially opened. War erupted everywhere, killing millions of people, especially in the central and urban areas, and destroying property, homes, infrastructure, urban achievements, and ammunition.
Sam Kok is considered to be the most bloody war era in ancient Chinese history. According to the Jin Dynasty census, more than 16 million people and troops were killed and more than 2 million homes were destroyed. However, according to data recorded in the late Han Dynasty, more than 56 million people were killed and more than 10 million homes were damaged.
