(Phnom Penh): Dr. Chheng Kimlong, Director of the Center for Innovation, Governance and Democracy at the Asian Vision Institute, affirmed that the Royal Government of Cambodia provides free immunizations to the people. It is important to create confidence for individuals to attract investment to restore the economy.
In addition, Dr. Chheng Kimlong stated that vaccination is to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 infection, which is important in providing the immune system to Cambodians and foreigners living in Cambodia.
Dr. Chheng Kimlong said that through the intervention of the leader as well as the relevant ministries, foreigners living in Cambodia can also get the vaccine, thus confirming the government's involvement in preventing Kovid-19, not just the Cambodian people. It also helps protect foreigners in Cambodia.
Dr. Chheng Kimlong stated that "the vaccine is a guarantee to reduce the spread of Kovid-19 to the community and to individuals in order to protect and maintain public safety and health of the people." "
He said that by providing vaccines to the people is to build trust for individuals, the confidence of the general population. This confidence is very important because when people have confidence, they can have the confidence to do business again.
In addition, Dr. Chheng Kimlong said that during the government can control the spread of Kovid-19, the country can reopen the national economy, which is in a new trajectory.
He said that at that time, not only the trust of the people, it gave the confidence of the private sector in general, the trust of public institutions, which laid the important foundation for social activities, cultural activities, general economic-trade activities to recover.
Dr. Chheng Kimlong argues that the recovery driven by the confidence of the people, the trust of the private sector and public institutions is the guarantee of economic recovery, which is the driving force behind the recovery of the economy. Economy.
He said that when the Royal Government of Cambodia provides vaccines to about 70 percent of the population, Cambodia's community-based protection system will be achieved and this will greatly reduce the likelihood of an outbreak. Kovid-19 disease.
Dr. Chheng Kimlong expects that Cambodia will achieve by the end of 2022 to vaccinate the people. When Cambodia has vaccinated more people, he thinks that both international and domestic tourism will reach a point where there is an increase in the inflow of business, foreign investors will be able to return. .
Dr. Chheng Kimlong said that the simultaneous provision of vaccines to countries around the world would be a good point for the recovery of the world economy, which in the region will also help the local economy.
He said that the provision of local vaccines and the provision of vaccines by various governments to people in their respective countries are the foundation for ensuring population security, public security and promoting economic and trade recovery. In the world.
