Kampot Provincial Governor Inspects Old Steel Bridge in Mak Prang Commune to Rehabilitate Traffic
(Kampot): Mr. Cheav Tay, Governor of Kampot Province, on March 19, 2021, led professional officers and relevant authorities to inspect and evaluate the project to renovate a steel ballet bridge called Chinese Bridge in Meat Peam village, commune. Mak Prang, Teuk Chhou district, to be repaired to facilitate people to travel to and fro.
Mr. Chiao Tai stated that this bridge is very important and necessary to facilitate people to travel through the fields, as well as transporting agricultural products and many large and small trucks every day. Currently, this bridge is old, dilapidated, and leaks on the bridge floor, which makes it difficult for people to travel as well as transport across this bridge.
The provincial governor also instructed the Teuk Chhou district governor and the provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, together with stakeholders, to hold an emergency meeting to jointly study, evaluate the project and examine the feasibility of repairs, as necessary. Improve this bridge as soon as possible according to the standards and technical standards.
It should be noted that the 42-meter-long and 7-meter-wide steel ballet bridge, also known as the China Bridge, was built in 2007 by the construction contractor of the Kamchay Hydropower Company (Sinohydro) connecting Mak Prang and Kampong Kreng communes of Toul Chhou district. After the completion of the hydropower project, it was handed over to the authorities to manage, repair, maintain and use the public until now.
