Samdech Techo Hun Sen Congratulates Bangladesh on Independence Day, Vows to Improve Relations
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, was honored to attend and address the valuable ceremony of the people of Bangladesh. The spread of Kovid 19 became an obstacle that prevented Samdech Techo Hun Sen from attending the ceremony in person in Dhaka.
Although not directly involved, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also delivered a congratulatory message via video. Samdech Techo expressed his pleasure to participate in the message to celebrate the celebration of "100th Birthday of the Father of Bangladesh, Benghazi, Dushek Muji Buraman" and "Bangladesh Independence Day 50th Anniversary".
In his speech, the Prime Minister also expressed his congratulations and appreciation to the Government and people of Bangladesh for the remarkable achievements over the past decade through a realistic and far-sighted leadership. Of the Father of the Nation, Benghazi, Dushek Mujiburaman.
"Under the wise leadership of President Abdul Hamid and Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina, Bangladesh has achieved high economic growth, better social progress and better living conditions for the people of Bangladesh," he said. This huge success has enabled Bangladesh to meet the requirements to leave the least developed countries by 2021.
Samdech Techo also recalled the exchange of high-level visits between the two countries, which took place in the past. In that, Samdech paid an official historical visit to Bangladesh in June 2014 and the official visit of Prime Minister Sek Hasina to Cambodia in December 2017.
Before concluding his speech, the Prime Minister of Cambodia reaffirmed his strong commitment to deepening bilateral relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Bangladesh and to develop a stronger and mutually beneficial partnership. Regional and international framework to contribute to peace, stability and prosperity in the region as well as the world. In particular, overcoming the current global health crisis caused by the Kovid 19 pandemic.
The Royal Government has decided to extend the validity of Angkor tickets for a longer period.
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to extend the validity of the purchase of "Angkor Resort" tickets to international tourists for a longer period from March 11, 2021 to December 31, 2021. .
The decision to extend the "Angkor Resort" tickets to facilitate and improve tourism services and ensure the attractiveness of tourists to Angkor during the outbreak of Kovid 19.
* Regular ticket type
There are three types of Angkor tickets: one-day tickets cost $ 37, three-day tickets cost $ 62 and seven-day tickets cost $ 72. One ticket must be deducted $ 2 to support Kantha Bopha Hospital.
Please be informed that in the first two months of 2021, according to statistics, foreign tourists bought tickets to visit Angkor, a total of 4,194 foreigners visited Angkor with a total income of 172,823 US dollars.
Japanese experts authorize lifting of anti-Kovid-19 alert in Tokyo
TOKYO (Reuters) - A group of Japanese infectious disease experts on Thursday approved a decision to remove Tokyo and surrounding prefectures from a state of emergency as planned this Sunday due to the epidemic. Of COVID-19 in the country is recovering. This is according to a release by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Thursday, March 18, 2021.
Experts' approval paves the way for Japanese Prime Minister Suga Yoshihide in an official announcement on the immediate removal of Tokyo and three surrounding provinces. The latest in the country, a little earlier he informed the parliament of this decision and is expected to explain it to the public at a press conference in the evening.
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia's Ambassador and Permanent Representative to the United Nations (UN), Mr. An Sok Khoeun, reminded the Special Rapporteur not to act as a judge during the report and conclusion.
The warning was made at the 46th session of the Human Rights Council "General Dialogue on the Fifth Agenda on Human Rights Mechanisms and Institutions" on March 17, 2021 in Geneva, Switzerland.
In front of the President of the Human Rights Council, Mr. An Sok Khoeun stated that cooperation is a reciprocal process in which the holder of the same special procedure mandate must fulfill his role with fairness and impartiality. One-sided and non-politicalization.
In this sense, in order for cooperation to be truly effective, special procedure holders should implement three points, including:
* First, fulfill its duties by strictly adhering to the "Code of Conduct" and the "Operational Manual for Special Procedures", which underscores the importance of gathering factual information from properly verified sources. Holders of special proceedings must refrain from presuming wrongdoing and rushing to release a press release without first verifying the information with a government source.
* Second, assist the state in the field of human rights through genuine dialogue and cooperation, taking into account the specific context of each country, and not acting as a judge in making reports and conclusions.
* Third: Provide advice on technical cooperation and capacity building assistance at the request of the state to address the root causes of challenges, rather than just looking at external factors.
"In the end, only by paying attention to the proper implementation of the above protocol can the special procedure mandate holders gain the trust of all states." This is the confirmation of Mr. An Sok Khoeun.
Mr. An Sok Khoeun, on behalf of the Cambodian Permanent Delegation to the United Nations, also supported the ASEAN Statement in emphasizing the need to improve the work of special procedure holders with a focus on professionalism, accountability and responsibility. Honestly.
He said that for the past three decades, Cambodia has accepted six special rapporteurs, whose terms have been extended by a resolution approved by the Consulate, and all requests for a visit to Cambodia have been granted. Approval from the Royal Government. These clearly demonstrate Cambodia's open and constructive participation in this mechanism.
