Phnom Penh Governor Inspects the Maintenance of the Stupa
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of March 18, 2021, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, together with professional officials and relevant local authorities, inspected the process of renovating the statue of His Majesty the King on the side garden. About 95% of the Independence Monument has been renovated so far and is scheduled to be completed by the end of March.
Mr. Khuong Sreng recommended the establishment of a commission to regularly repair and maintain the royal coffin, as well as to maintain the garden around the site.
The Governor stated that this is a place that the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has regularly repaired and maintained, where we always celebrate the dedication of the soul of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk every year.
The Governor of Phnom Penh also recommended a series of repairs, including the repair of the roof, the ceiling, the painting of the upper part of the statue, the repair of the marble pedestal and the rock, as well as the maintenance of the garden, the installation of the sprinkler system. Re-planting, including cutting down old decaying peacocks and replanting them.
Please be informed that the location of the statue of King Ratanakod, including the surrounding garden, has become a beautiful resort with fresh air and popular for international tourists to relax and popular for the general public to exercise to Health as well.
Kovid 19 outbreak erupts at 'February 20' event, severely impacting condominium rentals
(Phnom Penh): Due to the sharp decline in the number of foreign visitors, including the re-emergence of the Kovid 19 epidemic in the Cambodian community on February 20, there has been a greater impact on condominium rental.
Mr. Man Chandy said, "With the outbreak of the February 20 community event, we have not been able to estimate the impact of the condominium rental, as the disease is currently occurring. "The impact of condominium rental is very limited because we are not yet open to foreign investment."
He said that if there is more active participation from the people in closing the community on February 20, and if the Royal Government accelerates vaccination and can reduce the activity, the condominium sector will be better because it is new. Recently, some Chinese investors have come to Cambodia via flights in Sihanoukville, and this is a good sign of a recovery in the condominium sector.
"In fact, the condominium sector depends almost entirely on foreign investors who invest in the condominium sector because they have the right to control, so most foreigners are buying condominiums," said Man Chandy.
He added that currently vacancy in condominiums is high, but prices have fallen slightly by only 5-6 percent. But now there are a lot of changes in condominium rental, changing from annual rent to monthly rent, from monthly rent to daily rent.
He added that the condominium sector could not be frozen even if there were no foreign investors in case investors changed their strategy to rely on the local market by selling or renting to locals at a reasonable price or a good installment plan. For one, the condominium sector is bought by young people for living and is invested by many modern investors.
Please be informed that during the eruption of the community on February 20, in general, the real estate market in Cambodia has not decreased, but in some cases has decreased. This is according to Mr. Chrek Soknim, President of the Cambodian Association of Real Estate Appraisers.
Mr. Chrek Soknim claims that the real estate market continues to be strong due to the ongoing activities in this field.
Mr. Chrek Soknim said, "The February 20 community event is a new event that is more serious than the first and second events, but I expect it will close in a month and a half or two. Long months. "Looking at the current state of the real estate sector, it is still continuing its work, although we see that at the beginning of March, not many people travel out, especially to go out to buy and sell this property."
He added that although there is not much activity to visit and buy and sell, but the business is still going online and there are activities to visit land to find investment opportunities in the suburbs.
