Asia Vision Institute Holds Workshop on "Mekong Challenges: The Role of Mekong-Japan Cooperation"
(Phnom Penh): The Asian Vision Institute (AVI), with the support of the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia, on March 18, 2021, organized a workshop on "Mekong Challenges: The Role of Mekong-Japan Cooperation". In order to bridge the gap between the perspective and the input of relevant policies that are playing an increasingly important role in this growing region.
The workshop was attended by distinguished guests from foreign embassies and relevant ministries in the Kingdom of Cambodia, research institutions, organizations, professors, students and other stakeholders from the Mekong countries.
The workshop reflected that the Mekong region has become one of the fastest growing regions in the world and has attracted the attention of major external powers such as Japan, China, India, the Republic of Korea, the European Union and the United States. United States. Inputs and comments for policies to promote the socio-economic development of the Mekong region were also shared among the participants.
In addition, issues in the Mekong region of common concern and interest, such as the spread of the Kovid-19 pandemic, water and energy management, natural disasters, global warming and sustainable development, are also addressed. Also discussed in this workshop. These non-traditional security issues pose many threats to the hard-won peace and prosperity of the Mekong countries and the region as a whole.
