(Siem Reap): Prahok noodles in front of Angkor Wat temple are attracting a lot of attention from the public. Currently, despite the increase in the number of sellers and the outbreak of Kovid, the sellers of prahok noodles, mostly in Trapeang Ses Chas village, Kork Chak commune, Siem Reap province, in the north-east of Angkor Wat, still have a steady flow of customers. .
As the first seller of prahok noodles in the above location, Mr. Sip Srouy, 51 years old, started selling this new flavored noodles about 2 years ago. He said that at first he and his wife were famous for this delicious prahok noodles and also started to try to sell it, which was initially made in small quantities and delivered at home. After trying it for about six months, Mr. Sip Srouy's prahok noodles have gained the support of more and more people who admire its taste.
He described that before he had 19 cases of Kovid, he sold 2 bags of rice a day, equivalent to 300 kilograms of noodles. Today's sales during the 19-year epidemic have dropped to 1.5 pounds of rice, or about 100 kilograms of noodles.
In addition to selling noodles, Mr. Sip Srouy also sells grilled catfish, duck eggs, sniffles, sugar cane juice and other beverages, which are on sale daily from 9am to 5:30 pm.
Mr. Sikong, a customer from Kralanh district with his family, said that every time he came to the province, he always came to eat this prahok noodles.
As for Mr. Saing Sokhon from Banteay Srei district, he said that he often came to eat with his friends because the cakes here were delicious and the vegetables and fish paired with it made the spicy prahok noodles even more delicious. From ordinary cakes.
Mr. Sip Sroul, the owner of Che Samnang brand noodle stall, stated that the reason why his stall has a lot of customers is because the noodles are freshly made and sprinkled with fresh vegetables, hot water, good hygiene, prompt service to customers. Do not miss when riding through his prahok noodle stall.
