Private sector in Cambodia donates resources to help people living in poverty due to the Kovid 19 crisis in Chamkarmon
(Phnom Penh): The private sector in Cambodia has been actively involved with the Royal Government of Cambodia by donating a considerable amount of resources to contribute to improving the lives of the people affected by the Kovid 19 crisis in the community, especially in the 20 events. February in Phnom Penh.
In fact, Prince Holding Group has brought a large amount of food donations to the Chamkar Mon District Administration to help more than 800 poor families affected by the Kovid 19 crisis.
At the handover ceremony on the morning of March 18, 2021, Mr. Gabrielton, Director of the Public Relations Department and Representative of Prince Holding Group, said that this is an important opportunity to show support to the community. Victim by Kovid 19.
He said that since the outbreak of the February 20 incident, Chamkarmon district has been severely affected. In these difficult times, there are many uncertainties, worries and anxieties. As a private company, we need to recognize that they are considered as an important pillar to support society and play an important role in contributing to the maintenance of the community in which we live and operate.
He said that the company has taken immediate action and cooperated with Chamkar Mon District Hall to make this donation, which includes daily necessities such as rice, noodles and other materials to 804 families in need in the community.
In addition, we also donated hundreds of cases of pure water and drinks to the security forces who work tirelessly 24 hours a day in Chamkar Mon district to ensure the health and safety of the people. Through the efforts of leaders at all levels, he hopes that this donation will help the Royal Government of Cambodia to reach the goal of vaccinating at least 80% of the population, or nearly 13 million people.
On that occasion, Mr. Theng Sothol, Governor of Chamkar Mon District, thanked the company for its generous donations to help the needy people in this Chamkar Mon community. He considered this gift really special and at a time when the district administration is in need of these materials to help more than 800 families in the community who are experiencing livelihood problems due to Kovid 19.
