(Phnom Penh): The Bar Association of Cambodia has signed a Memorandum of Understanding between the National Council of Cambodia for Women on "Cooperation in Providing Defense Services to Poor Women and Girls Affected by Violence and Legal Education". This is according to a press release received by Fresh News this morning, March 18.
According to the Memorandum of Understanding, the Bar Association of Cambodia is obliged to provide protection services to poor women and girls who are victims of domestic violence, victims of sexual abuse, victims of sexual exploitation and victims of domestic violence. In particular, it involves violating the rights, honor and dignity of women, or providing a representative attorney to women who are no longer the cause of the violence.
In addition, the Bar Association can participate in training in the field of law to law enforcement officers of the General Secretariat of the National Council for Women of the Ministry of Women's Affairs and the Capital-Provincial Department of Women's Affairs. Separately, the National Council of Cambodia for Women is obliged to provide financial support of 1,200,000 Riels per case to the lawyer who defended or represented by mandate for the victim.
