Samdech Picheay Sena Tea Banh Instructs Troops to Increase Caution When Kovid 19 Vaccination
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, on March 17, 2021, instructed all army doctors to be very careful when vaccinating 19 Kovid. Get vaccinated.
Samdech Pichey Sena's instructions came after a case of 19 cases of Kovid was transmitted to a soldier named Dara Sakal at the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces General Command, who had already been vaccinated against Kovid 19 twice.
For the army doctors in charge of the vaccination, Samdech Picheay Sena advised to be extra careful, especially when interviewing the soldiers who went to vaccinate. Samdech said that doctors must protect themselves, even if they have been vaccinated, because the disease does not discriminate against people who vaccinate or not vaccinate.
Samdech Picheay Sena also warned all troops not to be negligent, especially to implement health measures properly.
At the same time, Samdech urged the interviewer to ask more information about the above 19 new Kovid patients in order to know the exact source of the copy.
