(Siem Reap): On the morning of March 17, 2021, the Siem Reap Provincial Electricity Authority and a representative of the provincial police commissioner visited and provided financial support to the police who investigated and cracked down on a suspect who stole a power line.
Colonel Lim Sambath, Prasat Bakong District Police Inspector, thanked the Siem Reap Provincial Electricity Authority for providing funds to the Prasat Bakong District Police Force as an encouragement for the efforts to crack down on burglars.
He said that he has already handed over the funds sponsored to each unit. He also thanked the leadership of the Siem Reap Provincial Commission for encouraging the forces directly.
At the same time, Brigadier General Pheng Chendareth, Deputy Commissioner for Criminal Planning of the Siem Reap Provincial Police, said that today he came on behalf of the representative of Major General Tith Narong, the Siem Reap Provincial Police Commissioner to guide, strengthen and encourage the police force in Prasat Bakong district added.
He said that in this case, he would like to commend the police forces of Prasat Bakong district, which have cooperated to successfully crack down on the theft of power lines. He also thanked the Siem Reap Electricity Authority for supporting and providing incentives to the police force of Prasat Bakong district.
