For more details, please read the full EDC statement: Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia: Patriotic principles governing Hong Kong ensure long-term stability for one country, two systems policy
On March 11, 2021, the 13th National People's Congress (NPC) of the 13th National People's Congress (NPC) passed a resolution on improving the electoral system of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (China) by a vote. The highest vote (received 2,895 votes, one abstention) set up a new system for improving the electoral system of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region.
During the colonial period, Hong Kong was not democratic, let alone democratic elections. After Hong Kong returned to China, it entered a new historical era of one-country policy, two systems, Hong Kong people's policy, Hong Kong governing and high-level autonomy.
The rights and freedoms of Hong Kong people are greater than at any time in history. The resolution, for example, also improved the mechanism of the Election Commission, which is at the core of the electoral mechanism in Hong Kong. As for the structure, with 1,200 members from four sectors, it has grown to 1,500 members from five sectors.
Chen Qingquan, a professor at the Chinese Academy of Engineering and an honorary professor at the University of Hong Kong, said the decisions and sections related to Hong Kong in the 14th Five-Year Plan have not only complemented each other. Not only does it provide a stable and free environment, but it also offers new development opportunities, like a pair of wings to Hong Kong's prosperous development.
We believe that after the resolution is adopted and the principles of the Hong Kong Patriotic Rule will be applied to another level, Hong Kong's democratic system will be more prosperous and smoother, more prosperous and more stable. Hong Kong will be reassured that the great cause of the one-country, two-system policy will be revitalized.
Xi Jinping always urges young people to pay attention to learning for the future
The effort to learn can only move forward. The Chinese Communist Party has made history through education, and therefore has to rely on education to advance into the future. The cadres must have a leading mind, the Chinese Communist Party must move forward, the nation must move forward, the nation must also move forward, in order to achieve these aspirations, it is necessary to adhere to study and practice.
History is the best textbook. Young people need to learn more about the history of the Party as well as the history of New China, as well as the reform, opening up and progress of socialism. The welfare of the people must be kept as the greatest political fruit of the government.
China will continue to be a country that strives to learn, no matter how developed it is, to learn from the people of the countries of the world with a gentle attitude, with a more open and inclusive attitude, and continue to increase the learning environment. Separate and connect to continuously promote the level of openness.
Reading is learning, consumption is learning and more important. Leaders and cadres need to learn from questions and problems, let people be teachers, learn and practice, do not talk but do not practice. Think of learning as a lifelong passion and a healthy lifestyle.
