The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications encourages students to consider choosing to study digital technology, or even if they are studying other skills, to have a basic knowledge of digital and information and communication technology to be ready to participate in digital economic and social development and The arrival of the fourth industrial revolution.
Mr. Chea Vandeth said that the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications will cooperate with the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports to prepare a digital government plan to promote digital literacy in both secondary and higher education.
