General Vong Pisen issues four instructions to subordinates to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease
(Phnom Penh): General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, on March 18, 2021, issued four directives to his subordinates to prevent and curb the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
According to the instructions of General Vong Pisen, obtained by Fresh News, "With concern about the situation of Kovid-19 disease, which has spread to Phnom Penh and some other provinces, especially the spread. "Into some units of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces recently, although the Ministry of National Defense has implemented the Kovid-19 vaccine has reached almost all soldiers across the country."
The four-point instruction of General Vong Pisen to the Commander of the Special Forces and the Director of the four subordinates of the General Command, including:
First, continue to strictly implement the health measures, especially the "3 prevention 3 measures" of the Royal Government in the fight against Kovid-19.
Second, to disseminate to the subordinate soldiers and to strictly implement the laws and sub-decrees on health measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and other deadly and dangerous infectious diseases.
Third, inspect the location of the cadet in the respective units that have been prepared for cadastralization in case the soldiers in the unit have any contact with Kovid-19 patients.
And fourth, to increase vigilance and tighten the control of forces, including specialized forces, health forces and intervention forces, to be ready in case of regulations.
