Senior officials of the Ministry of Economy and the Cambodian Fishermen's Association hold a video conference to address the challenges of fish farmers
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Phan Phalla, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Mr. Kao Thach, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of ARDB Bank, On March 16, 2021, an emergency video conference was held to discuss the problem of fish congestion in the pond.
The purpose of this meeting is to find out the real reasons for the drop in fish prices and to find inputs and specific solutions to the problem of declining prices of aquaculture in Cambodia.
The main challenge of aquaculture in 2021, namely in the first quarter from January to March, is the congestion of fish in the pond without brokers to catch fish as in the past due to fish imports. All species are imported from neighboring countries, which has severely affected the fish that local aquaculture farmers are trying to raise.
Through this emergency meeting, the members of the Cambodian Fishermen's Association made a request to the Royal Government of Cambodia and the relevant ministries, especially the Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries and Fisheries and the Ministry of Economy and Finance to find urgent solutions to the problem of falling prices. Of these fish, along with the stalemate, most of the fish produced locally from January to March are not yet available from brokers.
