The operation took place at 7 pm on March 15, 2021 by the 815th Border Police Battalion in collaboration with the Internal Security Department, the Malai District Police Inspectorate and the Malai District Gendarmerie under the command of General Ek Sam Vanvirak, Head of Internal Security Department.
Colonel Ben Sam Ath, Malai District Police Inspector, said that the two suspects were:
The two brokers hid 14 male and female workers in the Mimi Guesthouse in Doung Village, Malai Commune, Malai District, Banteay Meanchey Province, in preparation for crossing the border illegally to Thailand on the night of the 15th. March 2021. Om Chanra, a 63-year-old man who owns the Mimi Guesthouse, did not cooperate with the authorities who provided the location for the workers to hide.
The inspector confirmed that the two suspects and the innkeeper were being interrogated at the district police inspectorate to prepare a case to be sent to the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police for legal action. The 14 workers are being questioned at the inspectorate. Phnom Penh Capital Hall: 21 more places related to Kovid people need to be reopened
