(Ratanakkiri): The Ratanakkiri Provincial Administration has issued a notice to the public that weddings, parties and Buddhist gatherings have been temporarily suspended in order to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease in the community.
Ratanakkiri provincial administration ban comes after Cambodia erupts on "February 20" events in alarming situation, and the number of Kovid-19 cases continues to rise One day. Therefore, please follow the instructions of the Royal Government and the Ministry of Health, which have been published continuously and in the sense of preventing Kovid-19 disease from spreading to the community of Ratanakkiri province.
First: Suspend all weddings, parties, housewarmings, Buddhist gatherings, gymnasiums, karaoke, bars, discos, beer gardens, meetings, seminars, training sessions and events with large crowds. .
Second: All entrances and exits of municipal, district, commune, sangkat, departments, units, public and private institutions, restaurants, hotels, car stations, waiting places in crowded places must have thermometers, alcohol sprayers, QR Code scanners to prevent Kovid-19 at Adequate access to all units and public institutions.
Third, local authorities, communes, sangkats, municipalities and districts must continue to monitor, guide and restrict local people traveling from outside the province to implement self-defense measures and prohibit the movement outside the province if not necessary.
Fourth, continue to promote the implementation of the high recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, 3 and 3 firmly protect.
Fifth, in the case of funerals or funerals, which may take place during this period, it can normally be held in the traditional way, but only within the circle of relatives, without having to be crowded and must be practiced. Adhere to the safety measures of the Ministry of Health.
Sixth, if the community event on February 20 is relieved, the provincial administration will notify the re-launch of the programs as mentioned above.
