(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority on March 16, 2021 issued a notification on the status of water supply of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority in the dry season 2021.
The announcement that Fresh News this evening, Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has requested the people living in the center of Phnom Penh who have enough water and the right pressure, please save water to use. Possibilities and opportunities for people in the suburbs of Phnom Penh to have access to water in the sense of sharing water during this scarce season.
According to the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, in the context of Kovid-19, which affects all currents of the entire national economy, the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority is also affected. However, despite this difficult situation, Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority still operates its customers in Phnom Penh and Takhmao 24 hours / 24 hours and every day.
Although the river level has dropped lower than usual during the dry season, water production and water use are still unbalanced, with water supply differences in water pressure high or low as customers rush to use during the dry season. But one means that demand exceeds supply capacity, which will cause water pressure in the suburbs to continue to decrease than before or lack of water in some suburbs.
Currently, Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant is actively under construction, which was presided over by the opening ceremony of the construction site by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on February 1, 2021.
