Commentary: China's strong economic growth in recent years
From January to February this year, investment in fixed assets across China rose 35 percent year on year, according to data released by the National Bureau of Statistics on March 15. Over the same period last year, total retail sales of social goods increased by 33.8%, while the value added of small and medium-sized industrial enterprises nationwide increased by 35.1%.
Although widespread epidemics have occurred in some areas this year, China's measures to prevent and control the spread of the epidemic and to effectively implement macro-policies have worked. An important supporting role in strengthening the trend of economic recovery that has not come easily.
For example, during the traditional Chinese New Year 2021, many Chinese regional administrations have launched initiatives calling on Chinese people to celebrate the Chinese New Year in the area, which is not only conducive to preventing and controlling growth. The spread of infectious diseases not only promotes the rise of indicators such as the promotion of industrial production and provides additional energy to industrial production.
It should be noted that in the process of resilient growth of the Chinese economy, the momentum of innovation still needs to increase steadily. From January to February this year, the value-added value in the high-tech business increased by an average of 13 percent over the past two years, and the value-added value in the equipment business increased by 10.2 percent. Both growth rates are higher than the 8.1 percent growth rate of medium and large industries in general.
In addition, new products are also constantly growing. Production of new products such as new energy vehicles and industrial robots has grown at an average rate of more than 30 percent over the past two years. It is not difficult to see that China's resilient economic growth is moving towards the goal of high-quality development.
China's newly-concluded National People's Congress (NPC) has reaffirmed that it will continue to support macroeconomic policies and support enterprises, as well as maintain smooth policy implementation. This will bring more expectations and confidence to the key players in the market.
