General Neth Savoeun affirmed that the enforcement of the law on land traffic in accordance with the spirit of Sub-Decree No. 39 of the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Development in 2020 has achieved positive results by reducing the number of accidents, deaths, injuries and Property damage. But road accidents are still a long-term challenge, putting daily risks to the lives and property of our people.
In order to achieve the plan of the National Road Safety Committee in 2021 to reduce the number of accidents, deaths, injuries and property damage to the maximum, the National Police General Commission would like to recommend to the specialized departments and the Capital-Provincial Police. As follows:
* First, it must be based on the good experience achieved in 2020 in each geography of the capital and province, by clearly defining the goals, targets, causes, and timing of accidents or violations of the law in order to strengthen enforcement measures. Law on Road Traffic in the Spirit of Sub-Decree No. 39
* Second: To continue to inspect and restrict the types of offenses for motorcycles and tricycles, and the offenses for all types of vehicles, as instructed on May 1, 2020. Separately, for all types of vehicles that have been stopped and inspected in case of committing any of the 9 offenses, additional inspections and actions shall be taken in accordance with Sub-Decree No. 39 on the following offenses:
* Driving a vehicle without a technical inspection certificate (check) or using an expired technical inspection certificate (Article 7 new, point 4a)
* Driving a personal vehicle or legal entity without applying for a business license or using an expired business license (Article 7 new, point 3 "C" and Article 11)
* Third: Increase the enforcement of the law on workers' cars, passenger cars, sand trucks and all kinds of trucks to ensure that all drivers have a valid driver's license, legal vehicles. Adequate, technically correct and safe storage or transportation as required by law.
* Fourth: Strict action must be taken against the perpetrators of road traffic accidents who escaped by continuing to investigate and arrest and bring to justice according to the law. At the same time, the data of these harmful people must be included in the modern technology management system and disseminated to the relevant public and private institutions.
* Fifth: To increase the regular education of police officers under the supervision of an honest, gentle, polite but firm in performing their duties. With this, it is necessary to regularly monitor public reactions in social media to clarify, resolve requests, respond to false information and assign regular inspections to prevent inactivity in a timely manner.
