Comment: Consumer rights must be protected
However, despite the protection and vigilance of our consumers, there are always opportunists who illegally engage in the production and trafficking of counterfeit or substandard products or the provision of "trapping" services. »To the point of forcing customers to accept their services in order to benefit consumers.
Unscrupulous traders often list traps in the dark that lead to consumers unknowingly trapped. Some consumers, after realizing that they have bought counterfeit or substandard products or fall into the "shadowless trap" of unscrupulous traders, but because they do not want to "save a lot", think that they have lost without thinking. From the protection of their legal rights.
In this sense, traders must compete fairly in accordance with their conscience and the law. Enterprises or factories must produce products with the right standards and distribute them honestly, honestly, restaurants must sell food with hygienic standards and good quality, shops must sell quality and legal products, farms must supply agricultural products that are not damaged and have the right standards, especially traders can not sell Or provide compulsory services.
In short, as a supplier or service provider, we must always adhere to the protection of safety, health and respect for the rights of consumers. Consumers should also work together to protect their rights in accordance with the law in order to make the market more orderly and fair, better quality products, safer food, especially consumer rights must be protected. .
