Samdech Techo's statement was made on Facebook in response to a citizen who said that the sub-decree on health rules to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 had severe fines.
It should be noted that on March 12, 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to promulgate a new sub-decree on health rules to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and other serious and dangerous infectious diseases. More.
This sub-decree sets out health measures in accordance with the Law on Measures to Prevent the Outbreak of Kovid 19 and other serious and serious infectious diseases to protect the lives of the people, public health and public order, and to reduce Maximize the impact of this infection on the social and economic sectors in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The sub-decree stipulates severe fines and penalties for those who do not follow the rules of health in the fight against Kovid 19.
Article 19 stipulates that a health officer or competent authority shall issue a warning and recommendation to a person who fails to perform the duty of wearing a mask as stated in article 5 or the obligation to maintain a personal safety gap as stated in article 7 of this sub-decree.
A warning and guidance shall be given by the health officer or the competent authority to the person responsible for organizing the gathering of people or other social activities that do not respect the measures to maintain the social safety gap as stated in Article 7 of this sub-decree.
The Ministry, institution or competent authority may decide to impose additional administrative measures as stated in Article 4 of the Law on Measures to Prevent the Outbreak of Kovid-19 and other serious and dangerous infectious diseases to those responsible. In organizing public gatherings or other social activities that have committed the above offenses.
Article 20 states that warnings and instructions shall be given by health officials or competent authorities to enterprises or private establishments or business owners who do not perform their obligations in relation to wearing masks and maintaining safety gaps as stated in Article 6 and Article. 7 of this sub-decree.
In case of continuing to commit the same offense, shall be punished as a transitional fine from 2,000,000 (two million) Riels to 10,000,000 (ten million) Riels. The competent ministries and institutions may decide to impose additional administrative sanctions as provided in Article 5 of the Law on Measures to Prevent the Spread of Kovid-19 and other serious and dangerous communicable diseases against enterprises or private establishments or business owners who Committed the above offenses.
The payment of the transaction penalty does not exempt the individual from committing the offense by having health officials conduct a sample for KD-19 testing.
Shall be punished by a transitional fine from 500,000 (five hundred thousand) Riels to 2,000,000 (two million) Riels for a person who performs a willful act who does not perform the duties as stated in points 1 and 2 of Article 13 of this Sub-Decree. . The payment of the above transaction penalty does not exempt the person who has to perform the transcript from the obligation to perform the transcript.
