General knowledge: Which country made the first constitution, in what year? In what year did Cambodia establish its constitution?
(World): The Constitution is the supreme law of each country, in ordinary language it is called the master of laws and norms. In this sense, the laws and decisions of state institutions must be in strict accordance with the Constitution.
The United States was the first country in the world to establish a constitution on June 21, 1788. The Constitution of the United States is made up of Article 7, Preamble 1, and is signed.
The constitution was ratified by a national agreement of 17 September 1787 and then ratified by several states. Ratification was completed on June 21, 1788.
Cambodia first drafted its constitution in 1947, and by 2021, it has been amended eight times. The change came after Cambodia changed its regime.
Angkor Hospital for Children Announces Continuation of Child Rescue Mission Despite Difficult Circumstances
(Siem Reap): The Kovid 19 crisis cannot stop the mission of Angkor Hospital for Children to improve its health care system. This is the title of a news article published by Angkor Hospital for Children, which has been on a mission to treat poor Cambodian children for free for about 20 years.
Although the global crisis in 2020 caused the loss of a large portion of Angkor Hospital's assistance, the hospital's management refused to abandon pediatric patients in need of treatment.
According to a report by Angkor Hospital for Children in the last six months of 2020, the impact has been both positive and negative on the health of Cambodian children.
Dr. Nguon Chanpheaktra, Director of Angkor Hospital for Children, said, “The influence of Kovid 19 is a wave that our whole society must pay attention to. "Children's health is very important, so it is our duty to reduce these impacts, especially vulnerable children in impoverished areas."
"Along with the negative effects, we also see some positive effects, such as changes in the behavior of the Cambodian people related to hygiene, especially the practice of hand washing and house cleaning, which is a factor in stopping the spread of coronary heart disease. 19 After educating people about the prevention of this disease in the community. This is according to Mr. Phoeuk Amara, Deputy Director of the Community Health Office of Angkor Hospital for Children.
These behavioral changes have helped prevent many other diseases, such as diarrhea, parasites, and respiratory diseases, which are important ways to protect the well-being of children and infants. Looking back at the fundraising activities, despite the difficulty of seeking funding, the effort continues.
At the end of 2020, the huge fundraiser "Run for Charity with Say", initiated by singer Say, raised nearly $ 500,000 from the Cambodian people, an activity to make Angkor Children's Hospital more recognizable. More clearly from the public in Cambodia.
In addition, a number of businesses and philanthropists who have never provided assistance to the hospital are beginning to raise funds to help Angkor Hospital for Children continue its mission in 2020. This is a beautiful and precious picture that shows the unity, culture, sharing Khmer, helping Khmer of the Khmer people in the development of our society.
It should be noted that Angkor Hospital for Children regularly treats children from birth to 16 years old, with an average of about 400 children coming to the hospital per day.
For the new year 2021, in addition to the high quality and compassionate care of children, the management and staff have also made plans to reduce the growth of diseases, malnutrition and other health problems through activities such as providing assistance. Funding for poor parents visiting hospitals, primary health education in new target communities, and follow-up in older communities.
Through many other preventive activities and strategies, Angkor Hospital for Children has actively contributed to the Royal Government of Cambodia's measures to protect and care for the health of the Cambodian people, especially children who are the bamboo shoots of the Cambodian nation. . Svay Rieng residents are more aware of measures to prevent Kovid-19 after the authorities educate and disseminate
