(Phnom Penh): The Law on Measures to Prevent the Spread of Kovid-19 and Other Deadly and Infectious Diseases has been in force since March 12, 2021. This was confirmed by Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, in a press conference on the morning of March 15, 2021.
The new law was promulgated by Acting Head of State Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum on the evening of March 11, 2021, after a few hours of support by the Senate. According to Article 18 of the Constitution, Chapter 6 stipulates that the law on measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and other serious and dangerous infectious diseases has been promulgated.
Please be informed that Sub-Decree No. 27 dated 18 February 2021 of the Royal Government on measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in the community and some other administrative measures is the main mechanism to force individuals Those who violate the Royal Government's measures will be punished.
The use of sub-decrees is still widespread and violates a series of government measures to prevent infectious diseases, especially Kovid 19, which is currently occurring. This led the Royal Government to decide on a new law on measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and other serious and dangerous infectious diseases in order to prevent the spread of infectious diseases more effectively.
