Phnom Penh Capital Hall: Those who recover from Kovid 19 will be given 14 more days
(Phnom Penh): Phnom Penh Capital Hall will implement a new mechanism by requiring those who recover from Kovid 19 when he is discharged from the hospital to continue to undergo 14 more days. This is a new mechanism to prevent Kovid 19 from re-entering the community.
Phnom Penh Capital Administration told Fresh News on the afternoon of March 14, 2021, Phnom Penh Capital Hall requested the Ministry of Health to introduce a new mechanism requiring those who have been cured of Kovid 19 disease to continue to have 14 transplants. More days to help prevent the spread and spread to the community in the future.
At the same time, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will allow those who recover from Kovid 19 to make four contracts as follows:
1: Continue to work in a private home or private location with a separate room with good ventilation at all times as determined by the Ministry of Health, that is, do not walk out of the house or room or place to be a chandelier and Do not communicate with relatives, friends or any person during the lunar eclipse.
2: Continue to monitor personal health by checking the body temperature twice (2) times a day and if there are symptoms of fever, cough, sore throat, runny nose, difficulty breathing, headache, muscle aches or diarrhea will immediately report to the phone number 115 or group The nearest doctor for examination and treatment.
3. Commit to strictly implement the "3 protections and 3 do's" measures of the head of the Royal Government and the guidelines of the Ministry of Health of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
4. Failure to properly implement or neglect the administrative measures and / or health measures to participate in preventing the spread of Kovid-19 disease is an offense for which the offender must be subject to administrative and criminal penalties in accordance with laws and regulations. In force.
