Clearance force opens site to salvage 800-ton civil war shipwreck in Lvea Em district
(Kandal): General Neang Phat, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense and Chair of the Inter-Ministerial Working Group to Study and Resolve Unexploded Ordnance Disposal in a Shipwreck on the Morning of March 15, 2021 This led the team to open the site of the second submarine clearance operation in Boeung Krum commune, Lvea Em district, Kandal province.
The second groundbreaking ceremony was organized in the Buddhist style of Krong Pali to congratulate the team. The groundbreaking ceremony was also attended by General Chea Sokunthea, Deputy Chief of Cabinet of Samdech Krala Hom, leaders of the Ministry of National Defense and several Kandal provincial authorities.
