The sinking Marine in the Mekong River, Srey Santhor District, Kampong Cham Province, is an old ship from the Cambodian Civil War more than 40 years ago. For more than four months, special forces have been collecting and retrieving ammunition on land. According to the report, from October 2020 until the beginning of March 2021, the team recovered a total of 15,282 kilograms of munitions, as well as six human corpses and other weapons.
