The penalty is set out in a sub-decree on "Health measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and other deadly and serious infectious diseases" promulgated by the Royal Government on March 12, 2021.
Since 2020, in order to prevent the spread and transmission of Kovid 19 disease, the Royal Government of Cambodia has taken measures that are important. However, it is common to see many individuals violating the rules and regulations and stealing from the center.
The old sub-decree of 2015 does not seem to have a clear definition and the fines are also lenient in relation to this practice. Therefore, the Royal Government issued a new sub-decree on March 12, 2021 to increase the efficiency of the census.
The sub-decree also stipulates fines for those who evade the sanctuary or those who facilitate the evaders to escape from the sanctuary.
Article 22 stipulates that a transitional fine of 1,000,000 Riels to 5,000,000 Riels shall be imposed on a person who avoids doing charitable work or escapes from a charitable practice during a charitable practice but does not cause Transmit Kovid-19 to others.
Separately, Article 23 stipulates that the transitional penalty shall be from 10,000,000 Riels to 50,000,000 Riels for the initiator of leading, instructing, inciting, persuading or intentionally facilitating the person who has to do so to escape the control of Chattalysak officials or they know how to do Chattalysak or escape from the place of Chattalysak.
This penalty is in case the evasion of the control of the authorities or the avoidance of the authorities or the escape from the authorities does not cause the transmission of Kovid-19 disease to others.
