Residents in Srey Santhor District, who have had roadblocks for more than 16 years, send a letter of thanks to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Governor of Kampong Cham Province after the dispute is resolved
(Kampong Cham): Four families living in Tnot Leu village, Russey commune, Srey Santhor district, Kampong Cham province, sent a handwritten message thanking Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, for facilitating the settlement. Construction disputes blocking their access for more than 16 years have been successfully concluded.
In fact, on March 12, 2021, the owner of the building that closed their road to the four families decided to dismantle the building and reopen the road to allow them to travel in and out as usual. Crash has no way out until more than 16 years ago there was no solution.
Through a handwritten thank-you note received by Fresh News, the people thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, through Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, for taking care of the problem. People who have been without access for more than 16 years.
It should be informed that the Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on the afternoon of March 10, 2021, led the team to solve the problem of opening public roads: just over 10 hours, which is more than 16 years ago. This case is in Tnaot Leu village, Russey commune, Srey Santhor district, where the parties to the dispute agreed to dismantle the concrete fence and open the road to the public.
Please be reminded that this case of land dispute on public road occurred from 2005 until it was filed in court in 2006 and an urgent order was issued to open the road 3 meters wide. The court ordered the other party to comply, but that party refused to comply with the decision of the order until now.
However, on the afternoon of March 10, 2021, after receiving the high guidelines of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, Governor of Kampong Cham, Mr. Un Chanda led the Joint Provincial Committee to resolve this dispute. Also present were the President of Kampong Cham Provincial Court, Mr. Sous La, and the Prosecutor, Mr. Vong Bunvisoth, as well as the specialized departments, local authorities and the parties on both sides, as well as representatives of the parties.
By following the procedures of resolving the problem and reaching the consent of the parties to build the fence on the public road: to voluntarily dismantle the stone fence yourself. At the same time, in response to the request of the parties to the conflict, Samdech Techo Prime Minister has provided 5 million Riels for the removal of houses and stone fences from public roads that have been closed for more than 16 years.
It should be noted that the parties agreed to accept this settlement with pleasure and expressed their deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, including all working groups who came down to help solve them.
