Sub-Decree: Do not wear a mask or keep a gap at the location set by the authority, a fine of 200,000 to 1 million riels for individuals and a fine of 2 million to 10 million riels for business owners
(Phnom Penh): In addition to the Law governing 19 diseases and other infectious diseases, the Royal Government of Cambodia on March 12, 2021 issued another sub-decree on health measures to prevent the spread of 19 diseases and infectious diseases. Fierce and other serious dangers.
This sub-decree, which has 9 chapters and 35 articles, stipulates fines for individuals and stakeholders who do not comply with the rules set by the competent authorities.
Wearing a mask and keeping a gap is a rule to prevent the transmission of Kovid 19 and other infectious diseases. This sub-decree stipulates the need to maintain hygiene, wear masks and keep gaps for individuals and in enterprises or businesses.
Article 5 states that the wearing of a mask is mandatory based on the work activity or employment status of the individual and in places where there is a risk of transmission or infection. The person who is required to wear a mask and the place where it is required to wear a mask shall be determined by the Ministry of Health based on the level of transmission of Kovid 19.
All enterprises or private establishments or business owners must arrange in their premises to ensure that employees and customers can maintain a personal safety gap when waiting to enter and while in their premises. All enterprises or private establishments or business owners must not accept customers in excess of the number that can maintain a personal safety gap in their premises.
Those responsible for organizing public gatherings or other social activities, such as religious programs, traditional programs, sports or entertainment programs, must maintain the social security gap by minimizing the number of participants and avoiding gatherings. Crowd characteristics according to the guidelines of the Ministry of Health based on the level of transmission of Kovid-19 disease.
In addition to wearing a mask and keeping a distance to prevent the spread of Kovid 19. This sub-decree also stipulates fines for individuals or business owners who do not apply masked measures and keep gaps at locations designated by the authorities.
Article 19 stipulates that a health officer or the competent authority shall issue a warning and guidance to a person who fails to perform the duty of wearing a mask as stated in article 5 or the obligation to maintain a personal safety gap as stated in article 7 of this sub-decree.
A warning and guidance shall be given by the health officer or the competent authority to those responsible for organizing public gatherings or other social activities that do not comply with the measures to maintain the social safety gap as stated in Article 7 of this sub-decree.
In case of continuing to commit the same offense, shall be punished as a transitional fine from 1,000,000 Riels to 5,000,000 Riels. The Ministry, institution or competent authority may decide to impose additional administrative measures as stated in Article 4 of the Law on Measures to Prevent the Outbreak of Kovid-19 and other serious and dangerous infectious diseases to those responsible. In organizing public gatherings or other social activities that have committed the above offenses.
Article 20 states that warnings and instructions shall be given by health officials or competent authorities to enterprises or private establishments or business owners who do not perform their obligations in connection with the wearing of masks and the maintenance of safety gaps as stated in articles 6 and 7. Of this sub-decree.
The competent ministries and institutions may decide to impose additional administrative sanctions as provided in Article 5 of the Law on Measures to Prevent the Spread of Kovid-19 and other serious and dangerous communicable diseases against enterprises or private establishments or business owners who Committed the above offenses.
It is noteworthy that at a time when Cambodia is being severely harassed by Kovid 19, the Royal Government of Cambodia has drafted and promulgated the Law on the Control of Kovid 19 and other deadly and serious epidemics. . In addition to the law, the Royal Government has also issued additional sub-decrees on the management of measures against Kovid 19, as well as other deadly infectious diseases.
Legislation as well as this sub-decree, despite opposition from human rights groups. But for Mr. Keut Rith, the Minister of Justice came out to claim that the law as well as the sub-decree was made to protect the lives of the people and public health only.
