She urged people to take care of their health and take care of their children, not to go out all the time for adults, if it is not necessary, it is better to stay at home than to move to this place, where it is not convenient. Necessary, the risk of transmitting this new virus is very high for you right now.
This is a difficult stage where everyone has the necessary obligation to participate in the implementation of health measures and other measures that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the Ministry of Health have issued, such as the above call, and unite. Fight the shadowless enemies and do not know where all of us can go through all the hardships right now.
The full text of the above views is as follows:
As the richest countries in the world are dealing with the shortage of Kovid vaccine, 19 poor countries have also expressed serious concerns about access to the vaccine. So far, both solutions can be hidden in places that are easily seen: vaccines from China and Russia, and soon possibly from India.
When these countries inspected these vaccines, they confirmed their decision to accept them based on the safety and efficacy evidence presented by Chinese and Russian vaccine manufacturers (most of which were also tested). Published in scientific journals such as Lancet and JAMA) or after they run independent tests on their own.
In the face of vaccine shortages and delays in distribution, France, Spain and Germany are beginning negotiations to order vaccines from China and Russia. In the past, they have raised calls for a vaccine against non-Western vaccines.
The fact is that no Kovid 19 vaccine has been developed or demonstrated as transparently as it should be. Just because China and Russia can do better on their vaccines than Western companies does not mean their vaccines are bad.
There is ample evidence that Chinese and Russian vaccines are reliable and should be given the utmost attention, especially in distribution to the world.
In addition, major Western pharmaceutical companies have objected to granting their vaccine rights to non-Western manufacturers.
So how can these vaccines build confidence in those who want them more? One way is to have them formally evaluated by an international organization with technical expertise. At present, the World Health Organization (WHO) rules for recognizing vaccines are doubtful, depending on the ideas of rich countries, especially in the West.
For the whole world, the World Health Organization has created a service called Privilege. Theoretically, this is a way that vaccines from China or Russia can be placed on an equal footing with vaccines from the West. In fact, it is a difficult and time consuming process.
Doctors and activists have proposed to increase the widespread distribution of vaccines produced in the West. These are called good care, but they themselves also assume that vaccines from Western countries are the only drugs that are worth the wait.
There is an easy solution in hand: "It 's time to start believing in vaccines from other countries." Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen Praises and Encourages Traffic Police Women in Siem Pang District, Stung Treng Province Who Sacrifice Everything for Their Children and Work
