Commentary: China's Second National Congress focuses on innovation in order to make development more high-quality
(Beijing): Technology has now become the most active factor of modern productivity. How to make innovation an inexhaustible driving force for the prosperity and growth of a country is a challenge in this era that needs to be addressed.
During this year's two sessions of China's National People's Congress, innovation and technology were the most talked about issues. According to statistics, in 2019, China's budget for scientific research reached 2.2 trillion yuan, a double-digit growth for the fourth year in a row, and the total size ranked 2 In the world.
According to the "Global Innovation Index Report" released by the World Intellectual Property Organization, in 2019, China's innovation index ranked 14th in the world, maintaining the upward trend for four consecutive years. Each. These data show that China has entered the "innovative country" and is moving towards the goal of entering the "innovative country".
At present, China's development stage, environment and conditions are changing, so there is an urgent need to strengthen the capacity driven by new technological innovations. At present, China's technological innovation is at a critical stage, shifting from large quantities to high quality.
Bringing technological innovation to drive high-quality development means that supply, demand, environment, research, planning, investment and foreign trade, as well as national and international turnover, are essential. High quality too.
By accelerating the building of an innovative nation, China, full of enthusiasm and vitality, is leapfrogging one important goal after another in the pursuit of dreams.
