Minister of Justice: Law "Kovid 19" created to protect the lives of citizens and public health (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Minister of Justice Mr. Keut Rith said that the law on "measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and disease Infectious and other serious diseases "designed to protect the lives of citizens and public health. The penalty is only for the wicked who intend to spread the disease.
The law, which has six chapters and 18 articles, stipulates severe punishment for those who do not comply with the rules set by the Royal Government or the Ministry of Health to prevent the spread of the disease, with severe fines and imprisonment. Also.
Some civil society groups have reacted to the law. They see this law as an additional intention to restrict the rights and freedoms of citizens.
In a statement defending the law at the Senate, Keut Rith said the law was drafted after Cambodia was hit by 19 Kovid infectious diseases, an acute disease that has affected livelihoods, the economy and society. Citizens' lives, too.
The minister added that the law was designed to prevent and curb the spread of disease in the Cambodian community, especially to protect the lives of people and public health.
