Ministry of Posts warns postal business owners to stop doing business without a license and permit
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has issued a notice warning business owners in the postal sector to stop doing business without a license and license. This is according to the announcement that Fresh News just received on March 11.
The Ministry states that in accordance with the law on the postal sector and regulations, all types of postal business of the Kingdom of Cambodia must be under the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications. Every post business owner requires a license and a permit to do business.
In order to promote the management of the postal sector effectively, efficiently, orderly and protect the interests of consumers, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications would like to inform all business owners operating in the postal sector to cooperate as follows:
1. For business owners who do not have a license for the head office and a permit to open a branch located in Phnom Penh must apply to the General Department of Posts of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications.
2. For business owners who do not have a permit to open a branch located in the province must apply to the Provincial Post and Telecommunications Department where the branch is located.
Business owners who have not yet complied with the above regulations must hurry to apply for a license and / or license by April 30, 2021. Phnom Penh Authorities Permanently Close Love Guo Ji Business Club in Daun Penh District in Violation of Kovid 19
