Experts from the Ministry of Environment are studying fossils of animals in Koh Por, Koh Kong province, according to the study may be 65 million-190 million years old
(Phnom Penh): The archeological team of the Ministry of Environment is studying bone fossils found on Koh Por next to Tatai Wildlife Sanctuary, Bak Klang Commune, Mondul Seima District, Koh Kong Province.
