"After review and discussion, the Standing Committee of the Senate has set Thursday, March 11, 2021 at 8:00 AM for the 4th Extraordinary Session of the Senate with the agenda," the statement said. "The only thing is to review and comment on the draft law on measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and other serious and dangerous infectious diseases."
It should be noted that in order to effectively control the spread of Kovid 19, the Royal Government of Cambodia has drafted a law on "Measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and other deadly and dangerous infectious diseases."
The purpose of this draft law is to identify health measures, administrative measures and other measures to be taken to combat and prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and other deadly and serious infectious diseases to protect the lives of the people. Citizens, public health and public order, as well as minimize the impact of this infection on the social and economic sectors in Cambodia.
This draft law has 6 chapters and 17 articles. The Council of Ministers approved the draft law on February 28 and the National Assembly passed it on March 5.
