This guideline follows the call and recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the Ministry of Health in the context of the outbreak of Kovid-19 in the "February 20" community event to avoid the spread of Kovid-19 in the community. Large.
In the instructions stated that the Ministry of Rural Development would like to advise leaders and civil servants at all levels under the Ministry to follow the following guidelines:
1: To increase vigilance and strengthen the implementation of "3 protection and 3 do not" measures strictly.
2. Allow officials to work at home through the online system and to organize a small number of staff (10%).
3. Suspend all workshops, trainings, outreach and other meetings except online meetings.
4: Take care to protect personal and family health by wearing a mask and washing your hands often with soap and clean water or alcohol or regularly.
5. It is necessary to maintain the social safety gap and the personal safety gap of more than one and a half meters.
6. All entrances and exits shall be subjected to regular temperature measurements and wear of masks, in case of non-compliance, they shall not be allowed to enter the Ministry premises.
