General Knowledge: Cambodia has a total of 23 major bridges in daily use by 2020
(Phnom Penh): Bridges are an important part of supporting the public sector and transportation, as well as actively participating in the promotion of the national economy, under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, see that Cambodia has construction. A series of bridges to facilitate the travel and transportation of people.
According to the report of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, as of 2020, Cambodia has 23 major bridges that are serving the means of transportation and daily transportation, including:
First, the Tse Basa Bridge (Neak Leung Bridge) across the Mekong River from Leuk Dek District, Kandal Province to Peam Ro District, Prey Veng Province, a cable bridge with a length of 2,215 meters and a width of 13.50 meters.
Second, Koh Kong Bridge is located in Koh Kong Province, crossing the Koh Por Sandok canal from Khemarak Phoumin City to Mondul Seima District, a concrete bridge with a length of 1,900 meters and a width of 11 meters.
Third, the Mekong Bridge is located in Stung Treng Province, across the Mekong River from Stung Treng City to Thala Parivat District, a concrete bridge with a length of 1,731 meters and a width of 13.40 meters.
Fourth: Kizuna Bridge across the Mekong River, from Kampong Cham City, Kampong Cham Province to Tbong Khmum District, Tbong Khmum Province, a concrete bridge with a length of 1,500 meters and a width of 14 meters.
Fifth: Prek Tamak Bridge is located in Kandal Province, crossing the Mekong River, Sandok, from Muk Kampoul District to Khsach Kandal District, a concrete bridge with a length of 1,066 meters and a width of 13.50 meters.
Sixth: Sekong Bridge is located in Stung Treng City, Stung Treng Province, across the Sekong River, a concrete bridge with a length of 1,057 meters and a width of 11 meters. This bridge transports passengers from Stung Treng City to the Trapeang Kriel International Border Gate.
Seventh: Prek Phnov Bridge (Lyong Phat Bridge) is located in Phnom Penh, crossing the Tonle Sap River, crossing from Prek Phnov District to Khan Chroy Changva, a concrete bridge with a length of 996 meters and a width of 14 meters.
8th: Prek Kdam Bridge is located in Kandal Province, across the Tonle Sap River, from Ponhea Leu District to Muk Kampoul District, a concrete bridge with a length of 981 meters and a width of 13.50 meters.
9th: Koh Puos Bridge is located in Sihanoukville, a 900-meter-long concrete bridge over Koh Puos under private management.
10th: Tonle Bassac Takhmao Bridge or Samrong Bridge is located in Kandal Province, crossing Tonle Bassac Sandok from Ta Khmer City to Kien Svay District, a concrete bridge with a length of 855 meters and a width of 13.50 meters.
Eleventh: Cambodia-Japan Friendship Bridge (Old Chroy Changva Bridge) is located in Phnom Penh, crossing the Tonle Sap River from Daun Penh to Chroy Changva, a 700-meter-long and 13.50-meter-wide concrete bridge under the administration. Phnom Penh.
12th: Cambodia-China Friendship Bridge (New Chroy Changva Bridge) is located along the old Chroy Changva Bridge, from Chroy Changva to Daun Penh, a concrete bridge with a length of 719 meters and a width of 13.50 meters under the administration of Phnom Penh. Also.
14th: Koh Thom Bridge is located in Koh Thom District, Kandal Province, across the Bassac River, a concrete bridge with a length of 415 meters and a width of 13.50 meters.
15th: The old Monivong Bridge is located in Phnom Penh, crossing the Bassac River, Sandok, from Chbar Ampov district to Meanchey district, a concrete bridge with a length of 700 meters and a width of 13.50 meters under the management of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration.
16th: The new Monivong Bridge is located along the old Monivong Bridge, from Meanchey district to Chbar Ampov district, a 719-meter-long and 14-meter-wide concrete bridge under the administration of Phnom Penh Capital Administration.
17th: Kampong Thmor Bridge is located in Kampong Thom province, crossing Stung Chinit Sandok from Baray district to Santuk district, a steel bridge with a length of 88.5 meters and a width of 10 meters.
18th: Tang Krasang Bridge is located in Santuk District, Kampong Thom Province, crossing the Tang Krasang River, a type of steel bridge with a length of 109 meters and a width of 10 meters.
19th: Stung Sen Bridge is located in Stung Sen City, Kampong Thom Province, crossing Stung Sen, a type of steel bridge with a length of 140 meters and a width of 13 meters.
20th: Sre Ambel Bridge is located in Sre Ambel District, Koh Kong Province, across the Sre Ambel River, a concrete bridge with a length of 420 meters and a width of 10 meters.
21st: Andong Teuk Bridge is located in Botum Sakor District, Koh Kong Province, crossing the Andong Teuk Canal or Prek Pipot, a concrete bridge with a length of 270 meters and a width of 13 meters.
22nd: Trapeang Rong Bridge is located in Koh Kong District, Koh Kong Province, across the Trapeang Rong River, a concrete bridge with a length of 480 meters and a width of 13 meters.
