Commentary: The General Assembly of the two Chinese Parliaments is the annual roadmap for China's development that has attracted the world's attention.
BEIJING (Xinhua) - The beginning of March each year is a time of great anticipation for people across China, as both houses of the National People's Congress (NPC) will convene to convene a roadmap. New paths for national development, or passing new laws or amending laws for the benefit of the people throughout the country and for the benefit of the world, are also attractive to the world.
Before exploring the General Assembly of China's two parliaments, let's find out what is the role of these two parliaments? Why is the opening of the annual general assembly so popular throughout the country and the international community?
The first is the National People's Congress (NPC), China's supreme authority under the auspices of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress. The NPC and its Standing Committee are the implementers of the national legislature. The NPC is composed of representatives of the people from the provinces, autonomous regions, municipalities under the Central, Special Administrative Region and the army. There must be minority members as well. NPC has a term of 5 years.
Now let's look at the role of these two parliaments. NPCs have important rights such as: amending the constitution, overseeing the implementation of the constitution, approving various laws, and electing the president, vice president, etc. The CPPCC, on the other hand, has the role of political advisor, observes the implementation of national politics in a democratic manner, participates in politics and discusses political issues.
What is special during the opening session of the two houses of parliament each year is the presentation of the Prime Minister's Government work report, which summarizes the old annual work and sets the work direction for the new year. The report has been dubbed by the Chinese people as the "steering wheel of a Chinese ship" that will lead people through the storms of the new year and the future towards the shores of prosperity.
In particular, in the work report of the Chinese government this year is different from four years ago, because this year is also the beginning of the implementation of China's 14th Five-Year Development Plan, therefore, Chinese Premier Li Keqiang. Set out work directions for 2021, but also outline master plans for development over the next five years. This is the great concern of the Chinese people of all walks of life and the international community.
As we all know, the setting of a government direction is closely related to the development of a nation and the well-being of its people. China has always upheld the interests of the people as a whole, and has done politics for the benefit of the nation and the people. The NPC will discuss and approve.
Regarding the master plan for the next five years, the Chinese government's work report states:
* Economy is functioning properly * Urbanization rate should be raised to 65% * Average life expectancy increased by 1 year * Urban and rural job loss rate maintained at 5.5% * Older population 95% will get life insurance for the elderly
Now let's look at the key directions mentioned in this year's Chinese government work report:
In this regard, China seeks to increase employment opportunities every year, as well as encourage graduates to start their own businesses under various favorable policies, keeping the unemployment rate to a minimum.
As we all know, China is the world's second largest economy, so China's development is not only relevant to the Chinese people, but also closely related to other countries in the world. Also, especially in the context of Kovid-19, China, which has the first major economic growth and positive growth, what else will contribute to the global economic recovery?
In fact, we all always expect that countries will have more and more peaceful cooperation, less disagreements and conflicts to build a prosperous world together. Prosperity and lasting peace.
