The same farm owner said that they did not know why such a drop in prices, no buyers. This makes them lose at least 3 to 40,000 US dollars per factory.
Due to their high cost of raising chickens, the price is 2,000 riel per chicken, 15,000 chickens can raise up to 20,000 chickens in small and large farms. The day is over for sale. But now his chickens have dropped in price by 1,500 riel, there are no more buyers, and the chickens are up to 50 to 60 days old.
They face huge losses by paying for chicken feed, water, electricity and workers' salaries. They are asking the Minister of Agriculture and companies to help strengthen local prices and strengthen the market for local chicken farmers like them.
Farmers have stated that all market-free chickens grow in size and weight, making them much cheaper. The farmers added that each cage has 15,000 chickens, some of which have 20,000 chickens, and need to spend $ 30,000 to $ 40,000 at a time if there is no market for as long as now.
Farmers and farm owners said, "The Minister of Agriculture should take care of the affected farm owners, because raising meat for sale on the market is expensive, most borrow money from the bank to run a business. This.
