Ministry of Public Works Issues 9 Additional Guidelines to Implement Urgent Measures for Prevention and Control of Kovid-19 Outbreak
(Phnom Penh): To participate in the prevention and control of Kovid-19 virus in the February 20 community event, which has been increasing rapidly in the relevant capitals and provinces in Cambodia, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport has launched Provide urgent and strict measures to the leadership and staff of all civil servants under 9 points to increase participation to implement more effectively.
* First, all General Departments / Units must reduce the number of civil servants who come to work at the Ministry / Units instead of working from their respective homes online, but must be organized. Civil servants on a rotating basis in each unit in a small amount of only 10% until further notice.
* Third: The Personnel Department shall review and monitor the reporting data on the health status of the civil servants and contact immediately if any suspicious cases are reported and shall cooperate with the Department of Information Technology and Public Relations to prepare the results report. Monitor the health of civil servants by completing the above digital forms to the Ministry's leadership on a regular basis.
* Sixth: The Department of Administration must control all entrances and exits by setting the temperature and wear masks regularly, in case of non-compliance, it is strictly forbidden to enter the premises of the Ministry.
* 7th: All units, especially civil servants who work directly with documents at the port of entry or traffic officials, must scan and disinfect all documents before sending all those documents in accordance with the law. Way to the relevant management or unit. In some cases, the transfer and distribution of documents digitally (Telegram) is encouraged.
The issuance of the above emergency measures was made in accordance with the order and special message of the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the night of March 8, 2021 to prevent and prevent the transmission of Kovid-19 virus in the community on February 20. .
