(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection has issued instructions to temporarily suspend missions, meetings, seminars and training sessions or gatherings to participate in the prevention and control of the transmission of Kovid-19 virus in the community on February 20. This is according to the instructions to the civil servants of the Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, obtained by Fresh News on March 9, 2021.
This instruction states that according to the order and special message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on the night of March 8, 2021 to prevent and prevent the transmission of Kovid-19 virus in the community on February 20, the Ministry Liaison with the National Assembly-Senate and Inspection Please provide additional guidance to the leadership of civil servants and all units under the Ministry and all provincial departments as follows:
1. To continue the temporary suspension of one week of missions, meetings, seminars and training courses or gatherings until there is a new order from the head of the Royal Government. Each unit can arrange job replacements online (at home).
2. All units must keep only the most necessary officials at a maximum of 10% to work at the Ministry. In addition, allow civil servants to work at home online. Complaints and other missions are also suspended, pending new instructions.
3. Restricting security and order in the Ministry and the entrances and exits by requiring the same entrances and exits in front of the Ministry for officials who are in charge as assigned by the unit leaders and participate in heat, hand washing and cleaning with alcohol. And scan QR Code to prevent Kovid-19. Failure to comply with this principle will not result in entry into the premises of the Ministry.
4: Must strictly implement the measures "3 do not and 3 protect" according to the high recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
5. Implement social safety measures and individual safety gaps. Maintain regular hygiene by wearing a mask. Practice clean hand hygiene by washing hands with soap or alcohol.
6. Have a high sense of responsibility. If you suspect that you have been exposed to Kovid-19 or have suspected Kovid-19 symptoms or have a suspected cold, you should participate in the Kovid-19 test and be isolated immediately.
7: To report or if you have any questions, please call the hotline 115.
According to the same instruction, the leadership of civil servants at all levels under the Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection and all capital-provincial departments must strictly follow this instruction with a high sense of responsibility.
