The reason for the suspension of the Xin Yin Thai Hotel business was because the emergency response team of the provincial health department took samples from guests staying at the hotel and the test results were positive for Kovid-19 virus.
"In this regard, the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration has decided to temporarily suspend all types of business of the Sin Yin Thai Hotel and to set it up as a Chattalysak Center from the time of this notification until further notice." This is according to Mr. Kouch Chamroeun.
He added that at this stage, all stakeholders with the hotel must take a test sample and perform a proper catheterization according to the instructions of the Ministry of Health. In case of non-compliance with the above instructions, the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration will take action according to the procedures in force.
It should be noted that a man who ran away from this hotel to his hometown in Kang Meas district, Kampong Cham province also found 19 positive cases of Kovid, but for those involved, both directly and indirectly, the authorities have already taken them to court.
