The following is the announcement of the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration: Ms. O Vandin: "3 Defend 3 Doom" in the role of women in the context of the fight against Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): To celebrate the 110th International Women's Day on March 8, Ms. O Vandin, Secretary of State and Outstanding Spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, on March 7, prepared an article entitled "3 Defend 3 "in the role of women in the context of the fight against Kovid 19, which highlights the heroism and role of women in the fight against Kovid 19. Please read Ms. O Vandin's full article below:
Article written by: Lok Chumteav Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, Celebrates "International Women's Day March 8"
From the beginning of human history, we have observed that naturally there is already a gender-segregation, which as a result of the evolution of human life in the world has gradually created gender inequalities. Already gone until there is a demand for respect for women's rights and attention to the role and participation of women in activities that contribute to the development of society.
On the basis of respect for women's rights and the gradual recognition of competencies and realities that reflect the importance of women's participation, the attention of women in countries around the world We are also gradually starting to allow women to be actively involved in social work.
In fact, in the context of the fight against Kovid-19, women in Cambodia have been playing an important role in taking responsibility for preventing the spread of this deadly disease for themselves, their families and their communities. .
Not voluntarily vaccinating against Kovid-19 is a lack of vital equipment and protection for one's body, as well as a good chance of serious bodily harm when the Kovid-19 virus enters your body. That you can reach death.
The success or failure of the war with the shadowless enemy of the Kovid-19 virus depends on the genuine participation and dedication of all citizens, including foreigners living in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
I wish all women good health to continue their noble mission to participate in preventing the transmission of Kovid-19 virus and may all women avoid the spread of this deadly disease. May all women enjoy International Women's Day on March 8 and be safe and strong to be a strong core force of the nation.
BEIJING: China is ready to work with the United States to restore bilateral ties, Chinese State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi said on Sunday. Get back on track. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on Sunday night, March 7, 2021.
Wang made the remarks at a press conference on Sunday, stressing that the two sides should monitor the outcome of a telephone conversation between Chinese President Xi Jinping and US President Joe Biden on Chinese New Year. The past has set the relationship between the two countries on a new path of healthy and stable growth.
"As two countries with different social systems, China and the United States usually have differences and disagreements," he added. "But the most important thing is to manage it effectively through honest communication to prevent strategic misunderstandings and avoid conflicts and confrontations."
Wang said it is not surprising that there is competition between China and the United States for their own interests. But both sides should have a healthy competition based on justice and equity.
