In terms of size, Venus is so similar in size and shape to our planet that it is said that Earth and Venus are brothers. Because of this, it is suspected that Venus may have some form of life similar to Earth.
In terms of temperature, Venus is religiously like a fiery furnace of hell because of its dense atmosphere filled with greenhouse gases and about 1,600 large active volcanoes and many smaller ones. The surface of the planet has a temperature of up to 464 degrees Celsius, the temperature of which can dissolve some lead or metal in an instant, so it can not make any life possible.
Atmospheric pressure is 92 times stronger than Earth, which is similar to us sinking to a depth of more than 1,000 meters. In such pressure and heat, if people reach it, it is like a hot iron furnace and pushes us together, we will burn and die instantly.
On the other hand, Venus has strong winds of up to 724 kilometers per hour, which may be stronger than the major storms on Earth, such as cyclones or typhoons. For all these reasons, spacecraft that reach the surface of Venus are often damaged, unable to operate for long, and make the United States more interested in colonizing Mars than Venus.
