(Phnom Penh) - On March 6, 2021, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the Army and Chairman of the Sub-Committee on Security and Order Management in Target and Chattalysak Area, inspected Training of troops preparing to intervene to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease of the Security Management Sub-Committee of the 70th Brigade.
Speaking on the occasion, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet stated that our nation, our people and our families are at risk of the war on Kovid-19, which has had a major impact. Health and well-being have also created discrimination and fear among citizens across the country and around the world.
Now the nation and its people need forces to join forces with this invisible enemy, so be prepared to train and fully equip them to successfully carry out safe regulations to carry out joint tasks. Thorough protection of the Chaktabsak area ensures the prevention of the spread of Kovid-19 disease, which is the greatest enemy of the nation, society and family society.
