Nearly 50 students at Samrong High School, Sot Nikum District, Siem Reap Province fainted
(Siem Reap): About 49 students at Samrong High School, Sot Nikum District, Siem Reap Province, this morning, March 6, 2021, fainted while they were studying. Doctors suspect this case is due to a series of fears.
A report from the Siem Reap Provincial Information Department quoted Mr. Mak Pros, Governor of Sotnikum District, on the morning of March 6, saying that 49 Samrong High School students in Samrong Commune, all female students, had fainted and cried. Authorities and teachers transported to Sotnikum District Referral Hospital and Samrong Commune Health Center for examination and treatment.
Mr. Seng Sophea, Director of Samrong Health Center, Sotnikum District, said that 29 victims with serious symptoms were taken to Sotnikum Referral Hospital and 16 were hospitalized at Samrong Health Center and 4 were hospitalized. The other has been resting at Popel Health Center.
"According to the interrogation, the victims fainted when they ran out of the classroom and cried after seeing the shadow of a long-haired woman in the classroom."
He added that the same thing happened on March 5, with only about five to six people, and on March 4, there was only one person while they were studying at night. At the same Samrong High School.
The director of the health center said that according to the examination of blood pressure, sugar and oxygen in the body, there are no symptoms, so the victim is normal health, presumably no disease other than panic disorder. He also asked parents to advise their children to eat a lot and get enough sleep to avoid health problems when they are sleepy and malnourished, they may also have hallucinations.
Regarding this incident, the governor of Sotnikum district added that so far, the victims who were hospitalized at the district referral hospital and other Samrong health centers have been relieved and have returned to some homes, while others are At rest, wait to be healthy for a while, but no serious illness.
He added that the doctors took care of their health very carefully. Please note that this is the first time that a large number of students fainted, up to 49 in Siem Reap in early 2021. Mr. Thong Khon promotes work to prepare for the commune elections and strengthen the policy of safe villages and communes. In Baray and Tangkork districts
