Understand the law: crimes in the field of information technology
Of course, technology really makes it easier and less time consuming, and there are many benefits to using that technology. In particular, some people have used the advancement of these technologies in a bad way, committing various crimes through those technologies, which is causing problems for society as well as other users. What activities can be considered as IT related crimes?
Today, Fresh News' Legal Awareness Program in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation would like to raise the topic of "Information Technology Crimes" to the people and students. Which activities can be considered as crimes related to information technology as follows:
Therefore, in the Penal Code from Article 427 to Article 432, it states about activities or acts that are considered as offenses in the field of information technology, such as:
At the same time, legal experts from the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Justice and related units have been studying the draft law on cyber crime, which has seven chapters and 48 articles to prevent some online crimes such as arrests. Online kidnappings and scams after many problems in Cambodia.
In summary, any act or activity that infiltrates the private data of another person without permission is an offense facing the law. Technology is also the two main arrows, it can make us easier in daily life, work and communication, and can also pose a risk to us in society if we take advantage of the advancement of technology. In a bad way.
