The handover ceremony was held on the morning of March 6, 2021 at the location of the house in Sangkat Trapeang Krasaing, Khan Por Senchey in the presence of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh and accompanied by Mr. Hem Darith, Governor of Por Senchey and his wife. Both Duke Leng Navattra.
Mr. Khuong Sreng distributed to 30 families in Chhong Ruk village, and then Mr. Hem Darith, on behalf of the governor, continued to distribute to 15 families in Trapeang Anchanh community, Sangkat Trapeang Krasang.
Mr. Khuong Sreng confirmed that this is the second time that Samdech Techo has donated food to the people who have been doing rituals at home.
Mr. Khuong Sreng confirmed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen always take care of the people and these food gifts are provided to facilitate their daily life while doing meditation at home.
The governor of Phnom Penh continued that the administration also has a policy of subsidizing 20,000 riels per day for 15 days for people to do charitable work with four qualifications. The four qualifications include: being directly involved in the "February 20" community event, being tested, and having a negative result, being a homemaker in a house or a hotel, and being a poor person.
Mr. Hem Darith stated that out of these 45 families, 30 families live in the barn village and 15 families live in the Trapeang Anchanh community. They are the people involved in the February 20 community event.
