BEIJING (Xinhua) - The annual National People's Congress (NPC) inaugurated the Chinese People's Republic of China (PRC) Li Keqiang on Tuesday. China's growth rate this year, which has attracted global attention, is set to exceed 6 percent.
Most of the external estimates for China's economic growth rate are higher than 6%, according to the International Monetary Fund, China will grow 8.1% this year. But China has set a growth rate of more than 6 percent, which means that 6 percent is the lowest figure and has applied "excess", which differs from the "approximate" stated in previous years. This year will probably be higher than this figure.
