Religious harmony! Khmer-Muslim couple invite monks to cook their wedding day
(Phnom Penh): Outbursts of interest and admiration for a Khmer-Muslim couple who invited monks to cook on their wedding day because it is rare and shows the peace of religion in society Khmer.
Mr. Chhorn Vibol, Deputy Director of the Office of Buddhist Affairs and Social Affairs of the Department of Cult and Religion of Kampong Speu Province, who learned of this, told Fresh News that the Khmer-Muslim couple who did something shocking and very interesting. The groom, Sled Sly, and the bride, Aziz, live in Village 13 Krom, Koh Sotin Commune, Koh Sotin District, Kampong Cham Province.
Mr. Chhorn Vibol confirmed that the invitation of monks to bless and bless the wedding day in a Khmer-Muslim family like this has never happened in Koh Sotin commune.
Mr. Chhorn Vibol said that the monks were invited to pray at the Khmer-Muslim wedding ceremony because the monks in the commune, especially Venerable Heng Hoeung, always had good relations and communication with the Khmer people. - Islam. In addition, Khmer-Muslim brides who marry are also his children.
Mr. Chhorn Vibol added that the Khmer-Muslim couple invited the monks to cook and pray, there was no objection or resentment from the religious leaders of the Khmer-Muslim elders in any village.
Pictures showing the cooking and blessing of weddings of Khmer-Muslims of different religions are very rare, which is why it is so interesting.
Both in the region and in the world today, conflicts between worshipers and of different religions have become a matter of concern. In some lands conflicts over different religions have even ignited wars.
In Cambodia, after the liberation from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, all religions were revived, and people also had the right to practice their religion according to their beliefs. In Cambodia, the most widely practiced religions are Buddhism, which is the state religion, and Islam and Christianity.
Despite the different religions, more than 40 years after the liberation of the country from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, people of different faiths continue to live in the same village and Communicate with the brothers with pleasure.
The image of a Khmer-Muslim wedding in Koh Sotin is another testament to the religious harmony and peaceful coexistence of different religions.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has always expressed his deep satisfaction with the religious harmony in Cambodia, which leads to the well-being of the people and the progress of Cambodian society.
At the same time, may the hand of the soul of the former King, Queen of Cambodia, all of you, especially the soul of His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, please keep the Prince, Queen, Mother of the Khmer Nation. By the four blessings of the Buddha: age, class, happiness, and strength, do not forget.
