After the second vaccination of Kovid 19, the Special Forces Command thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for seeking to give Kovid 19 vaccine to the people for free.
(Phnom Penh): On March 05, 2021, the Special Forces Command organized the second vaccination against Kovid 19 under the cooperation of the working group of the Department of Health, Ministry of National Defense, Health Office, General Command of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Office of Army Health. Land.
The vaccination against Kovid 19 was carried out in accordance with the recommendations of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces. Army Command.
After the vaccination, the Special Forces Command thanked and expressed his gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who was always thinking of finding 19 Kovid vaccine to give to people all over the country for free.
Please be informed that as of now, Cambodia has two types of Kovid 19 vaccine: Sinofam, which is a gift from a Chinese friend and AstraZeneca, which is supported by the World Health Organization through the Kovak mechanism (COVAX). The AstraZenica vaccine was delivered to Cambodia in the initial phase of 324,000 doses on March 2, 2021.
For the Sinofam vaccine, a gift from a Chinese friend, 1 million doses were also given to Cambodia. In the first phase, China shipped 600,000 doses of the vaccine, which arrived in Cambodia on February 7, 2021, while another 400,000 will arrive before Khmer New Year.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has announced that the Royal Government of Cambodia will provide 20 million doses of vaccine for 10 million people to be vaccinated free of charge by one person. Of the 19 vaccines against Cambodia's 20 million doses, 11 million were also donated.
Of the 11 million doses, 1 million doses of Chinese Sinofam vaccine, 7 million doses for the Caucus mechanism, and 28 million dong worth of Australian aid, equivalent to 3 million doses. As for the demand for another 9 million doses, Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that he will continue to request and buy from some countries. Vietnam continues to detect 6 new cases of Kovid-19 in Friday's report
In 4 days, health workers in Kampong Chhnang province vaccinated 19 Kovid 19 to nearly 1,000 frontline officials
(Kampong Chhnang): With the efforts of the Director of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Health Department and the attention of the Director of the Provincial Referral Hospital, only for 4 days from March 2 to March 5, 2021 The referral team of Kampong Chhnang province has vaccinated 19 people against Kovid 19 to the front line officials of the province.
Today, our health workers are injecting police officers, prison officials, health workers, tax officials and customs officers in the province. This is according to Dr. Tum Sambath, Director of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital.
According to the doctor, by the fourth day, the leaders in some provinces have also come to get vaccinated against Kovid 19 once.
More than 700 people were put on duty at the "Yongyuan" casino in Koh Thom district after two Chinese nationals were found carrying 19 Kovids while visiting the casino.
Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, led a team of relevant departments, competent forces and district authorities on March 5, 2021 to inspect the location of "Yong Yuan" Casino, which was made after finding a man. A Chinese man with 19 cases of Kovid is in Sampov Poun commune, Koh Thom district, Kandal province.
In addition, the district authorities and the competent forces have been on guard to ensure safety and not to allow anyone to come out during the siege.
The provincial governor said that the casino has 723 guests and staff who are working on the test and have already checked the test twice and the first test is not. No one was found to be infected with Kovid 19, but after a second examination, a Chinese man was diagnosed with Kovid-19.
