China to create nearly 12 million new urban and rural jobs by 2020
BEIJING, March 5 (Xinhua) - Chinese Premier Li Keqiang said in a statement on March 5, 2021 that the country will face "historic challenges" in 2020, and that China has made employment opportunities a top priority. To the livelihood of the people.
By 2020, 11,860,000 new jobs will be created in urban and rural areas across China, while the urban and rural unemployment rate fell to the end of the year. 5.2 percent. By 2021, China plans to add more than 11 million new jobs in urban and rural areas, with an urban and rural job loss rate of about 5.5 percent.
According to some sources, in December 2020, US non-agricultural organizations laid off 140,000 workers and the unemployment rate was 6.7 percent. The eurozone unemployment rate was 8.3 percent. The unemployment rate in Japan was 2.9 percent and in India it was 9.06 percent, while in South Africa it was 32.5 percent in the fourth quarter of 2020.
Earlier, according to data released by the National Bureau of Statistics, China faces a tense and complex environment both domestically and abroad, especially the severe impact caused by the spread of Kovid 19 gross domestic product. China's GDP in 2010 amounted to 101.6 trillion yuan, up 2.3 percent from the same period in 2019, becoming the world's only major economy. Positive growth.
