How will China plan the roadmap for development in the future? And what benefits will China bring to other countries in the world? The international community is expected to receive even more exciting good news from the General Assembly of both houses of China this year.
14th Five-Year National Development Plan: This year, the National People's Congress of China will discuss the 14th Five-Year National Development Plan and the draft law on long-term vision goals for 2035. According to foreign media reports, this will be one of the topics of this year's General Assembly of the Chinese National People's Congress, which has received widespread attention.
According to the report, by 2035, China's total economic size and average per capita income will double compared to the present, and this goal will be achieved under China's commitment to Achieve an end to carbon emissions by 2060. For China, this is a big challenge.
Development target: China's total economic size by 2020 will reach 100 trillion yuan, and GDP will grow by 2.3 percent compared to 2019. Despite the impact of the 19-Kovid epidemic, China is still moving in the opposite direction of becoming the world's only major economic entity that has achieved positive growth.
Technological Innovation: Since the implementation of the "13th Five-Year National Development Plan", China has achieved significant achievements in building an innovative nation, which has created a situation that provides a strong technological force to Economic development, improving people's livelihoods and national security.
Due to the attractiveness of China's rapid economic growth and the 14th Five-Year National Development Plan, which is about to be announced by the General Assembly of both houses of parliament, global capital is pouring into the Chinese market. As of the end of February, the total value of Chinese treasury holdings held by foreign investors exceeded 2 trillion yuan for the first time, breaking a new record.
It is expected that the roadmap for future development presented by China will send more positive signals to the world and bring more benefits to the development of the whole world. The 3rd Assistance Package for Cambodian Entrepreneurs is still open for applications to help small and medium enterprises and start-ups
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance, through Cambodian entrepreneurs, continues to accept applications for the third grant program to help small and medium enterprises and start-ups.
The package aims to help local businesses, both small and medium-sized, and start-ups in the areas of communications, information technology, agricultural services and manufacturing, facing the crisis during the Kovid-19 crisis.
In fact, to date, there are applicants from almost every province in Cambodia, covering the four main priority areas that Cambodian entrepreneurs have focused on: business, services, hospitality, information technology and agriculture.
Dr. Chheang Vann Monin, Executive Director of Cambodian Entrepreneurs, said, “Seeing the effectiveness of the two Cambodian Entrepreneurship Assistance Packages since 2020, the Ministry of Economy and Finance through Cambodian Entrepreneurs still provides opportunities for local entrepreneurs. "Can apply to compete for a package that can help them stay in business during the Kovid 19 crisis."
He also encouraged entrepreneurs who participated in the competition last season who did not receive the grant package to try again and reminded those who have not yet applied to hurry up so that this golden opportunity does not pass.
In fact, the process of selecting a business to receive this grant package includes: presentation of the business process and strategies for using the budget package until the winner is selected.
