(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries issued a press release as people complained about the high price of pigs between 32,000 riel to 38,000 riel per kilogram.
According to traders selling pork at the market, the previous price was between 15,000 riel, 18,000 riel, 20,000 riel or 23,000 riel, but now the price of pork has risen to more than 30,000 riel per kilogram. . Vendors say the rise in pork prices has forced buyers to cut back on purchases because it affects their incomes.
The people who are the sellers and the buyers have called on the ministries and institutions to help check the case of the increase in the price of pork in this market so as not to raise the price too much, which will affect the people's livelihood as the crisis spreads. Let Kovid 19 seriously affect the economy.
A trader who has been selling pork for more than 10 years at Kilo Market 4 said in an interview this morning, March 5, 2021, that the price of pork in the market has risen sharply between 32,000 riel and 38 riel. 000 Riel per kilogram.
Another pork seller also complained about the impact on their livelihoods as sales were not as good as before due to high prices.
(Pursat): Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province, on March 5, 2021, has been using and fulfilling his role as a servant of the people by trying to mediate and resolve all conflicts as well as 6 different challenges. Brothers and sisters, parents at the forum in the provincial hall.
Coordinating through the above public forum was attended by Mr. Mak Ra, Chairman of Pursat Provincial Council, Provincial Councilor, Deputy Provincial Governor, Deputy Chief of Citizens' Office, District / Municipality, Commune / Sangkat Authority, Record Secretariat and other stakeholders.
Mr. Mao Thunin said that this is a habit that His Excellency always meets with parents and people to contribute to the well-being through the forum now. Previously, he was involved in solving all these problems twice a week, but now, due to the conflict as well as the challenges have decreased, he is involved in solving only once every two or three weeks.
The Governor emphasized that due to the high pressure situation of Kovid 19 epidemic, especially during the February 20 community event, HE decided to select the most important cases in daily life to mediate and resolve first. In fact, today, there are 6 cases where this work must be carried out according to the instructions of the Ministry of Health.
Mr. Mao Thunin continued that the current mechanism is the mechanism of the Royal Government through public forums, which pointed out that the provincial level at the local level directly connects the people with the challenges and needs in daily life. .
He always uses two hierarchies, including:
* First: As the provincial governor to facilitate the resolution of legal challenges for parents * Second: As a family, there are roles as brothers, sisters, children, nieces and nephews in one family of more than 50 people Tens of thousands of people throughout the province to mourn with them at all times.
