Senior Minister Sun Chanthol urges subordinates to increase sales of personal numbers
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, urged members of the Inter-Ministerial Commission to continue their efforts to promote the sale of personal special numbers to large private companies wishing to use special numbers. More personal to raise more revenue for the national budget.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said this on March 5, 2021, during a meeting to review the progress of work and discuss the value of personal registration number at the Ministry with the participation of members of the Inter-Ministerial Commission. Manage the sales of car registration numbers and relevant professional units.
The meeting focused on discussing the progress of work related to the management of vehicle registration and pricing formulas in the online system to ensure the management and collection of more national budget.
At the same time, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also informed about the project development program (App) to reduce the driving license points of drivers who violate traffic laws, such as: driving without a seat belt, speeding and driving in violation of traffic lights. In that program, the police can deduct points on the driver's license of the offender immediately.
The Senior Minister expressed great pride that Cambodia, especially the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, has the ability to use information technology mechanisms to facilitate the provision of public services in line with advances in information technology, globalization and the Industrial Revolution 4.0 to manage and collect Revenues to the state effectively, transparently and save time.
