Annual General Assembly of China's top authority opens in Beijing with future development path set
BEIJING, March 5 (Xinhua) - The fourth session of the 13th National People's Congress (NPC) convened in Beijing on March 5, 2021. Chinese party and state leaders such as Xi Jinping and nearly 3,000 people's representatives attended the opening ceremony.
2021 is the beginning of the implementation of the 14th Five-Year Plan. The general public is paying close attention to how China, which is about to embark on a new phase of building a modern socialist country from all angles, will focus on development.
Chinese Premier Li Keqiang outlined the government's work over the past year, summarizing the fruits of China's economic and social development over the past five years, and outlined key directions and tasks. China's economic and social development during the implementation of the 14th Five-Year Plan to be submitted to the review meeting.
It should be noted that the report of the plan related to the living standard of the people and the state and the report of the national budget were also submitted to the meeting at the opening ceremony of the General Assembly. In addition, the meeting will discuss the draft law on the amendment of the Law on the Administration of the National People's Congress and the draft law on the amendment of the statutory examination of the work of the National People's Congress. Across China as well.
The two draft laws will further legitimize the People's Congress, China's basic political system. The meeting will also discuss the "Draft Law of Resolution of the National People's Congress on the Fairness of Electoral Regimes in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region."
