(Phnom Penh): Macro Sen Sok Market claims that it always pays attention to the safety and health of customers, employees and other stakeholders as instructed by the Ministry of Health to participate in the fight against Kovid 19. This is according to Mr. Sin Vibol, Head of Human Resources of Macro Market, told Fresh News.
When one of the many customers went to Mark Market, Sen Sok Branch on February 20, 2021 and was confirmed to be infected with Kovid 19, Macro Market also introduced additional safety measures to ensure Safety, health of customers and staff.
Mr. Sin Vibol stated that in order to prevent the spread of this disease and ensure the health and safety of our customers and employees as a top priority, we have implemented the following measures:
* First: We usually prevent the spread of the disease to customers and employees by cleaning and spraying disinfectants in all areas of the market and all appliances, in accordance with international health standards every week and carefully. Posted on March 1, 2021.
* Second, we identified and separated employees who contacted and spoke with clients that day and recommended a 14-day work stoppage during which they were monitored for symptoms to ensure they all had Safe and non-infectious.
* Third: A new team of staff has been set up to replace staff suspended during symptom monitoring to ensure that our services can continue uninterrupted after thorough cleaning and disinfection.
"In addition, all employees are asked to wear a mask at all times while on duty in our market. Customers can ensure that we are taking all necessary measures to prevent the spread of Kovi-19 virus for the health of our customers, employees and society in general. We apologize for any inconvenience and thank you for your continued support and cooperation. ” This is an additional confirmation from Mr. Sin Vibol.
