Commentary: "US antagonism does not benefit trade with China at all"
The US Trade Representative recently released the "2021 Trade Agenda Report and 2020 Annual Report." According to the 308-page report, "China" is mentioned 467 times.
The media has noted that China is the only country to be included, especially on the list of countries that "Biden's government will resist." More and more analytical articles are now noting that Biden's government is likely to follow the same path of strong opposition with China, simply "correcting the image but not the content."
In the field of trade, Biden plans to develop a more comprehensive and systematic strategy than the previous government. In the field of high technology, Biden wants to draw allies to jointly oppose China's technology and try to lead China in the field of artificial intelligence in chip technology, as well as advanced technology in the economic and military fields in the future.
There is no doubt that China has provided a huge and incomparable market to the United States, but there is a precondition for cooperation without prejudice. However, it is unfortunate that a small number of large countries have bad intentions. In the face of such evil intentions, China will bravely overcome all obstacles and move forward.
