Romeas Hek District Police Arrest Two Thieves for Stealing Monks' Money at Kampong Trach Pagoda
(Svay Rieng): Two suspects were arrested by Romeas Hek district police after stealing money from a monk's hut in Kampong Trach pagoda, Romeas Hek district at 11:00 on March 4, 2021.
According to the authorities, before the incident, while the monks were going to cook, two suspects went up to the attic and stole 287,000 riels.
They went up to the attic and stole 287,000 riel from the monks. After the action, the two suspects rode a motorcycle to the south.
According to the police, after receiving information from a monk at Kampong Trach pagoda that two thieves broke into the apartment of Romeas Hek District Police Inspector, they ordered to reach all destinations, while the suspect suddenly reached the traffic law enforcement destination. Turning around, the police chased after the car until they arrested the two suspects and confiscated two motorcycles belonging to the thieves and 287,000 riels in cash.
