Commentary: "The Second National People's Congress of China focuses on the well-being of the people in order to make the well-being of the people more comfortable."
BEIJING: From today onwards, China has entered the "time of the two sessions of the National People's Congress", which is held once a year, the fourth session of the National People's Congress, the 13th National People's Congress and The fourth session of the 13th National People's Congress (NPC) will be held on March 4 and 5 separately in Beijing.
As the starting year of the implementation of the 14th Five-Year National Development Plan, the two houses of the National Assembly in 2021 will be especially important. Of all the issues discussed at the two sessions of the National People's Congress, the issues that the Chinese people pay the most attention to are issues related to livelihood.
During the "13th Five-Year National Development Plan", China has been spending more and more money on people's living standards, and living standards in all areas have been continuously improved. At the same time, job search will be the most important issue in people's lives by 2020, and new job opportunities in urban and rural areas across China will increase by 11,860,000.
China's regional administrations have introduced policies to reduce taxes, reduce administrative fees, support enterprises and expand employment opportunities, in order to promote orderly rehabilitation in all aspects of business development. New and new formulas as well as new job opportunities will be created in 2021 as the employment situation is improved economically and generally stable.
In addition, the living standards set by the people in both houses of parliament last year have all been met. The National Social Security Fund system has been consistently accurate throughout China. Nearly 1 billion people are covered by old age insurance, and the rate of participation in basic health insurance is over 95%.
In particular, the precise goals in the field of equilibrium have been well achieved, while social causes such as education, culture, medical treatment, health, sports and exercise have also been developed in all aspects. Adhering to the people-centered and people-loving stance is the governing principle of China's top leader Xi Jinping, which was repeatedly highlighted at the two sessions of the National People's Congress last year.
Especially during the past year, in the context of facing many negative factors such as the outbreak of Kovid 19, the Chinese government has always adhered to the priority of people's lives by working hard to raise the level. Ensure people's livelihood.
