(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly of Cambodia will hold an extraordinary session on Friday, March 5, 2021, to discuss and approve the draft law on measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and other deadly and dangerous diseases. Other serious. This is the decision of the National Assembly Standing Committee meeting this morning, March 4, 2021, chaired by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly.
In addition to approving the agenda for the extraordinary session, the National Assembly Standing Committee approved the composition of three extraordinary session secretaries: Mr. Thong Vorleak, Mr. Ma Chhoeun and Mr. I Sam Ol.
The draft law on measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and other deadly and serious infectious diseases has six chapters and 18 articles that will define health measures, administrative measures and other measures to be taken to combat Prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and other serious and dangerous infectious diseases now and in the future.
This draft law aims to protect the lives of the people, public health and public order, as well as minimize the impact of the disease on the social and economic sectors in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as several other senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia, also vaccinated AstraZenica's Kovid 19 vaccine. After the vaccination, Samdech Techo Hun Sen held a press conference on vaccines and the fight against measles 19 in Cambodia. The following are the main contents of Samdech Techo:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen revealed that the possibility of receiving Chinese vaccine assistance may exceed 1 million doses, while an additional 400,000 doses will arrive before Khmer New Year
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reaffirms why he did not vaccinate China against Sinofam due to age
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the reason why Samdech went out to receive Chinese vaccine directly because the vaccine was the first aid to arrive in Cambodia
* In response to the critics, Samdech Techo Hun Sen claims that China has never ordered Cambodia
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen Thanks to International Partners for Facilitating Vaccine Assistance in Cambodia
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says Cambodia is the first country in the Asia-Pacific region to receive the vaccine from Kovak
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says that in the future, Cambodia will be able to vaccinate 20% of the population from Kovak, but this will be done in stages, which in the first half will be more than 1 million doses
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces once again that vaccination of officials, citizens and foreigners is free
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasizes that vaccination is not the golden solution to eradicate Kovid 19 from Cambodia, but must be combined with three measures to prevent further
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirms that until now, there is no clear source that the vaccine will be effective for any period of time or for life.
