(Siem Reap): The management of Siem Reap Provincial Hospital on March 2, 2021, publicly clarified that the death of Dr. Seang Tola, an officer in the outpatient and emergency department of the Provincial Referral Hospital. Siem Reap is not involved in the Kovid 19 vaccination.
In a clarification letter sent by the management of Siem Reap Provincial Hospital to Fresh News Agency on the afternoon of March 2, 2021, it was clarified that according to the evaluation of the hospital management and the medical team, Dr. Seang Tola died of cardiovascular problems and was not involved in the Kovid-19 vaccine.
According to the letter, Dr. Seang Tola, a 39-year-old man from Phum Thmey, Sangkat Svay Dangkum, Siem Reap City, an active duty officer in the outpatient and first aid department of the Siem Reap Provincial Referral Hospital, died at his home about an hour later. 4 a.m., March 2, 2021.
The letter added: "As usual, the doctor came to the meeting in the morning and was treated until 3 pm. He volunteered to be vaccinated against Kovid-19 (Sinophorm) at the referral hospital. Siem Reap Province. The pre-vaccination examination of the staff at the vaccination site shows that he does not have a problem with the vaccination ban.
After the injection, he followed the rules, rested for 30 minutes, after which there was no disturbance and no problem, he returned to work until 5 pm, then he opened. The car went to pick up his wife, who works at the Angkor Hospital for Children, and then took the children from school to his home, and then he returned to work at the referral hospital until 8 pm before returning home to rest. Back.
According to the letter, the victim's wife and friends confirmed that Dr. Seang Tola had suffocation while sleeping and had severe snoring, especially in the last week, as well as a history of chest pain and frequent heart tests. Also.
The letter stated that, according to the assessment of the hospital management and doctors confirmed that he died before arriving at the hospital.
