The verdict is one of the former French president's longest-running legal decisions. Sarkozy, 66, who led France between 2007 and 2012, remains popular among conservatives.
Sarkozy's sentencing is the second time in modern French history that a former president has been convicted of a crime.
He was found guilty of bribing a judge to illegally obtain intelligence on another lawsuit against him in exchange for promising to use his influence to provide a prestigious position in the country for a judge. .
Under the charges, Sarkozy faces up to three years in prison, with two years suspended. However, the former French president is expected to appeal, delaying the trial.
