(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has decided to cancel the recruitment of 133 new officials for 2021 to help reduce state spending, which is struggling with the Kovid 19 crisis.
In a request to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to cancel the recruitment of new officials on February 25, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, emphasized that the cancellation of the recruitment of officials to save money. National budget for sustaining economic and social stability in times of crisis due to Kovid 19.
The Senior Minister also informed Samdech Techo that although the Ministry does not recruit new officials, it will examine the creative potential of existing resources through the transfer of officials and additional training of human resources within the Ministry and at Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport to ensure quality, transparency and efficiency for 2021 and beyond.
In the letter, the Prime Minister agreed and expressed his appreciation to the Ministry, which has considered reducing the national budget.
