(Siem Reap): Experts to repair the pond north of Angkor Wat have so far completed archaeological research and repaired 56 meters of pond bank and added 60,000 cubic meters of water to the pond.
However, the veil is still closed and tourists are not yet allowed to take pictures of Angkor Wat from the pond, as the project to renovate and upgrade the pond structure may continue to be completed in the next two years.
In 2021, the APSARA Authority has three more pond stairs to be strengthened and is excavating to see the actual damage to complete the project to repair an additional 65 meters in two years, but if the case, it will May procrastinate longer.
The structure of the northern pond is damaged due to the sandstone reacting strongly to the sun with hot water, causing the sandstone to erode and break easily, and in some places the stone disappears, causing gaps, causing water to flow and erode the soil. Into the pond. Therefore, the team needs to study how to strengthen the closure of the gap so that it does not filter again.
