(Phnom Penh): The King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, has ordered the appointment of Keang Seng as Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Interior.
A Royal Decree appointing Mr. Keang Seng as Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Interior was issued on February 25, 2021.
Mr. Keang Seng was born on Wednesday, 11 Roch Khek Tak, Chhnang Chhlov Panchasak, BE 2516, in Wat Kandal Village, Svay Por Commune, Sangke District, Battambang Province. In 1991, he continued his studies at the Chamkar Dong Agricultural Technical Institute (now the Royal University of Agriculture) in the 7th generation fisheries in Phnom Penh.
In 1996, after graduating, he joined the Department of Fisheries (now Fisheries Administration) with the Aquaculture Program of the Asian Institute of Technology in Cambodia. In 2000, he was sent to study at the Asian Institute of Technology, based in Bangkok, Thailand.
In 2011, he completed his PhD at the University of Traditional Medicine in Colombo, Sri Lanka. Dr. Keang Seng is also the founder of Comfort in Cambodia and has the title of Positive Doctor.
Dr. Keang Seng expressed his deep gratitude to the King of Cambodia for appointing him as Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Interior.
Dr. Keang Seng also expressed his gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, for their trust and opportunity to contribute to society.
