(Singapore): Singapore is the smallest country in ASEAN with a total area of more than 700 square kilometers, as the government has set a target to expand by 100 km by 2030, but you may be wondering. Singapore is so small, is there any wildlife like other countries?
The answer to this question is that Singapore does not have wildlife living in the mountains like other countries, but this Asian dragon administration has set up a large zoo for tourists to visit and be able to visit at night. Also.
The Singapore Nightlife Tour continues for nearly two decades, first opening in May 1994, making it the world's first nightlife zoo.
The Night Zoo receives more than 1 million visitors every year. Tourists come here to see many species of animals, including Indian rhinos, squirrels, rare species, reindeer, deer and giant winged squirrels.
Although the zoo is at night, the moonlight-like lighting technology makes visitors feel like they are in a real forest while the animals are not disturbed by light. Shine too. On the other hand, the animals are not tied up or kept in cages, that is, guests can ride a car to visit with a natural barrier.
In addition to the spectacles of wildlife above, what is more special is the cultural performances of ethnic groups, ethnic flutes and fireworks performances, while some animals are trained. To be able to perform circus at night. In the past, the zoo tonight had a tiger out of the park and a Chinese tourist was bitten by a cat while watching the show.
The popularity of this Singapore Zoo has earned it many accolades on the international stage. The Night Zoo is open from 7:30 pm to midnight with a ticket price of around $ 20.
