This subcommittee has the following roles and responsibilities in managing the target areas and areas:
* Lead and coordinate security and order management
* Monitor, evaluate and advise on security and order management
Collaborate with relevant institutions to plan, train and equip the forces and health officers in charge of security and order management.
Develop Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) in the management of security and order to request a decision from the Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Commission on Combating Kovid-19
* Disseminate, implement and monitor the implementation of operating standards (SOP)
* Develop a plan to prepare the intervention force of health officials, materials and means to ensure security and order management.
* In case of need, assign, use and manage the intervention force in the designated target area and Chattalysak area.
* Cooperate with local authorities, institutions and relevant units to perform their duties
* Manage the data of the target operators in the target area and the control area under control
* Develop a plan to ensure the supply of security and order management processes
* Summarize the daily report on the results and activities of security and order in the target area and Chattalysak area during the operation.
Perform other duties as assigned by the Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Commission for Combating Kovid-19.
