Commentary: Efforts to Achieve Success in Eradicating Poverty in China
BEIJING: Recently, a film titled "Emotions for Homeland", a TV movie celebrating the 100th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China, was broadcast on Chinese television. Popular with the Chinese people.
As we enter 2021, China has achieved the task of overcoming the obstacles of poverty eradication, with nearly 100 million poor people lifting themselves out of poverty and achieving the goal of reducing poverty. Under the UN Sustainable Development Agenda 2030, 10 years ahead of schedule, this achievement has created "China's wonder" in overcoming the obstacles of poverty eradication.
What efforts has China made to overcome the difficult obstacles to eradicating poverty? Take a look at the following figures for sure: By 2020, nearly 99 million rural poor will be lifted out of poverty. In 832 poor districts, poverty was eliminated and 128,000 poor villages were eliminated.
The average annual per capita income of the poor rose to 10,740 Chinese yuan. 108,000 compulsory education schools in poor, underprivileged areas have been rehabilitated and improved, and the contribution to the global poverty reduction mission exceeds 70%.
"Helping each other" is a Chinese character in the miracle of eradicating poverty. On the road to building a society where people have a decent standard of living in all aspects can not give up anyone, by overcoming the campaign to overcome obstacles to eradicate poverty and achieve prosperity together is a great cause. The greatness of the Chinese nation and also the greatness of the superiority of the socialist regime.
On February 25, the National Rural Development Administration of China officially unveiled a banner that not only marks the full-scale success of overcoming China's poverty alleviation campaign. It is also the beginning of the restoration of rural prosperity in all aspects and the new struggle for a better life.
In particular, avoiding the return to poverty is the real elimination of poverty. Therefore, I believe that after the success of the campaign to overcome poverty eradication, the Chinese people will continue to follow the path of rural prosperity to open a new era with a brighter future.
