An outstanding alumnus of Kosomak Polytechnic Institute, an electrical engineer, fell seriously ill with cancer and lacked money for treatment. Please call on philanthropists to help as much as possible.
(Phnom Penh): Born from a poor farmer who loves to study, Touch Nonn struggled to become an excellent student, gaining the love of many teachers in the school because of his perseverance and diligence. As an outstanding student, he came to study in Phnom Penh, got a scholarship at Kosomak Polytechnic Institute, majoring in electrical engineering, and worked part-time to earn money for his poor mother in his hometown.
For 5 years, this young man has developed well to become an engineer who is full of work experience, but unfortunately, alumnus Touch Noun has not been able to do much work, he was suffering from malignant colon cancer. He. Going through the first surgery with a doctor in Takeo province and giving him regular medication did not help him recover.
Starting as a construction worker at a theoretical school, the school developed into an experienced engineer born of the struggle to break free from poverty. Going out to work as an engineer, an experienced contractor, but unfortunately not yet well, the malignant tumor came to disturb his friends until he lost his job and lost all his wealth.
Hopefully, his friend can fight this terrible disease to continue his career as an experienced engineer (Chinese company hired him to work because of his ability and perseverance) and hope that his friend still has High commitment to parents who are still waiting for their children, waiting for their children, waiting for their children to be healed.
Mr. Pech Bunly and the struggling young man Touch Non, who was lying in a hospital bed, raised their hands to ask the benefactors to help with this great suffering, while so far he could not afford treatment and despair in the struggle. Keep going.
