(Phnom Penh): The Royal School of Administration and the Korea Research Institute of New Southwale University, Australia, on the morning of February 25, 2021, jointly organized the International Policy Reform Conference for 2021 under the theme "State Capacity for Development. "Nation in the post-Kovid 19 situation, opportunities and challenges for Korea-ASEAN cooperation."
The conference was chaired by Mr. Youk Bunna, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Public Works, Mr. Seung-Ho Kwon, Director of the Korea Research Institute, Mr. Geun Lee, President of the Korea Foundation, Professors, Speakers and Trainees from Australia, Korea, ASEAN Member States and Leaders Officials of the Royal School of Administration, a total of about 700 people through the online system to maintain a safe gap during the period of Kovid 19.
The main objectives of this conference are to: (1) discuss and understand the ways in which the governments of ASEAN Member States and Korea should respond to the spread of Kovid 19; (2) identify challenges and opportunities for Develop the country in the aftermath of the Kovid 19 crisis, and (3) continue to strengthen economic and political cooperation between ASEAN member countries as well as Korea to promote mutual economic growth.
