The Deputy Prosecutor and the Officer in Charge of Bailiff's Affairs presided over the Joint Commission and had the Greffiers read out the Supreme Court Judgment No. 84 of 31 March 1998 in full for the creditors of the practice and the debtors. Of the implementation, as well as a joint committee to hear the contents of this letter.
While enforcing enforcement, adherence positions and concessions remain in place to avoid coercion, and as a result, the debtors' spouses agreed to the practice by accepting a 24-meter-wide frontage. , The back size is 27 meters and the length of the north side is 42 meters, the size of the south side is 50 meters, keeping the house unaltered.
The Joint Commission, under the coordination of the Deputy Prosecutor, under the direction of the Governor, the Provincial Unity Command and the Prosecutor, instructed the parties (creditors and debtors to implement) to erect fence posts, demarcate the territory and hand over the land to the debtors. Of performance and creditors of performance.
Finally, the Joint Commission headed by Mr. Touch Udom decided to hand over the land of the implementation site to the creditors of the implementation, Nin Chentra, the son of Nin Ton, and to the debtor, Muth Im, and his wife, Pheng Chanphon. For the part of the land which the wife of the debtor of the agreement agrees to and there is a concession from the creditor of the practice.
(Prey Veng): A traffic accident occurred on the afternoon of February 25, 2021, when three cars collided, causing two vehicles to explode completely and three people were seriously injured in Prey Veng City, Prey Veng Province. .
Prey Veng City Police Inspector said that before the incident, three vehicles were driving in the opposite direction from north to south. Two vehicles were almost completely damaged and three people were injured, two with broken legs and one with full body pain.
According to the inspector, after the incident, the competent authorities intervened to put out the fire. As for the identities of the victims, the authorities are searching and sending them to the hospital for emergency treatment, while the three vehicles have been temporarily stored at the specialized office waiting to be dealt with later.
National Bank of Cambodia urges all banking and financial institutions to implement health measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) has issued a directive to the Director General, Managing Director, Director and Director of all banking and financial institutions to strengthen the implementation of measures to participate in preventing the spread of Kovid 19 in the community event on 20 February.
