(Rattanakiri): The Rattanakiri Provincial Health Department on the morning of February 25, 2021, opened a training course on Kovid-19 vaccination campaign for health officers and the National Police Force of Rattanakiri Provincial Police.
The training for Ratanakkiri Provincial Health Officers was conducted in the presence of Dr. Ong Ratana, Advisor to the Ministry of Health and Director of the Provincial Health Department, and attended by Dr. Hing Phan Sokunthea, Director of the Provincial Referral Hospital, Dr. Eng Kun Vuth, Director Office of Infectious Disease Control and Prevention, Mr. Ou Deth, Director of Vaccination Program, as well as 30 doctors.
Dr. Ung Ratana said that the Ratanakkiri Provincial Health Department received 3,600 doses of Kovid-19 vaccine under the auspices of the Ministry of Health to prepare Kovid-19 vaccine for health officials and the National Police Force of the Police Commission. All Ratanakkiri provinces.
The Kovid-19 vaccine is given from 18 to 59 years of age and is voluntary, the doctor said.
According to Mr. Ou Deth, Director of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Vaccination Program, the first phase of the Kovid-19 vaccination will start on March 1, 2021 at the Provincial Referral Hospital and the Bor Keo Referral Hospital.
He said 520 health officials and 1,300 national police officers of the provincial police commission would be vaccinated against Kovid-19, and those who were vaccinated for the first time 20 days after the second vaccination. . In particular, people have not yet been vaccinated against Kovid-19.
