Xi Jinping: "China has achieved complete success in eradicating poverty"
Xi Jinping, secretary-general of the CPC Central Committee and chairman of the Central Military Commission, has announced that poverty has been eradicated from the world's most populous country. The announcement came as Xi was addressing a major conference in Beijing to mark the nation's achievements in reducing poverty.
In the last eight years, the last 98.99 million poor people living in rural areas have been removed from the poverty list by the beginning of 2021, while 832 poor districts and 128,000 poor villages Also removed from the list of poverty.
China contributed more than 70 percent of global poverty reduction over the same period. With these achievements, China has created a "miracle" that will go down in history. According to data, by 2020, China will have a total population of more than 1.439 million.
