(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate of the Prime Minister, Delegate of the Royal Government in charge of the General Department of the General Department of Taxation, on February 25, 2021, explained the tax obligations for community-based humanitarian organizations in Cambodia.
The Minister stated that the income-generating activities of organizations and associations must be obliged to pay taxes to the state, but for the income-generating activities of organizations and associations that provide purely humanitarian activities, the income tax is exempted by the state, but other taxes The other is usually paid to the state.
Mr. Kong Vibol stated that "activities that earn a living and earn absolute profits must be obliged to pay taxes to the state, even if registered as a non-governmental organization is obliged."
This was confirmed by Mr. Kong Vibol in the live program on the official page of the General Department of Taxation on "Introduction of the online income tax return management system and the latest events of the General Department of Taxation" On February 25, 2021.
