Cambodia, Philippines vow to strengthen cooperation in employment and vocational training in both bilateral and ASEAN frameworks
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and the Philippines are committed to further strengthening and expanding cooperation in the field of employment and vocational training, both within the bilateral framework and within the ASEAN framework.
Through this agreement or joint statement, the two sides agreed to assist each other when Filipino citizens or troubled Cambodians in other countries do not have embassies and sub-commissions to provide assistance. Supporting any of them, Cambodians can seek help from the Philippine Embassy in that country, which has worked well together in the past on this cooperation.
The ambassador said that nearly 5,000 Filipinos living and working in Cambodia enjoy the same rights and benefits as Cambodian workers, especially through the National Social Security Fund.
Recently, about 800 Filipinos, with the support of the Royal Government of Cambodia, repatriated safely in the wake of the Kovid 19 pandemic.
In addition, the two countries also have another cooperation in the field of social security through a memorandum of understanding between the National Social Security Fund (NSSF) and the Health Insurance Organization of the Philippines (Philhealth) as a framework for operation. In collaboration, share experiences, especially on technical, operational and financial system management in providing protection to workers.
The two sides will continue to review the expansion of existing cooperation under the Memorandum of Understanding, which has expired and is preparing to renew it.
Because the Philippines is a highly experienced country, there are many Filipinos working abroad who can share a lot of knowledge and experience in providing support to migrant workers.
