(Koh Kong): Koh Kong Governor Mithona Phuthong has ordered police, soldiers and relevant officials stationed along the Thai-Cambodian border to step up their efforts to find and crack down on smugglers. Cambodian workers cross the border illegally into Thailand.
Koh Kong provincial governor issued such strict orders as brokers continue their activities to smuggle Cambodian migrant workers at risk to Thailand as Thailand is in the throes of a crisis. In the community and so on.
The order was made on the afternoon of February 24, 2021, during a visit to the 827th and 199th Border Guard Battalions guarding the Cambodian-Thai border line in Mondul Seima district.
The Governor of Koh Kong Province ordered: "The police force stationed at the natural channel must take a strong position on the migrant workers who smuggle back into the country through the natural channel to avoid the transmission of Kovid-19 disease. It is a global communicable disease. Therefore, if any migrant workers pass through the natural channel, they must be detained for questioning and sent to the health officer for a 14-day biopsy test, ”he said.
The provincial governor continued, "All authorities stationed at each checkpoint, if there are migrant workers at their checkpoints, must detain migrant workers returning home or smuggling workers into Thailand. The brokers who bring all the workers to see for the authorities to take action according to legal procedures.
On the occasion of inspecting the situation and strengthening the capacity of the police force of the 827th Border Police Brigade and the mainland border police post (199), she also brought food, equipment to prevent communicable disease-19, medicine and some money to the police force. .
