Ministry of Foreign Affairs: Cambodia-South Korea Legal Aid Treaty to enter into force tomorrow
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation said that the treaty on legal aid in the field of criminal law between Cambodia and South Korea will enter into force on February 24, 2021 tomorrow. This. This is according to the letter of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs sent to the Ministry of Justice, and the Ministry of Justice presented on February 23, 2021, which was received by Fresh News.
According to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the Korean side provided information related to the completion of internal procedures for the entry into force of the Cambodia-Korea Criminal Assistance Treaty signed last year. November 25, 2019 in Busan, Republic of Korea. Pursuant to Article 25, the above Treaty shall enter into force on 24 February 2021, 30 days after receiving the final written notification through diplomatic channels.
It should be noted that His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, has issued a Royal Decree promulgating the Law on the Approval of the Treaty on Mutual Legal Aid in the Criminal Field between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Republic of Cambodia. Korea (South Korea) on November 14, 2020.
The Draft Law on Mutual Legal Aid in the Criminal Sector aims to define the legal mutual assistance in the criminal field between the Kingdom of Cambodia and foreign states in relation to criminal proceedings. And freezing, seizing and confiscating assets in order to strengthen and expand international cooperation.
This law applies to:
* Legal assistance in the field of criminal affairs shall be provided to all requesting States, even if the requested State does not have an agreement with the Kingdom of Cambodia.
* Seeking legal assistance in the field of criminal justice from all recipient states, even if the recipient state does not have an agreement with the Kingdom of Cambodia. This law does not apply to legal mutual assistance in the criminal field in accordance with bilateral or multilateral treaties or conventions ratified by the Kingdom of Cambodia.
