(Phnom Penh): The entrance exam for the Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport will close on February 28 this weekend. Candidates who wish to study and win 100% free scholarships, please hurry to apply.
Please note that Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport needs to recruit 200 first generation students. The top 50 students will receive 100% scholarships for four years of study.
In addition, female students will receive an incentive of 50% scholarships for four years of study.
The entrance exam will be held online on March 3, 2021. Subjects to be tested include: Mathematics, Physics and Chemistry. To take the exam at this institute, candidates must have a high school diploma or equivalent.
The Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport, established by the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, is another new achievement for the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, in developing human resources on the skills of building roads, bridges and ports.
Creating human resources is the first political priority for the Royal Government of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Samdech Techo expressed his pleasure at the efforts to establish this institute. Samdech Techo expects that the institute will create new human resources on the skills of building infrastructure, roads, bridges as well as ports.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that his expectation after the establishment of this institute is that in the next four to five years, Cambodia will have more Cambodian engineers to build their own roads and bridges.
The Ministry of Public Works and Transport, in collaboration with the Institute of Technology of Cambodia (Techno), trains students to ensure the quality and effectiveness of education. In addition, the institute has gathered professional professors to train and equip modern technology systems to provide knowledge to students. The institute has set up equipment, laboratories and laboratories in the field of bridges and roads to provide a better understanding of students.
The institute will train undergraduate +1 (engineers) for 5 years, Bachelor of Road Transport for 4 years, Bachelor of Logistics for 4 years and Bachelor of Navigation for 4 years.
Bachelor of Road Transport, majoring in Economics and Land Transport Management.
Bachelor's degree in Logistics, majoring in Logistics and Supply Chain Management.
Bachelor's degree in Navigation, majoring in Ship Management and Ship Engine.
For students studying at Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport after graduation will be a priority in the entrance exam of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. During the study period, students can visit the construction sites that are building roads across the country by the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, as well as companies.
In addition, students can do internships at companies or units under the Ministry that are building roads and projects in the field of public works and transportation. Students also have the opportunity to receive scholarships to study abroad.
Candidates interested in studying at this institute, please contact 096 933 4253 or 095 404 590. Candidates can also contact the Institute directly under the Ministry of Public Works and Transport on Street 598 (Chea Sophara Street), Sangkat Chrang Chamres 2, Khan Russey Keo. Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivers a message on the occasion of the 9th National Clean City Day under the theme "New habits for a clean city"
