Mithona Phu Thong Appointed King of Koh Kong for New Mandate
(Phnom Penh): The King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, has ordered the appointment of Mithona Phuthong as Governor of Koh Kong Province for a new term.
The Royal Decree appointing was made on February 5, 2021. In the Royal Decree obtained by Fresh News on February 23, 2021, it was also stated that the appointment of Ms. Mithona Phu Thong as the new Governor of Koh Kong Province was also addressed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
It should be noted that Ms. Mithona Phuthong, 40 years old, was appointed by the King to be the Governor of Koh Kong Province for the first time at the request of Samdech Techo during June 2017.
She is also the first and youngest female provincial governor in Cambodia. Mithona Phuthong is the eldest daughter of Yuth Phuthong and the granddaughter of Say Phouthong, the leader of the Southwestern resistance movement. She is married to a naval police officer and has two sons.
Mithona Phuthong told Fresh News that she has a bachelor's degree in information technology and a master's degree in law. She joined the civil service in 2009.
She recalled that after graduating, she worked for a private company and did not intend to work as an official because her father feared that his daughter would not be able to serve the society.
However, in her first term as Governor of Koh Kong Province for the past four years, Mithona Phu Thong overcame many obstacles and difficulties in leading this remote province and highlighted many achievements in the province. .
In an interview with Fresh News, Ms. Mithona Phuthong expressed her gratitude to the King of Cambodia and Samdech Techo Hun Sen for their trust and confidence in giving her the opportunity to serve the Royal Government, the Royal Government and the people of the province. Koh Kong in the new mandate.
The young provincial governor expressed her determination to work hard to achieve new work and achievements for the Royal Government, the nation and the people of Koh Kong province.
