Cambodian Entrepreneurs and Cambodian Agriculture Sustainability Partnership jointly promote agro-industry through new business training programs for entrepreneurs in the farming community
(Phnom Penh): Cambodian Entrepreneurs, an institution under the Ministry of Economy and Finance with the vision of becoming a national nursery for the promotion of all activities of the Cambodian Entrepreneurship and Partnership for Agricultural Sustainability (CPSA), a multilateral partnership forum. Participated in partnerships to promote entrepreneurship in agriculture.
The two sides agreed on the process of promoting innovation, adaptation to new technologies, production solutions, skills development, linking educational and industrial institutions and entrepreneurship in agriculture, as well as exchanging information and data related to agriculture. In order to create support mechanisms.
Dr. Chheang Vann Monin, Executive Director of Cambodian Entrepreneurship, said that according to the "Status and Vision of the Cambodian Economy" presented by the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the agricultural sector is estimated to have a positive growth rate of about 0.5% by 2020 during When Kovid-19, while other sectors such as industry and services were estimated to have negative growth.
"In this new context, we expect that increasing innovation and business skills in the community can help boost the agricultural sector to its full potential." The Agricultural Community Entrepreneurship Innovation Program is designed to meet the above needs by promoting entrepreneurship for young people and students at the university, expanding the capacity of agricultural communities and farmers, and increasing innovation in the agricultural value chain.
"If agriculture in rural areas shows economic attractiveness, young people, women and men will benefit from on-the-job employment, that is, will not be forced to migrate to find employment opportunities away from their communities," he explained.
The project will connect with stakeholders such as universities, farmers, agribusiness, government agencies and civil society organizations. Cambodian entrepreneurs and partner organizations for the sustainability of Cambodia's agricultural sector welcome other partners to support the implementation of this project.
