General Yon Min, Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense, said that the construction and renovation of the Veterans' Cemetery is more than 9,500 square meters in Village 3, Sangkat Smach Meanchey, Khemarak Phoumin City, Koh Kong Province. The cemetery has a coffin, a grave for each warrior, a funeral home, a charitable name and a parking lot.
"During the war, officers and soldiers sacrificed a lot of lives to protect the country, so as to pay tribute to and respect the souls of the brave warriors who dared to sacrifice their lives," said General Min.
The General continued that the implementation of the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia and the implementation under the guidance of Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, will build this area to be suitable and become a transport zone. Concerns: Veterans' corpses.
