Mrs. Men Sam An Inaugurates the Ancient Temple of Kandal, Srah Srang and Ancient Waterfall in Angkor Resort
(Siem Reap): Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, High Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister, and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, presided over the inauguration ceremony of the temple. Ancient Srah Srang and ancient water exercises in the Angkor resort on the morning of Monday, the 11th of Phalkun, the year of Chuot Tosak, B.E. 2564 is on February 22, 2021.
In particular, the large swimming pool, 18 meters long, 12 meters high, 11.6 meters in diameter, was renovated by experts of the APSARA Authority, preserving the entire traditional style and incorporating modern architecture to ensure the Originality and robustness ensure long-term use for the public good.
This large swimming pool has a history dating back to the 1960s and was built during the Sangkum Reastr Niyum era, accompanied by a luxury house nearby. However, due to the war during the Khmer Rouge era, this exercise was almost completely destroyed. In the late 1980s, the Siem Reap Provincial Forestry Administration rebuilt the dam, but there was no house as before to draw water from the Siem Reap River to irrigate the saplings in the Takeo Nursery.
As for the budget for the renovation, it was supported by Mrs. Oknha Moha Upasika, Honorary Doctor Dr. Seang Chanheng, General Director of Heng Aphivath Company, through the Dharma of Dr. Tat Mahathy, Chief Inspector of Wat Preah Indakosa, with the support of The head of the Royal Government, through the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, the Apsara National Authority, which spent more than 600,000 US dollars, including the repair of the Takao gate.
