(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ken Sambath, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Taxation, represented by Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Taxation on 22 February 2021. Chaired a seminar on "Capital Gains Tax".
Also present were Mr. Khem Tola, Director of the Department of Taxation of Real Estate and Real Estate, Deputy Director of the Central Department, as well as tax officials, a total of 70 participants in this workshop, implementing safety principles in accordance with Ministry of Health guidelines to prevent the transmission of Kovid-19 virus.
The workshop consisted of two presentations, “Presentation on Capital Gains Taxes of Some Countries and the Case of Cambodia” and a presentation on “Capital Gains Taxes” presented by two speakers, Mr. Chey Rithy. Deputy Director of the Department and Mrs. Dy Chanthy, Director of the Second Capital Income Tax Office of the Department of Real Estate Tax.
For the calculation of tax on capital gain is the profit from the sale or transfer of capital multiplied by the tax rate of 20%, and for capital as real estate, the property owner can choose the method of deducting expenses. Expenditures account for 80% of the proceeds from the sale or transfer of real estate;
In addition, the Royal Government has decided to waive the tax on capital gains on the sale or transfer of agricultural land owned or occupied by people who are farmers who are actually growing crops and have a residence in the commune / sangkat where the agricultural land is located. .
