The dedication ceremony for the 447 veterans was held for two days on February 22-23, 2021 at the Koh Kong Provincial Veterans 'Tomb (Veterans' Cemetery) in Village 3, Sangkat Smach Meanchey, Khemarak Phoumin City, Koh Kong Province.
General Yon Min, Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense and Chairman of the Construction Commission, said that the construction and repair of the Veterans' Cemetery covers an area of more than 9,500 square meters in Village 3, Sangkat Smach Meanchey, Khemarak Phoumin City, Koh Kong Province.
According to General Yon Min, the construction and renovation of the Veterans Tomb is now in retaliation for the veterans who sacrificed their lives during the war to defend their homeland and Protect the lives of the people to bring peace to the nation and the people, regardless of the sacrifice of their lives.
"During the war, officers and soldiers sacrificed their lives to protect the nation, so as to pay tribute to and respect the souls of the brave warriors who dared to sacrifice their lives," said General Min.
