The meeting was attended in person and online by more than 300 delegates from 80 countries, as well as political parties, civil society organizations, journalists and local and global think tanks. 200 people.
Tep Ngorn made a keynote speech, highlighting that Kovid-19 has been a serious threat to the economy, well-being and millions of lives around the world. In this regard, he encouraged all countries to continue to prioritize the lives, safety and health of the people and promote global solidarity in response to the spread of Kovid-19 in the vision of building a global health community. For all and equal.
According to Tep Ngorn, poverty is a major obstacle to achieving human rights. The interests of the people should be considered as the most important task and development should provide greater benefits to all people with equity.
He stressed that there is no one-size-fits-all model for the protection and improvement of the human rights situation. Diversity in the path of human rights development should be respected, and any attempt to take human rights issues as a political issue, implement two standards or use human rights reasons to interfere in the internal affairs of other countries. Deny.
He encouraged the joint efforts of all parties, based on the principles of respect for sovereignty and non-interference in the internal affairs of other states, to promote the establishment of a global governance on human rights that is equitable, fair, environmental and comprehensive. Than before.
"Today's meeting has provided us with a comprehensive and in-depth understanding of China's policy on ethnic groups and the development of ethnic minority areas," he added. There is a lot of living, including the real situation in Xinjiang, where the economy, social stability, equality and solidarity among different ethnic groups, and the living standards of the people are constantly improving.
He praised the work done by the Chinese government to promote the economic and social development of ethnic minority groups and areas with a large population and protect all their rights to freedom of religion. Religions will be able to use their own language and oppose the behavior of a small number of people and some countries who have incited, distorted facts and fabricated rumors to mislead the international community on the situation in Xinjiang.
Tep Ngorn added that Cambodia supports the fight against terrorism and supports any measures that guarantee sovereignty, social order, national security and development. Cambodia adheres to the "One China Policy" and considers the Taiwan, Hong Kong, Tibet and Xinjiang internal affairs of the People's Republic of China.
At the end, the meeting approved the adoption of a joint statement on "The Story of the Communist Party of China: A Summary of the Problems in Xinjiang." Cambodian Facebook Activist President and 11 Associates Appointed as Civil Society Outreach and Communication Team
