* First: All pregnant women should go for a health check-up, consult with a doctor / midwife at a health center or hospital near your home 4 times regularly according to the time and advice of the doctor to accept the service. Prevent all treatments, especially voluntary blood tests for HIV / syphilis to jointly eliminate mother-to-child transmission.
* Second: Go to give birth at a health center or hospital with a well-trained midwife.
* Third: Go for health check-up after delivery, both mother and baby, take the baby to get 11 vaccines on time, monitor the health and growth of the baby until the baby is 2 years old.
* 5th: Take the baby to the hospital immediately when you see any danger signs of respiratory disease, diarrhea or other diseases and take the baby or young child who is thin or does not gain weight at all to consult and receive. Hospital treatment.
