(Phnom Penh): 19 Kovid disease that has plagued Cambodia since 2020 has caused a serious crisis to the national economy and people's livelihood.
Seafood wholesalers at O'Pour Port, Khemarak Phoumin commune, Khemarak Phoumin city, Koh Kong province, were also affected and lost tens of thousands of dollars.
Ms. Kong Touch confirmed that there were many seafood that she collected from the fishermen, but Moy did not buy them, so she threw the rest and gave it to the fish to eat.
According to the seafood wholesaler, throughout 2020, he will lose about $ 100,000 due to some scams and no money for seafood.
After nearly a year of deteriorating conditions, seafood sales have improved slightly between December 2020 and January 2021, after the situation of Kovid 19 has calmed down. Especially after the cafeteria and wedding reopened.
But the sales situation is back to normal after the announcement of the 19 cases of Kovid infection in the community on February 20, 2021.
Ms. Kong Touch said that two days after the announcement of the 19 new Kovid outbreak in the community, she had about 1 ton of seafood left due to the cancellation of the order.
Despite the hardships, seafood wholesalers in Koh Kong province, including Kong Touch, continue to buy seafood from fishermen. This purchase is due to the small number of orders as well as the sale to tourists.
On the other hand, this trade to support the livelihood of seafood fishermen as well.
Ms. Kong Touch appealed to tourists to visit Koh Kong to help buy their seafood. She claims that their fresh seafood does not contain chemicals and the price is reasonable.
