(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, stated that in order to encourage more female students to study engineering and road and bridge construction, in the past, only students were trained in this field. For boys, Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport will offer a 50% discount when female students come to enroll.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol stated this this morning, February 21, 2021, on the occasion of presiding over the Orientation Program on Education and Employment at Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport, which was held at the Ministry. The participation of relevant officials and more than 500 students.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said, "All female students, as long as they are women, we offer a 50% discount because I want to encourage female engineers, not just men to build bridges." "Women can also build, so to encourage our Cambodian women to become engineers, we will reduce the price by 50 percent for everyone."
Eligibility: Applicants must have a high school diploma or equivalent. Applicants may provide a transcript at a later date. 100% scholarship for 50 outstanding students for 4 years (5 years for engineers) and to evaluate the results of each year Tuition fee: $ 600 per year.
Kampong Popil Market in Pearang District, which was burnt down, buried a two-story foundation stone, General Vong Pisen called on the people to join in protecting and preventing Kovid
(Prey Veng): General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF), Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group visited Pearang District on the morning of February 21, 2021, presided over a groundbreaking ceremony and groundbreaking ceremony for the reconstruction of Kampong Popil Market. Also present at the occasion were His Excellency Chea Somethy, Governor of Prey Veng Province, as well as several Pearang District Field Team.
