(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kao Thach, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Rural Development Bank for Agriculture and Rural Development (ARDB), said that Cambodia is currently in need of agricultural experts, focusing on seed breeding and seed production experts. Other to distribute to farmers to farm.
He stressed that this skill should be available, especially the private sector investment, because now farmers are facing the wrong selection of seeds, growing yields and so on.
Mr. Kao Thach added, "Farmers still have problems in selecting seeds, importing seeds from abroad, do not know that these seeds are grown to benefit. Currently, Cambodia is short of breeders for sale, which means that if farmers go to buy seedlings or seeds from seed farms for sale, they will benefit, because those who grow seeds for sale are experts in seed and seed production. And so on. ”
"Currently, Cambodia has a large shortage of vegetable and fruit growers, while some countries, such as Thailand, have this expertise, and obviously, like fragrant coconuts, whoever imports fragrant coconuts from Thailand and Vietnam," he said. "While Cambodia does not yet have industrial cultivation, this is a skill that Cambodia must have to help farmers. I hope the private sector will see this and start investing."
He added that this skill is indispensable because it helps farmers to grow the agricultural sector in Cambodia, and if there is more participation from the private sector, the agricultural sector will be strong, but growing and stable. .
In addition, he also asked people who are farmers engaged in subsistence farming to change their mindset from farming to meet their own needs, but to turn agriculture into a business that can buy and sell for profit because Doing so will not only improve living standards but also contribute to poverty reduction.
