(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kao Thach, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Rural Development Bank for Agriculture and Rural Development (ARDB), requested the people who are farmers engaged in subsistence farming to change their mindset from farming to meet their own needs. But to turn agriculture into a business that can buy and sell for profit, because this not only improves living standards, but also contributes to reducing poverty.
Mr. Kao Thach said, "Farmers should change their mindset from farming for their own needs and the rest should be sold. Farmers should turn to production, think about doing business, buy and sell for profit to improve their lives and Reduce poverty.
He added, however, that in order for farming to become a business, farmers need to understand more about how to grow crops in accordance with the standard, not to cultivate in parallel.
He said that currently the main problem is facing the farmers to cultivate in accordance with the standards, especially the standard of sanitation, good practices in agriculture.
He said that all farmers need to change this mindset, start specializing, work together, produce groups and set up planting plans to ensure a stable harvest. On the other hand, farmers should specialize, which means that when in the village "A" grow this type of vegetable in the village "B" should not grow the same vegetables so as not to have oversupply in the market. Lower prices.
He said that apart from the problem of overlapping cultivation, farmers also have problems in selecting seeds, importing seeds from abroad, do not know that these seeds are planted to benefit. Currently, Cambodia is short of breeders for sale, which means that if farmers go to buy seedlings or seeds from seed farms for sale, they will benefit, because those who grow seeds for sale are experts in seed and seed production. And so on.
