Mr. Un Chanda stated that the Royal Government, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister, has made our country grow steadily, so while the country is at peace with this progress, our youth group can have Opportunity to study hard to strengthen their ability to be worthy of succession, as the old saying goes, "bamboo vine."
He added that while the country is at peace, it is an opportunity to strengthen human resources. The next priority is to build roads to facilitate people to travel and transport other agricultural products, and the next pole has water and electricity.
However, at present, one of the four priorities is to build human resources, that is, to organize training for young people to take turns, because the country is still developing, so there must be Provide successors with real ability to participate in the development of our country to grow. Senior Minister Sun Chanthol Continues to Lead a Cycling Technical Team to Inspect National Road 21, Koh Thom District, Kandal Province
(Kandal): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, this morning, February 20, 2021, continued to lead the technical team of the Ministry of Cycling to inspect the quality of the construction of National Road No. 21 from Koh Thom District Stadium to the village. Chrey Thom, Sampov Poun Commune (Vietnam border) is located in Koh Thom District, Kandal Province.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also inspected the construction of a concrete wall to protect the canal bank at border post No. 246 in Chrey Thom village, Sampov Poun commune (Vietnam border), implemented by the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kandal Province. To prevent and protect the border posts, which are historical structures, from collapsing into canals, as well as to protect against changes in territorial integrity and national sovereignty.
Please be informed that: National Road No. 21 with a total length of 63.6 km (from Takhmao to Chrey Thom) was opened for improvement on March 28, 2016 and completed in October. 2017 ago under a loan from the Government of the Republic of Korea and a contribution from the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Senior official of the Ministry of Health: General pediatric diseases decline in the context of Kovid-19 because parents pay high attention to care for young children
(Phnom Penh): Professor Yit Sunnara, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Health and President of the Cambodian Pediatric Association, confirmed that general pediatric diseases, especially infectious diseases, have dropped significantly in the context of Kovid-19 due to the care of parents. Highly cared for young children and have better hand washing, wearing a mask as well as better personal hygiene.
This statement was made by Professor Yit Sunnara on the morning of February 20, 2021, on the 23rd Pediatric Day, with the participation of the President of the Cambodian Pediatric Association, as well as the professors, doctors and doctors who are members of the association. 150 Cambodian pediatricians and 250 online doctors.
"Prevention of various respiratory infections due to the same preventive measures as Kovid, we see a significant reduction in pediatric diseases, and when free travel reduces restrictions, we see that children are more susceptible to re-infection," he said. "Children are starting to get sick again."
The President of the Cambodian Pediatric Association said that in terms of percentage for the National Children's Hospital and Kantha Bopha Hospital, there was a 30 to 40 percent reduction in the general disease of children in the context of Kovid, which is a significant decrease. Note.
At the same time, Professor Yit Sunnara said that despite this decrease, parents must continue to protect children, implement proper hygiene measures, wear masks, wash hands and be careful for children's food. As Kovid 19, there has been a decrease or disappearance because when strict measures reach the closure of pediatric schools, the number of pediatric cases starts to increase.
"Through Kovid, people are afraid that there will be less gatherings and keep washing their hands and wearing masks. There is a decrease in the number of children in the children's hospital. Breathing is the same as hand and foot hygiene. ” This is the additional confirmation of Professor Yit Sunnara.
He also said that through careful and decisive action by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Cambodia has 19 fewer cases of Kovid in ASEAN in the world and the death toll. There is none.
"In 2020, we had 19 new outbreaks of Kovid, so when there was an outbreak during the outbreak, we thought the number of patients coming out of the hospital was declining," he said. "It could be for two reasons."
