In addition to Prayuth, nine other Thai ministers also escaped the vote of no-confidence. This is the second time that Prayuth and his minister have escaped a no-confidence vote in the National Assembly since he took office in July 2019. In February 2019, the Prime Minister and five other ministers easily won the no-confidence vote.
Of the 487 lawmakers, 277 were from Prayuth's ruling coalition and 210 from the opposition. To withdraw the trust of the Prime Minister or the Minister of the National Assembly requires a simple majority vote or 244 votes. However, in Saturday's election, Mr. Prayuth received 272 to 206 votes of no-confidence, while the other three abstained.
Rhinoceros dies after being trapped in forest in Preah Vihear province
(Preah Vihear): A rare species of wild rattlesnake was found dead by a park official in a forest in Sen Rong Roeung Bei village, Moratok commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province, due to being trapped by a wild hunter.
According to the report of the Bizarre officials, on the afternoon of February 19, 2021, the park rangers at the 91st Mobile Headquarters patrolled the Otam Ek spot and found a raccoon lying dead due to a hunter's trap. .
According to the report, the dead wild raccoon, which weighed about 1 ton, was trapped in its right leg and slept for about one night and one day. Oh, Kak.
On February 20, 2021, Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, confirmed to Fresh News that on behalf of Minister Say Sam Al and The ministry and the people are saddened by the loss of the raccoon. Rhinoceros, a rare species in the world.
The senior official said that by 2020, nearly 50,000 traps had been removed by rangers from protected areas across the country. Traps are hidden killers who have killed countless Cambodian wildlife.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that according to the study report, the population of raccoons in Cambodia is between 2,700 to 5,700. This makes Cambodia the most populous country in the world, with the total number of leopards in the world being estimated at between 5,900 and 11,000. Thailand and Indonesia also have only a few hundred raccoons.
The spokesman for the Ministry of Environment said that the raccoon is an endangered species in the world and Cambodia is proud that all people must participate in the protection and conservation of wildlife by saying no to Wildlife trafficking, eating wildlife meat and not hunting and trapping wild animals.
After removing the carcass from the forest on the morning of February 20, environmental officials organized a ceremony for the monks to give birth to a raccoon that died from the trap. The raccoon was buried at the Chong Environmental Office in O'Kak village, Po commune, Tbeng Meanchey district, Preah Vihear province.
