Ministry of Tourism Presents Tourism Safety Labels and Certificates of Appreciation to 8 Local Tourists After Participating in the Implementation of Affordable Tour Package Project
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism on February 19, 2021 handed over tourism safety labels and certificates to local tour operators, hotels and restaurants, a total of 8 companies that have volunteered to participate in the implementation of affordable tour packages and implemented correctly. According to tourism safety rules.
The awarding ceremony was presided over by Mr. Nep Samuth, Director General of the General Department of Tourism Industry Management, and was attended by local tour operators, hotels and restaurants, as part of a volunteer business with the Ministry of Tourism. Affordable tour packages and properly implemented tourism safety rules.
Mr. Nep Samuth stated that the affordable tour package is organized according to the concept of "Patriotism, Know the Territory" and the mechanism to facilitate people's travel easily, safely and affordably to various destinations in Cambodia. .
He added that in addition to promoting new tourist destinations, the Ministry of Tourism has cooperated with local tour operators to organize attractive, competitive and competitive tour packages, enabling tourists to visit more places. Appropriate and safe.
Mr. Chhun Makara, Director of the Department of Management of Transport Agencies and Tour Guides, said that through the past practice, an average of 400-500 tourists per month traveled on this package, and this number could reach 700-800 in One month during long holidays or national holidays.
Mr. Nep Samuth, Director General of the Ministry of Tourism, emphasized that the Ministry of Tourism will continue to implement the program to distribute certificates of appreciation for the efforts of the tourism business on the promotion of internal tourism movement, the implementation of tourism safety measures and participation in discounted services. Provide the safest, most attractive and affordable travel in the "live together" cause.
Cambodia sends 204 shifts to Central Africa
(Phnom Penh): 204 Engineering Forces No. 576, including 15 women, which is a shift force, on the evening of February 19, 2021, went out to carry out humanitarian missions in the Central African Republic under the United Nations umbrella. .
The 204th Engineer Brigade 576 of the National Center for Peacekeeping and Mine Action and Demining (Blue Hat Soldiers) left Phnom Penh International Airport at 11:45 tonight.
The deployment of the 576th Engineer Peacekeeping Force will continue to build horizontal and vertical structures in the UN-designated mission area.
By the time the 576th Engineer Corps arrives in the Central African Republic, 204 brigades, including 10 women, have completed 10 UN peacekeeping missions in the Central African Republic. One year ago, he will return to Cambodia on February 21, 2020, and will be required to stay 14 days in advance and be allowed to visit his family.
For 204 members of the 495th Engineering Corps, including 10 women, who completed 14 days of missionary work in the Central African Republic, all were healthy and free of Kovid-19 infection.
It should be noted that since 2006, Cambodia has sent a total of 7,517 troops, including 466 women to participate in UN missions, while Cambodia currently has about 1,000 troops on mission. In five countries: Sudan, the Republic of South Sudan, Central Africa, Lebanon and Mali.
Through the work of the Cambodian Blue Hat Force, which participates in all these humanitarian missions, Cambodia has become the largest donor of peacekeeping forces in ASEAN.
