Ministry of Transport Says Awareness of Traffic Laws Really Important in Preventing Traffic Accidents in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) emphasized that mainstreaming traffic laws to people from all walks of life is very important in preventing traffic accidents in Cambodia.
Mr. Pen Boran, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Public Works and Transport and Deputy Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the National Road Safety Committee, spoke at a training workshop on road traffic officers on the morning of February 19, 2021 at the Ministry. That awareness of traffic laws to everyone is very good to participate in preventing traffic accidents in Cambodia.
"The law is a habit, so if you all obey the law in society, it will be smooth," he said. After all, without law, there would be anarchy. "For example, if one is on the left and the other is on the right, it will definitely turn into an anarchy."
At the same time, the Undersecretary of State also said that the problem that arose in 2019, the problem of traffic accidents caused by speed and disregard for priority rights, but for 2020, the most prominent problem is disregard for priority rights that As a solution point.
"Today we look at the issue of non-compliance with priorities, study in depth and address this issue," he said. "So we, as trainers, have to learn from the speakers who present the road traffic rules."
He added that the priority rights set out in the law are very important because it gives each vehicle rights. On the other hand, those who do not respect the law will be able to cause accidents.
Mr. Pen Boran also mentioned that the trainees who come to study today will be both learners and lecturers will be experts in traffic law.
Mr. Prum Vantha, Director of the Department of Road Safety, said that the officers who attended today's training course is very important to take the knowledge to train others. On the other hand, if there is misinformation or misinterpretation, it will be difficult because the inquirer will always take the interpretation to study or debate.
Please be informed that the training course on road traffic law was held in order to strengthen the capacity of traffic law to the officials of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport as trainers to educate and disseminate to the people who are road users.
(Phnom Penh): Lawyer Ly Chantola, President of the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia, stated that as a volunteer lawyer, he must not defend his client in order to fulfill his duties, but must fulfill his duties in accordance with the professional ethics. The law stipulates that a small number of lawyers have already been punished in this case.
During the past 100 days, the Bar Association of Cambodia has assigned volunteer lawyers to help protect the poor in 2,167 cases at all levels, with 3,658 clients, including 312 women and children. 787 people.
Lawyer Ly Chantola added: "Since I took office as the President of the Bar Association, I have met with delegates from all capitals and provinces, so we have advised them when they receive the defense and to protect. "To the fullest, do not do the job, and in the past we have punished the lawyer who did the job."
At the same time, lawyer Ly Chantola said that all lawyers have a professional code of conduct that stipulates that all lawyers must defend their clients carefully, especially to perform their duties to the best of their ability. .
Lawyer Ly Chantola said that in addition to defending and providing legal advice to the poor, the Bar Association has a total of 308 volunteer lawyers representing the poor across the country, although this number is still limited, but the results The team of lawyers who volunteered for 100 days has also received good results.
In order to strengthen the prestige of the legal profession, the President of the Bar Association of Cambodia added that the Bar Association has been cooperating with the Ministry of Interior in arranging for lawyers in the Capital-Provincial Administration in accordance with the Notification No. 1028 Dated 27 November 2020 of the Office of the Council of Ministers on the organization of a group of lawyers for the Capital-Provincial Administration.
