(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kim Santepheap, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Justice, said that the revision of the sub-decree on health measures to prevent and respond to the international spread of the disease at the entrance by increasing the fines for those who do not do so is to prevent the spread. Of Kovid 19 in Cambodia.
His remarks came as some questioned whether the government lacked money or wanted to raise revenue by raising fines. Mr. Kim Sandepheap confirmed this case, "This increase in fines is not to earn money. "The sole purpose of the Royal Government of Cambodia is to prevent the spread of Kovid in the country."
He said this at a press conference on the revision of the sub-decree on health measures to prevent and respond to the international spread of diseases at the gates on February 19 at the Ministry of Health.
The spokesman for the Ministry of Justice also stated that when governments see fines increase, they are afraid because the people do not participate in enforcing the law. So raising fines is not a matter of happiness, it is a matter of concern.
"The Royal Government of Cambodia is adjusting the increase in fines as a measure to prevent crime from escaping or escalating health measures to prevent the spread of 19 diseases," he said.
Please be informed that the Royal Government of Cambodia on February 18, 2021 issued an amendment to this sub-decree to increase the efficiency for the census. In particular, take action against those who do not cooperate in the practice of seduction. The sub-decree decided to increase the level of fines for evaders and conspirators to evade arbitrariness.
Article 8 states that the transitional fine is from 1 million Riel to 5 million Riel for the person who avoids committing acts.
Article 9 states that the transitional fine is from 1 million Riel to 5 million Riel for the person who escapes from the place of work during the process of doing the work.
Article 10 stipulates a transitional fine of 1 million to 5 million riels for individuals who perform sedation without cooperation with health officials to take samples for analysis of Kovid-19 virus. The payment of this transferee does not eliminate the person who has to be vaccinated to have a health officer take a sample to be tested for Kovid-19 virus.
Article 11 states that the transitional fine shall be from 10 million Riels to 50 million Riels for the initiator, leader, guide, instigate, persuade or intentionally facilitate the person who has to perform the ritual to escape the control of the officer or avoid doing so. Chattalysak or escape from Chattalisak.
Article 12 states that the transitional fine is 10 million to 50 million for all private health facilities that help to conceal and do not immediately notify the Ministry of Health in case it is found that patients who are receiving medical services in their institutions. There are indications that the patient is avoiding sedation or is avoiding sedation.
Article 13 states that the fine will be doubled if the offense continues.
It should be noted that the adjustment to increase the level of severe fines for those who do not participate in the censorship came after the Royal Government found that some workers who returned from Thailand evaded the censorship at the border. Such cases have led to the recent removal of the Kamrieng District Inspector of Battambang Province. Vietnam continues to detect "15 new cases" of domestic Kovid-19 infection on Friday
