(Kampong Chhnang): Rev. Lim Chhun and Rev. Chay Kong, who are the parents of Duke Ing Bunhou and Ms. Heng Sokha, and all their children, on the morning of February 19, 2021, celebrated the inauguration ceremony. Completed in 31 pagodas in Kampong Leng district, Choul Kiri district, Kampong Chhnang and Kampong Speu provinces.
The ceremony was held at Wat Ampovan (Wat Thmey Kampong Boeung) in Kampong Boeung village, Kampong Hav commune, Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province, with the participation of Mr. Oknha, Mr. and Mrs. Ponh Kosal through the power of generosity, transparency, respectively.
Mr. Sam Chanthorn, Governor of Kampong Leng District, said that Rev. Lim Chhun and Rev. Chay Kong, as well as their children, have also built achievements in both Buddhism and the Empire for the local society in Kampong Leng, such as:
* For education: Many school buildings were built in Kampong Leng district, including secondary schools, primary schools and kindergartens, and contributed to the construction of school buildings in Kampong Leng district and in Kampong Chhnang district. Well.
* Health and clean water: Help fund the construction of water wells for people in 6 communes in Kampong Leng district for use as clean water.
* Administrative work: Contribute to strengthen the administrative work system to facilitate the improvement of service delivery to the people, provided computers to the district administration, police inspectorate, Hun Sen High School, Kampong Leng, Kampong Boeung Primary School and the Chief Inspector of Wat Ampawan.
* Buddhism: Participated in the construction of temples, halls, iron bricks, gates, dynamos, generators, flagpoles, ponds, schools and achievements in the pagoda and tens of millions of riels.
On behalf of the monks, government officials, commissioners, Buddhist priests and all the people of Kampong Leng, Mr. Sam Chanthorn expressed his deep gratitude to Rev. Lim Chhun and Rev. Chay Kong, as well as their children, and wished them a happy and prosperous life. Appropriately experience happiness, prosperity, and may glory, prosperity, and happiness in all things forever.
Please note that in the inauguration ceremony of these achievements, Rev. Lim Chhun and Rev. Chay Kong, along with their children, contributed 10 tons of cement and an additional $ 3,000 to build in the pagoda.
At the same time, gifts were distributed to Ta Chi, Yai Chi, teachers, students and nearly 500 students, and there was a counting ceremony for 231 monks from pagodas in Kampong Leng district.
