(Phnom Penh): Lawyer Ly Chantola, President of the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia, on February 19, 2021, held a press conference on the achievements of the Bar Association for 100 days under his leadership for the 13th mandate.
It should be noted that Mr. Ly Chantola was elected as the President of the Bar Association of the 13th mandate in the general election organized by the Bar Association on October 16, 2020, with an overwhelming majority of 1444 votes. Approximately 78.65% of all votes cast.
On October 4, 2020, Mr. Ly Chantola, a lawyer, solemnly announced the following eight principles:
Second, strengthen and enhance the capacity of lawyers by increasing training courses, seminars, quoting and exchanging experiences, study tours both in the country and abroad.
Third, strengthen cooperation, value and understanding with national and international institutions, especially with the police, justice, prisons and the judiciary.
Fourth: Increase the dissemination of the role of lawyers and the tasks that lawyers can provide clients.
Fifth, expand the scope of work that lawyers can provide to clients more and against illegal competition by individuals who do not have the right to be a lawyer.
Sixth, establish a mechanism to value and honor lawyers who have made outstanding contributions to assisting the Bar Association, the legal profession, and the work of justice in society.
Seventh, continue to implement and strengthen the welfare mechanism of all lawyers, especially the mechanism related to the fund to help lawyers who are old and seriously ill.
And eighth: to increase the interaction between the Bar Association and all lawyers and to provide better services to all lawyers.
In addition to these eight principles, as President of the Bar Association of Cambodia, Mr. Ly Chantola called on all members of the Bar Association to be more involved as Bar Association Volunteers in legal counseling as well as defense. To poor people and workers who lack the ability to rely on lawyers to defend their legal rights.
In order to contribute to the better service of the social justice sector, the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia has established a policy on free consultation and protection of the poor.
To achieve this policy, the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia needs the voluntary participation of all members of the Bar Association in the process of legal consultation and defense for the poor. Siem Reap Provincial Department of Tourism supports the establishment of a tourism community to contribute to attracting local tourists and creating jobs for local people
