(Phnom Penh): Ms. Pum Chantyny, Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, led a 15-member delegation to visit the "Samdech Mey Library" on the morning of February 19, 2021.
For many years, the Documentation Center of Cambodia has partnered with the Cambodian Red Cross to locate relatives, families of Cambodians lost or displaced by war and genocide. To date, about 230 Khmer Rouge survivors have applied for relatives through the Documentation Center of Cambodia.
Before concluding, the delegation and the team of the Documentation Center of Cambodia discussed some important topics on the promotion of the role and opportunities of women in society. Discussions also focused on current and ongoing projects of the Documentation Center of Cambodia, such as the Khmer Rouge Survivors Health Promotion Project and the Promoting Women's Participation in Remote Communities, as well as future collaboration between institutions. Both.
The visit went smoothly and in a pleasant atmosphere. Finally, Ms. Pum Chantyny, on behalf of the Cambodian Red Cross, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, wrote a memorandum on the book "Samdech Mey Library" with the following contents:
"On behalf of the Cambodian Red Cross delegation visiting the" Samdech Mey Library "today, we all appreciate the rich research initiatives and achievements to make history for the future of Cambodian children. Counting the generations ahead, let's not forget the only dark and bitter past in Cambodia. This is also a lesson for future generations to strive to maintain peace and stability of the country forever.
