Citizens in Cheung Prey, Kang Meas and Batheay Districts Lack Water to Increase Dry Rice Yield
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on the morning of February 19, 2021, led a working group of relevant departments and units to inspect and launch emergency measures to solve the water problem for the people who have grown about 2,000 dry rice crops. Hectares in Sotip commune, Pdao Chum commune, Prey Char commune, Cheung Prey district, Prek Koy commune, Kang Meas district and Chbar Ampov commune, Batheay district to be used and cultivated in the dry season.
Mr. Un Chanda said that after receiving the report from the local authority and the request of the people in Cheung Prey district, he led the district governor and relevant departments to inspect and put in place urgent measures to solve the water problem for the people. Dry rice harvest on time.
The provincial governor confirmed that the solution to this problem, he decided to lower the water level 1 meter in the lake, starting from Boeung Chroy as the base in Sotip commune, Cheung Prey district, and excavated two more drains at the dam. Anlong Chrey and Kay Dey open 2 more sewers in front of Stung Chhveng Dam, Chbar Ampov Commune, Batheay District.
With this emergency measure, the team of experts and machinery immediately acted as of this afternoon, the work is about 90% completed and completed by tomorrow morning.
