The district governor said that after receiving a complaint from the landowner, Hang Reang, about the case of a group of people who came to build a strong structure on his land, the district authorities have summoned both parties to resolve the procedure three times, but the party Citizens have never come to solve this problem and continue to build strong structures and build fences on their land, which is why the authorities take legal action to clear.
He said that after the clashes on February 16, 11 people were brought in for questioning and explained in detail the law so that they would not be fooled and misunderstood that the land It still belongs to them because they have been selling the land for many years.
Around this case, two people representing 10 families, one named Grud Sok Chan and one named Pha Sokleap claimed that this land is a common solidarity land that the state has distributed to 10 families since 1983 on a land width of 70 meters 700 meters long. In 1987-1988, all 10 families agreed to sell a piece of land in the middle of this land, almost one hectare, to the former Prek Takov commune chief Hang Reang without a contract, at that time they only said word of mouth.
Both of them said that when they got the land, Mr. Hang Reang started clearing and encroaching on the land of the villagers, intending to take it as their own land, but the people complained to the commune, but there is no solution until today.
He added that immediately after the incident, he filed a complaint to the commune authorities to seek justice, and the authorities summoned him to resolve the dispute, he was summoned, but the other party never came to resolve. Three times.
Mr. Hang Reang asked the authorities to help stop a group of people who wanted to take his land by inciting the people to create problems and create problems with the evil intention of angrily encroaching on his land, so he asked to be removed. From his land, because he bought a valid title deed and the authorities also recognized and issued a valid title deed.
