This morning, the Minister of Health held a press conference on the Royal Government's sub-decree to increase the level of fines for those who evade indulgence.
(Phnom Penh): At 8:30 am on February 19, 2021, Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, held a press conference on the revision of the Sub-Decree on Health Measures to Prevent and Respond to the International Outbreak of Diseases at the Port. In and out.
The Royal Government of Cambodia on February 18, 2021 has just released the revision of this sub-decree to increase the efficiency for the census. In particular, take action against those who do not cooperate in the practice of seduction.
The sub-decree decided to increase the level of fines for evaders and conspirators to evade arbitrariness.
Article 9 states that the transitional fine shall be from 1 million Riel to 5 million Riel for the person who escapes from the place of work during the process of doing the work.
Article 11 states that the transitional fine shall be from 10 million Riels to 50 million Riels for the instigator, leader, guide, instigate, persuade or intentionally facilitate the person who has to perform the ritual to escape the supervision of the officer or avoid doing so. Chattalysak or escape from Chattalisak.
It should be noted that the adjustment to increase the level of severe fines for those who do not participate in the censorship came after the Royal Government found that some workers who returned from Thailand evaded the censorship at the border. Such cases have led to the removal of the Kamrieng district inspector in Battambang province.
