Of the 190 countries, only the Cambodian Red Cross has parks and more than 2,460 trees.
(Siem Reap): Mr. Kuch Lina, Vice Chairman of Siem Reap Red Cross Branch Committee, said that in the world, there are more than 190 national Red Cross Red Crescent Societies, only the Cambodian Red Cross has parks and trees. More than 2,460 trees.
This statement by Mr. Kuch Lina took the opportunity to lead the environmental clean-up activities in the Cambodian Red Cross Millennium Park on February 18, 2021 to celebrate the 66th anniversary of the Cambodian Red Cross (February 18, 1955 to February 18). 2021) and to celebrate the 22nd anniversary of the Cambodian Red Cross Millennium Park.
Mr. Kuch Lina said that the Cambodian Red Cross Millennium Park, located in Siem Reap-Angkor province, is a precious heritage of the Cambodian Red Cross, almost 22 years old, spread over an area of nearly 5 hectares and planted trees. Since 1999, under the presidency of Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Honorary President of the Cambodian Red Cross.
Mr. Kuch Lina continued, "Currently, the park has more than 2,460 trees, which is part of the natural cover to protect the environment in Angkor, while in the world, only the Cambodian Red Cross has a park and has Many such trees among the National Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies in more than 190 countries.
