Senior Minister Sun Chanthol inspects the construction quality of National Road No. 2 and 22, more than 27% completed
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, inspected the quality of construction of National Road No. 2 and National Road No. 22 on February 19, 2021. As of February 18, more than 27 percent of the two national roads have been completed.
The inspection of the construction of the two roads was attended by senior officials of the Ministry, the technical working group of the Ministry, representatives of construction companies and technical consulting companies and stakeholders.
The purpose of this inspection is to check the quality and progress of the construction, whether the construction company and the technical consulting company comply with the specified technical standards and load books, and in addition to find solutions and make additional recommendations. To the construction side, which can ensure the construction of roads that are strong and durable.
Please be informed that according to the report of the General Department of Public Works of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, the progress of the construction project of National Road No. 2 and 22 as of February 18, 2021 has reached 27.10%.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kim Santepheap, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Justice, called on social media players to be very careful and cautious before distributing any information so as not to face liability for punishment for distributing false information. Incite social chaos.
Kim Santepheap's warning came after a number of people shared false information about the news that "a teacher died because of the Sinofam vaccine" manipulated by "Son Hai" and " Asangha ”on February 17.
At a press conference on the revision of the sub-decree on health measures to prevent and respond to the international outbreak of diseases at the gates on the morning of February 19, 2021, Mr. Kim Santepheap called this posting as an intention in Incitement leads to social unrest.
The spokesman for the Ministry of Justice also raised legal issues related to the creation of the incitement. Mr. Kim Santepheap pointed out that the legal aspect is incitement defined in Article 494 of the Penal Code. He added that incitement is a performance expressed through words, writing or drawing and disseminated by all means.
He added that Article 495, which is the next article in the Penal Code, stipulates that if the incitement causes serious social unrest, there will be a sentence of six months to two years in prison and a fine of 1 million. To 4 million riels.
Misinformation related to the cause of death of teachers in Kratie province, manipulated by "Son Hai" and "Asangha" individuals, has been widely shared on social media.
Mr. Kim Santepheap also emphasized that for those who create provocative information will definitely be punished according to the law. But those who spread all this false information will also face punishment and will also be the subject of the authorities' investigation.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Justice called on the people to check carefully before distributing any information. In particular, look at the source clearly, because the source of information is a dead point that determines whether the information is true or false?
Mr. Kim Santepheap appealed, "Our people all over the country, please reconsider to avoid any criminal liability caused by our negligence."
The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications responds to some reactions from the media and NGOs regarding the sub-decree establishing the National Internet Gateway
In response to this reaction, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications on February 19, 2021 issued a press release in response to those reactions:
1. Allegations of the establishment of this national Internet gateway are baseless, politically motivated, contrary to the facts and contrary to the purpose stated in this sub-decree.
2: National Internet gateway is established in almost all countries, not just planned to be established in Cambodia.
3. The preparation of the sub-decree on the national Internet gateway was carried out openly and in consultation with experts in the field of telecommunications, private operators and relevant institutions on several occasions.
4: The establishment of this national Internet gateway aims to increase the efficiency of national revenue collection based on the principles of fair and honest competition and transparency between the state and operators, as well as help prevent illegal cross-border network gambling online gambling. Illegal cyberbullying, pornography, and online fraud.
