British trade envoy urges British investors to seek investment opportunities in Cambodia
Her remarks were made during a working meeting with Cambodian Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak via video on February 18, 2021.
During the meeting, she acknowledged Cambodia's growth, annual economic growth and export potential. She also praised the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to facilitate the business operations of British businessmen and investors in Cambodia in the past.
She claimed that she would work to encourage and persuade British investors to learn more about investment potential in Cambodia.
Through this meeting, Minister Pan Sosak expressed high hopes that Ms. Prasit will be able to promote good dialogue, cooperation and fruitful diplomatic ties between Cambodia and the United Kingdom.
The Minister also thanked the Royal Government of the United Kingdom for its significant contribution to the development of human resources and the promotion of the Cambodian economy through financing for the development of a number of priority sectors. In particular, education, economy and trade, as well as through the provision of trade preferences that will take effect in January 2021 after Britain leaves the European Union.
The Minister also highlighted the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to reform institutions and regulations for economic integration and expressed strong will to expand trade partnerships through the establishment of a free trade agreement with Major trading partners in the region.
Mr. Pan Sosak also expressed his support for the progress of the UK-ASEAN Dialogue Partnership, which has great potential. The Minister also informed the British side that Cambodia will host the 13th Asia-Europe Summit in 2021 and chair the 40th ASEAN Summit in 2022.
During the meeting, Mr. Pan Sosak and Ms. British Business Envoy vowed to continue their close cooperation in promoting trade relations between the two countries and reviving the economy after being affected by the Kovid-19 outbreak. To promote economic development, raise living standards and provide well-being to the people of the two countries.
