(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Chhem Savuth, Director General of the General Department of Prisons, explained the procedure for evaluating prisoners who can be pardoned and commuted.
This explanation was made at the conference on the outcome of the meeting on "Dissemination of the Royal Decree on Mitigation and Amnesty" and strengthening the work of the amnesty, which was held on February 17, 2021 at the Ministry of Justice.
According to Lt. Gen. Chhem Savuth, only exemplary prisoners who have transformed into good people can apply for pardon. He added that in order to become a model prisoner, all prisons and correctional centers have to pass a competitive examination committee.
Please be reminded that on January 12, 2021, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, issued a new Royal Decree on Mitigation and Pardon. Chapter 2, Article 3 of this Royal Decree states that the ceremonies that can request the commutation of pardons and pardons are five times a year, including:
The same article further stipulates that commutation of sentences and pardons can also be done at major national festivals or events. In addition, mitigation and pardon can also be made for each of the above ceremonies, either separately or together.
