(Kandal): Mr. Bun Pheng, Governor of Khsach Kandal District, Kandal Province, asked the people to stop encroaching on the private land of others after some people protested for the right to own the land on the land of others with the correct documents without being deceived. The instigator behind.
The district governor said that after receiving a complaint from the landowner, Hang Reang, about the case of a group of people who came to build a strong structure on his land, the district authorities have summoned both parties to resolve the procedure three times, but the party Citizens have never been able to settle down and continue to build strong structures and build fences on their land, which is why the authorities have taken legal action to clear it.
He said that after the minor clashes on February 16, 11 people were taken in for questioning and explained in detail the law so that they would not be deceived and misunderstood that the land was still It belongs to them because they have been selling this land for many years.
Around this case, two people representing 10 families, one named Grud Sok Chan and one named Pha Sokleap claimed that this land is a common solidarity land that the state has distributed to 10 families since 1983 on a land width of 70 meters And 700 meters long. In 1987-1988, all 10 families agreed to sell a piece of land in the middle of this land, almost one hectare, to the former Prek Takov commune chief Hang Reang without a contract, only word of mouth.
Both of them said that when they got the land, Mr. Hang Reang started clearing and encroaching on the villagers' land, intending to completely occupy their land, but the people complained to the commune, but there is no solution until today.
He added that immediately after the incident, he filed a complaint to the commune authorities to seek justice, and the authorities summoned him to resolve the dispute, he was summoned, but the party never came to resolve the three. That time.
