Philippine Ambassador Introduces Some Companies to Do Business in Angkor Rice in Cambodia
The Ambassador emphasized this during a courtesy call and discussion with Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce on February 17, 2021.
During the meeting, the ambassador mentioned that the trade volume of the two countries has grown steadily but decreased slightly in 2020 due to the Kovid-19 crisis.
The Minister of Commerce requested the Philippine side to look into the possibility of importing rice from Cambodia and mobilizing Filipino businessmen to invest in Cambodia, such as setting up agro-industrial processing plants for export to the Philippine and global markets.
In response, the ambassador stated that the new Philippine policy would allow its private sector to purchase rice directly in accordance with Philippine sanitary-phytosanitary measures without having to go through government mechanisms. .
She said the Philippine government has given recognition to a number of companies for the rice trade, and the embassy will send the list to the Ministry of Commerce for coordination with Green Trade and the Cambodian Rice Federation.
Minister Pan Sosak also asked Filipino businessmen to examine the possibility of exporting other agricultural products from Cambodia, including cassava, corn and other key potential products to the Philippine market.
The Minister of Commerce also urged the Cambodian and Philippine Chambers of Commerce to sign a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) to promote trade and investment and invited the Philippine side to participate in the Cambodia International Trade Fair. Every year after the Kovid-19 crisis ended.
(Phnom Penh): Siem Reap Angkor Thmey International Airport is facing a shortage of electricity and clean water during construction. This is what the company that invested in construction told the Minister in charge of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation.
Mr. Sin Chanserivutha, Undersecretary of State and Spokesperson for Civil Aviation, stated that on February 17, 2021, Dr. Mao Havanal, Minister in Charge of Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, met with Mr. Lou Veng, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Siem Reap International Airport Construction Company. Angkor to ask for intervention.
He said that the construction of the new Siem Reap Angkor Airport is scheduled to be completed by the end of 2023, but the airport construction company has been facing obstacles such as lack of water for use, no clean water connection for use on construction and not. There is a network for connecting electricity and building an airport.
He added that there are two sources of water and electricity supply at the airport, the first: from Siem Reap and the second from Banteay Meanchey, which is 180 km away, so the company built the Siem Reap International Airport. The new Angkor seeks the intervention of Dr. Mao Havannal to urge the relevant ministries to help resolve the construction process of the new Siem Reap Angkor Thmey International Airport, which was successfully planned in 2023.
To this challenge, Dr. Mao Havanal also accepted the proposal and promised to help solve these problems so as not to miss the construction process of the new Siem Reap Angkor International Airport, and he also submitted a proposal to the relevant ministries to solve the electricity. Help speed up the construction of the new Siem Reap Angkor International Airport in a timely manner.
