Tomorrow, Tbong Khmum Provincial Police Commissioner, Brigadier General Mont Monrear, will be transferred to replace the retired Major General Ben Roth.
(Phnom Penh): The handover ceremony and appointment of the new commissioner of Tbong Khmum Provincial Police will be officially held tomorrow morning, February 19, 2021, presided over by General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner.
Brigadier General Mon Meakrea, Deputy Commissioner for Human Resource Planning, has been appointed Tbong Khmum Provincial Police Commissioner, replacing retired Major General Ben Roth. Major General Ben Rath has been appointed by the King by Royal Decree as an Advisor to the Ministry of Interior with the rank of Undersecretary of State.
The provincial police station was built on an area of 65,004 square meters in Nikom Leu village, Sralop commune, Tbong Khmum district, Tbong Khmum province, about 1 km from Tbong Khmum provincial hall, a former teak plantation with no infrastructure and the foundation stone was laid. On November 17, 2018, the construction took a total of 20 months to complete both the building and the infrastructure.
Kratie Provincial Administration Holds Consultation Forum to Strengthen Cooperation and Partnership with Civil Society Organizations
(Kratie): The Kratie Provincial Administration on February 18, 2021 organized a consultation forum to strengthen cooperation and partnership with civil society organizations operating in Kratie province.
