General Knowledge: Brahma Banan is the largest temple in Indonesia and the second largest in ASEAN after Angkor
(Indonesia): When it comes to the largest temple in the world, everyone is familiar with the Angkor area of Cambodia, and another famous Hindu temple is the Brahma Banan or Harajungrang temple on the island of Java. Central Indonesia, the region is named the second largest temple in ASEAN after the Angkor resort.
The village of Prasat Brahma Banan has a three-story square wall surrounding the innermost courtyard with three temples, while the central temple was built for Shiva, the southern temple for Brahma and the north temple for Vishnu.
These magnificent temples were left in ruins from the fall of the Mataram Empire until 1918, when they were rebuilt. The shrine was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List in 1991.
