According to the general, "Everything must start from peace first, where we have to spend physical, mental, intellectual and spiritual strength to overcome all obstacles and dare to sacrifice our lives for the cause of peace." In this sense, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, the backbone of the nation, at all costs, must firmly defend peace and resolutely oppose the color revolution.
It should be noted that the training program for the ninth generation of Army officers has a total of 236 people, including 40 female students, with practical training for 4 years.
