Senior official of the Ministry of Interior: The government is committed to implementing the social accountability framework to strengthen the rights of local people
Mr. Ngy Chanphal's statement was made when he presided over the inauguration ceremony of the second phase of the Social Accountability Action Plan Support Project in collaboration with World Vision Cambodia (WVIC) on This February 18, 2021, with the participation of representatives of ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations, as well as development partners and civil society organizations, a total of about 150 people at the Raffles Royal Hotel.
The Citizens' Engagement project to improve public services through social accountability will focus on ensuring that the participation of people in all villages in the target areas has a dialogue with local authorities to strengthen the quality of public services. The project will be implemented with a network of 1,900 community accountability facilitators.
Mr. Ngy Chanphal stated: "The Royal Government has a strong political commitment to implement the Social Accountability Framework (ISAF) to strengthen the rights of the people, strengthen the partnership between the sub-national administration and the people. "Citizens will strengthen the accountability of those lower-level administrations to improve the provision of more efficient public services."
Mr. Ngy Chanphal added: "The expansion of ISAF coverage will increase the capacity of sub-national administrations to provide more efficient and accountable public services, as well as respond to evolving needs. "People and the private sector in the future."
We believe that this project will bring better public services in the areas of education, health and public administration, and benefit millions of people, especially vulnerable people, who will benefit from these improved services. ” .
