Ms. Uon Kim Yon, 38 years old, resident of Chroy Ampil 1 Village, Chambok Commune, Prek Prosop District, Kratie Province, confirmed on February 18, 2021 that Ms. Chhorn Nary, 21 years old, a teacher at Snuol Secondary School, had a fever. Body and headache on January 29, 2021.
After the symptoms, the family was taken to the home of the director of Chambok Health Center, Prek Prosop district. He was not cured and still had a fever, so he was sent to Kampong Cham Hospital and then transferred to Calmette Hospital.
Chhorn Nary, the mother of the teacher, confirmed that after being sent to Calmette Hospital, doctors diagnosed her with severe meningitis and continued treatment at Calmette Hospital for 17 days.
Despite the best efforts of the doctors, they were able to save Chhorn Nary from this disease and died in the hospital on the night of February 16, 2021.
Ms. Uon Kimyon confirmed that Ms. Chhorn Nary had not been vaccinated against Kovid 19. The loss of her beloved daughter is a tragedy and sad for Uon Kim Yon and her family. But it is even more sad and painful when the death of a daughter is misrepresented by some unconscious group, causing confusion in society.
Ms. Uon Kim Yon condemned the group of people who distorted the truth about the death of her daughter and called on the authorities to follow the rule of law to those who take the body of their daughter to inspire unrealistic, causing chaos in society .
Please note that Ms. Uon Kim Yoon's statement came after a person named Son Hai, a Khmer Kampuchea Krom living in France, and a person named "Asangha", an illegal Khmer worker in South Korea, took your death. Teacher Chhon Nary went on to announce that she had died from the Chinese Kovid 19 syphilis vaccine.
In connection with the distortion, Ms. O Vandin, Secretary of State and spokesperson for the Ministry of Health, also denied the allegations. Of those who vaccinated nearly 3,000 Chinese-vaccinated Kovid 19, no teachers were yet available, she said.
The distortion of information by Son Hai and "Asangha" also led to a backlash from the masses. They also expressed criticism and insults for the misrepresentation of the two individuals.
