(Battambang): On the night of February 17, 2021, on Street 57 Krawat, O'Dambang Village, O'Dam Commune, Sangke District, Battambang Province, under the leadership of Mr. Nop Dara, Deputy Governor of Battambang Province, and under the coordination of the Prosecutor's Office, organized a joint force and Officials from the Ministry of Health inspect urine for drugs and alcohol for people who drive all kinds of vehicles.
After a urine test, police found 16 drug addicts, including a bus driver, a 10-wheeler driver and a minivan driver.
On that occasion, Mr. Nop Dara said that the campaign does not only focus on drivers in cars or trucks, even motorcyclists must check for drugs and alcohol to prevent any accidents that occur. Every day in our country.
