The handover of this rice will be held on the morning of February 17, 2021 in the presence of Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap Province.
The 2,668 families are from 6 communes, including: The first location is Preah Dak commune, Run Ta Ek commune and Romchek commune, equal to 1,083 families, including people who have volunteered to live in Tani village, Run Ta Ek commune. 259 families and the second location is Khnar Sanday commune, Khun Ream commune and Tbeng commune, equal to 1,585 families.
The rice distributed to the villagers came from the cultivation of 40 hectares of farmland, which the Siem Reap provincial administration leased from 88 families in Preah Dak commune called Sre Sangkom. Leasing the farmland from the villagers, the Banteay Srei district administration pays the rice owners per family 3-4 bags of rice depending on the size of the land available to the villagers.
It should be reminded that these social rice farming projects are the result of a joint effort to survey 40 hectares of farmland with 88 families in Preah Dak commune, as well as to receive seed support, expenses and volunteer labor. From the Siem Reap Provincial Department of Agriculture, philanthropists and youth volunteers.
The project also received an output of 84 tons and was gradually distributed to farmers, poor people and victims of floods in the past, and was completed today. BREAKING: As of the evening of February 17, the Ministry of National Defense vaccinated more than 10,000 Kovid 19 armed forces
According to the report, on February 17, 2021, the Kovid 19 vaccination team of the Ministry of National Defense vaccinated 1,152 officers, deputies and soldiers for the Ministry of National Defense, including 200 women.
Upon arrival in Cambodia, Kovid 19 Sino-Farm vaccine was administered on a voluntary basis to government leaders, journalists and the military at several locations, including: Calmette Hospital, Ang Duong Hospital, Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital, National Pediatric Hospital and Ketomealea Hospital (for the Army).
Ministry of Health rejects polls: "Teacher dies of Kovid 19 vaccine"
(Phnom Penh): Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State and spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, came out to deny the false broadcast that a teacher died due to the Kovid 19 vaccine.
The dismissal comes after Son Hai, a Khmer Krom who fled Cambodia a few years ago, posted on his Facebook page that a teacher had died after being vaccinated with Kovid 19.
Ms. O Vandin emphasized that as of February 17, 2021, Kovid 19 vaccine has not been vaccinated by any teachers.
Ms. O Vandin also called on the authorities to take legal action against the dissidents.
Please note that Ms. Chhorn Nary, 21 years old, is a teacher in Kratie province. The teacher died of meningitis. Indonesia launches second phase of large-scale vaccination campaign that will cover more than 38 million people
The second priority group of the vaccination program will cover 38.5 million people, including market vendors, the elderly, teachers, religious figures, lawmakers, government officials, police, journalists and staff. Being in a hospital or transport and tourism office.
On Wednesday, Indonesian President Joko Widodo visited a textile market in central Jakarta to observe the implementation of the second phase of vaccination for traders.
The president said the event was the start of the second phase of the COVID-19 vaccination, adding that the first phase, which focuses on health workers, began in mid-January and will end soon. ⁇.
A large-scale vaccination campaign in Indonesia began on January 14, a day after President Joko Widodo and several other government officials received a vaccine produced by Sinovac's company. The Chinese vaccine Sinovac will arrive in Thailand in the first phase next week.
Dr. Mao Phirun promotes and promotes good marketing for farmers in Saang district at an affordable price
(Kandal): Dr. Mao Phirun, Chairman of the Provincial Council, promotes and promotes good marketing for farmers in Saang district to help them have a good market with good prices and the Saang district authorities have an important duty to This is due to the training of other techniques in growing vegetables, killing insects and raising animals.
The Chairman of the Provincial Council said so on the occasion that he led a delegation to study and grow vegetables in Svay Proteal commune, Saang district, Kandal province on February 17, 2021.
Dr. said that farmers have already produced their crops, but what is remarkable is that their crops seem to have a low market, which makes them less motivated to continue to produce crops. Therefore, the district authorities and relevant authorities need to find markets for farmers in the community by mobilizing companies to buy agricultural products produced by farmers in the community.
Meanwhile, Mr. Bun Toun Simona, Director of Kandal Provincial Department of Agriculture, said that he has taken steps to promote marketing, namely the establishment of a weekend farm in Takhmao City and is eager to help find markets for farmers and still Keep up the good work.
It should be informed that throughout Saang district, there are 8,169 hectares of vegetable growing area, with 12 communities per day, Saang district can produce an average of 115 tons of vegetables. Attorney General of Battambang Court of Appeal Encourages Journalists to Report More to the Public
(Battambang): Mr. Nuon San, Attorney General of the Battambang Court of Appeal, said that the press is very important for the society, he encouraged the journalists to follow the news to present to the public.
